WEBVTT

1
00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:51.870
Theatre – it can show us who we are,
who we were and who we could be.

2
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.080
It means imagining bigger,

3
00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.950
understanding better,

4
00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.290
feeling together –

5
00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:03.080
on our stages and on tour,

6
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.910
in schools

7
00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.620
and with communities,

8
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.160
on cinema screens worldwide

9
00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.330
and now at home.

10
00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:13.370
We are the National Theatre.

11
00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:16.370
We make theatre for everyone.

12
00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:29.660
Art helps us to see the world in new ways.

13
00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:32.830
The stories behind great works
help to bring them to life,

14
00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.870
and hearing them shouldn't be a privilege.

15
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.540
That's why we built Bloomberg Connects.

16
00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:42.250
An app that lets you discover a growing
number of museums, gardens and parks,

17
00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:45.580
behind-the-scenes interviews
and public art from around the world,

18
00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:49.160
all in a single download
right in the palm of your hand.

19
00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:52.580
Bloomberg Connects offers
a world of inspiration.

20
00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:57.250
Join the National Theatre community
and hundreds of cultural institutions

21
00:01:57.330 --> 00:02:00.540
to get a deeper look into the world of art
through Bloomberg Connects.

22
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.080
(Audience chatting indistinctly)

23
00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.120
(Sinister music starts playing)

24
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.620
(Audience quiets down)

25
00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.120
(Barnardo) Who's there?

26
00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.620
(Clock ticking)

27
00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:01.750
(Ticking stops)

28
00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.450
- Long live the King!
- (Barnardo gasps)

29
00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:44.620
(Francisco chuckles)

30
00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:47.250
- Francisco.
- What ho, Barnardo.

31
00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:50.000
You come most carefully
upon your hour.

32
00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.580
'Tis now struck twelve.
Get thee to bed, Francisco.

33
00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.700
For this relief much thanks.

34
00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.870
'Tis bitter cold.

35
00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:01.370
And I am sick at heart.

36
00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:05.250
- Have you had quiet guard?
- Not a mouse stirring.

37
00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:10.370
(Barnardo) Well, good night.
If you do meet Horatio and Marcellus,

38
00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:12.330
Bid them make haste.

39
00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:15.120
I think I hear them!
Stand, ho! Who is there?

40
00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.620
(Horatio) Friends to this ground.
(Marcellus) And liegemen to the Dane.

41
00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.370
(Francisco) Give you good night.
(Marcellus) O, farewell, honest soldier.

42
00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.330
- Who hath relieved you?
- (Francisco) Barnardo hath my place.

43
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.080
Give you good night.

44
00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.200
(Marcellus) Holla, Barnardo.

45
00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:34.000
(Barnardo) Say, what,
is Horatio there?

46
00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.620
(Horatio) A piece of her.

47
00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:39.200
(Barnardo) Welcome, Horatio.
Welcome, good Marcellus.

48
00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:41.370
What?

49
00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:44.120
(Scary voice) Has this thing
appeared again tonight?

50
00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.500
(Laughs)

51
00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:46.870
I have seen nothing.

52
00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.830
Horatio says 'tis but our fantasy,

53
00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:51.830
And will not let belief
take hold of her,

54
00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:55.500
Touching this dreaded sight
twice seen of us.

55
00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.370
Therefore I have entreated her along

56
00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.750
With us to watch the minutes
of this night.

57
00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:03.080
That if again this...apparition come,

58
00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.500
She may prove our eyes
and speak to it.

59
00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:08.080
(Horatio) Tush, tush,
'twill not appear.

60
00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.870
(Barnardo) Sit down awhile,

61
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.120
And let us once again
assail your ears

62
00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:14.250
That are so fortified
against our story,

63
00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:16.500
What we have two nights seen.

64
00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:20.500
(Horatio) Well, sit we down,
And let us hear Barnardo speak of this.

65
00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:26.950
(Barnardo) Last night of all,

66
00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:30.120
Marcellus and myself,
The bell then beating one...

67
00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:33.250
(Marcellus) Peace, break thee off.

68
00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:53.750
(Gasp and scream)

69
00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.120
(Marcellus)
Look where it comes again!

70
00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.330
(Barnardo) In the same figure
like the King that's dead!

71
00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:59.700
(Marcellus) Thou art a scholar,
speak to it, Horatio!

72
00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:02.450
(Barnardo) Looks it not like the King?
Mark it, Horatio!

73
00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:06.120
(Horatio) Most like!
It harrows me with fear and wonder!

74
00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.370
(Barnardo) It would be spoke to!
(Marcellus) Question it, Horatio!

75
00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:12.000
(Horatio) What art thou
that usurp'st this time of night,

76
00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:14.450
Together with that fair
and warlike form

77
00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:17.620
In which the majesty of buried Denmark
Did sometimes march?

78
00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:21.120
By heaven, I charge thee speak!

79
00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:22.870
- (Dramatic music)
- (Echoing yell)

80
00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:31.450
(Marcellus) 'Tis gone.

81
00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:36.500
(Barnardo) How now, Horatio?
You tremble and look pale.

82
00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.870
Is not this
something more than fantasy?

83
00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.950
Before my God,
I might not this believe

84
00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:44.200
Without the sensible and true avouch
Of mine own eyes!

85
00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:48.200
(Marcellus) Is it not like the King?
(Horatio) As thou art to thyself.

86
00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:50.200
Such was the very armour he had on

87
00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:52.450
When he th’ambitious Norway
combated.

88
00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:53.580
‘Tis strange.

89
00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.330
Thus twice before,
and jump at this dead hour,

90
00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:59.330
With martial stalk
hath he gone by our watch.

91
00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:02.250
This bodes some strange eruption
to our state.

92
00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:03.700
- (Eerie music)
- But soft!

93
00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:06.620
Lo, behold where it comes again!

94
00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:10.250
I'll cross it though it blast me!

95
00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:12.080
Stay, illusion,

96
00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:15.700
If thou hast any sound or use of voice,
Speak to me!

97
00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:17.870
If thou art privy
to thy country's fate,

98
00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:21.000
Which, happily, foreknowing may avoid,
O speak!

99
00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.620
- (Clock chimes)
- Stop it, Marcellus!

100
00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.450
(Marcellus) Shall I strike at it?
(Horatio) Do!

101
00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.120
- (Gunshot)
- (They scream)

102
00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:34.370
(Marcellus) 'Tis gone.

103
00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:39.120
We do it wrong, being so majestical,

104
00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:41.500
To offer it the show of violence,

105
00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:44.080
For it is as the air, invulnerable.

106
00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:46.200
It was about to speak
when the clock struck.

107
00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:47.370
Come, good sirs,

108
00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:51.620
Let us impart what we have seen tonight
Unto young Hamlet; for, upon my life,

109
00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:54.000
This spirit,
dumb to us, will speak to him.

110
00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.700
Let’s do’t, I pray,

111
00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:58.750
and I this morning know
Where we shall find him most convenient.

112
00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:00.080
(Quiet orchestral music)

113
00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:15.500
(People chatting)

114
00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.120
(Music intensifies)

115
00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:31.870
(Music stops)

116
00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:36.370
Though yet of Hamlet
our dear brother's death

117
00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:37.620
The memory be green,

118
00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:40.830
and that it us befitted
To bear our hearts in grief,

119
00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:44.250
and our whole kingdom
To be contracted in one brow of woe,

120
00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:48.080
Yet so far hath discretion
fought with nature

121
00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:51.330
That we, with wisest sorrow,
think on him

122
00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:54.580
Together with remembrance
of ourselves.

123
00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:59.580
Therefore our sometime sister,
now our queen,

124
00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:03.250
Th'imperial jointress
to this warlike state,

125
00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:06.080
Have we,
as 'twere with a defeated joy,

126
00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:09.750
With mirth in funeral
and with dirge in marriage,

127
00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:11.000
Taken to wife.

128
00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:14.500
Nor have we herein barred
Your better wisdoms,

129
00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.950
which have freely gone
With this affair along.

130
00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:20.370
For all, our thanks.

131
00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:23.750
♪ Tomorrow is Saint Valentine’s day

132
00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.080
♪ All in the morning betime

133
00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:28.450
♪ And I a maid at your window

134
00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.700
♪ To be your Valentine

135
00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:34.370
♪ Then up he rose
and up he rose and up he rose

136
00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:38.500
♪ And donned his clo’es
and dupped the chamber door

137
00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:41.120
♪ Let in the maid
and out that a maid

138
00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:45.500
♪ Never departed more, more
more, more, more, more, more ♪

139
00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:47.120
(Claudius) And now!

140
00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:49.200
(Laughter)

141
00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:51.120
Laertes, what's the news with you?

142
00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:54.620
You told us of some suit.
What is’t, Laertes?

143
00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:57.870
You cannot speak of reason to the Dane
And lose your voice.

144
00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.500
What wouldst thou have, Laertes?

145
00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:00.620
My dread lord,

146
00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:03.370
Your leave and favour
to return to France,

147
00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:06.000
From whence though willingly
I came to Denmark

148
00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:08.750
To show my duty
in your coronation,

149
00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:10.870
Yet now I must confess,
that duty done,

150
00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:13.370
My thoughts and wishes
bend again toward France

151
00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:17.250
And bow them
to your gracious leave and pardon.

152
00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:19.620
Have you your father's leave?
What says Polonius?

153
00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:22.750
He hath, my lord,
wrung from me my slow leave

154
00:10:22.870 --> 00:10:24.450
By laboursome petition.

155
00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:28.000
Take thy fair hour, Laertes,
time be thine,

156
00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:32.120
And thy best graces
spend it at thy...will.

157
00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:36.700
But now, my cousin Hamlet!

158
00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:38.580
And my son.

159
00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:41.500
A little more than kin,
and less than kind.

160
00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:43.950
How is it that the clouds
still hang on you?

161
00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.080
Oh.

162
00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:48.330
Not so, my lord,
I am too much in the sun.

163
00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:51.620
Good Hamlet,
cast thy nighted colour off,

164
00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:54.450
And let thine eye
look like a friend on Denmark.

165
00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:56.500
Do not for ever with thy vailed lids

166
00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:59.000
Seek for thy noble father
in the dust.

167
00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:01.000
Thou know'st 'tis common:

168
00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:04.830
all that lives must die,
Passing through nature to eternity.

169
00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:07.620
Ay, madam, it is common.

170
00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:10.870
(Gertrude) If it be,
Why seems it so particular with thee?

171
00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:13.620
Seems, madam?

172
00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:16.120
Nay, it is.

173
00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:17.870
I know not "seems".

174
00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:21.000
'Tis not alone my inky cloak,
good mother,

175
00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:23.370
Nor customary suits of solemn black,

176
00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:26.080
Nor windy suspiration
of forced breath,

177
00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.500
No, nor the fruitful river
in the eye,

178
00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:30.830
Nor the dejected haviour
of the visage,

179
00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:33.120
Together with all forms,
moods, shapes of grief,

180
00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:35.000
That can denote me truly.

181
00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:37.950
These indeed seem,

182
00:11:38.450 --> 00:11:40.950
For they are actions
that a man might play;

183
00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:45.120
But I have that within
which passes show,

184
00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:48.620
These but the trappings
and the suits of woe.

185
00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:51.830
'Tis sweet and commendable
in your nature, Hamlet,

186
00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:54.250
To give these mourning duties
to your father,

187
00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.200
But you must know
your father lost a father,

188
00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:59.000
That father lost, lost his.

189
00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.250
But to persever
In obstinate condolement

190
00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:04.500
is a course
Of impious stubbornness,

191
00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:06.120
'tis unmanly grief,

192
00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:08.620
It shows a will
most incorrect to heaven,

193
00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:11.000
A heart unfortified,
a mind impatient,

194
00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:13.120
An understanding
simple and unschooled.

195
00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:16.000
Fie, 'tis a fault to heaven,

196
00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:18.330
A fault against the dead,
a fault to nature,

197
00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:21.250
To reason most absurd,
whose common theme

198
00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:23.200
Is death of fathers.

199
00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:25.330
We pray you

200
00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:28.000
throw to earth
This unprevailing woe,

201
00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:30.080
and think of us
As of a father;

202
00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:33.370
for let the world take note
You are the most immediate to our throne,

203
00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:35.120
And with no less nobility of love

204
00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:37.700
Than that which dearest father
bears his son

205
00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:39.500
Do I impart toward you.

206
00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:44.500
For your intent
In going back to school in Wittenberg,

207
00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:47.330
It is most retrograde to our desire,

208
00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:49.830
And we beseech you
bend you to remain

209
00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:53.200
Here in the cheer
and comfort of our eye,

210
00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:55.700
Our chiefest courtier, cousin,

211
00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:57.950
and our son.

212
00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:00.500
Let not thy mother
lose her prayers, Hamlet.

213
00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:02.870
I pray thee stay with us,

214
00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:04.120
go not to Wittenberg.

215
00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:10.000
I shall in all my best obey you,
madam.

216
00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:13.500
(String music)

217
00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:18.870
(Exhales)

218
00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:25.000
That this too too sullied flesh
would melt,

219
00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:26.370
Thaw

220
00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:29.370
and resolve itself into a dew!

221
00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.950
Or that the Everlasting had not fixed

222
00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:34.200
His canon 'gainst self-slaughter.

223
00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:36.830
O God!

224
00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:41.750
God! How weary, stale, flat,
and unprofitable

225
00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:44.000
Seem to me
all the uses of this world.

226
00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:47.250
Fie on't... Hm.

227
00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:49.700
Fie.

228
00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:53.870
'Tis an unweeded garden
That grows to seed.

229
00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:55.870
Things rank and gross in nature

230
00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:58.450
Possess it...merely.

231
00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:02.830
That it should come to this.

232
00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:04.580
But two months dead.

233
00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:07.450
Nay, not so much, not two.

234
00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:09.700
So excellent a king,
that was to this

235
00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:13.250
Hyperion to a satyr,
so loving to my mother

236
00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:14.750
That he might not beteem
the winds of heaven

237
00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.120
Visit her face too roughly.

238
00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:18.830
Heaven and earth,
Must I remember?

239
00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:21.080
Why, she would hang on him

240
00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:25.000
As if increase of appetite had grown
By what it fed on; and yet within a month...

241
00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:26.750
Let me not think on't.

242
00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:29.700
Frailty, thy name is woman.

243
00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:37.000
A little month,
or ere those shoes were old

244
00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:39.750
With which she followed
my poor father's body,

245
00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:43.120
Like Niobe, all tears; why she,
O God,

246
00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:47.700
a beast that wants discourse of reason
Would have mourned longer;

247
00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:49.870
married

248
00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.500
with my uncle.

249
00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:55.080
(Audience laughs)

250
00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:58.500
My father's brother,

251
00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:02.000
but no more like my father
Than I to Hercules.

252
00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:03.830
Within a month!

253
00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:07.620
Ere yet the salt
of most unrighteous tears

254
00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:11.500
Had left the flushing
in her galled eyes,

255
00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.120
She married.

256
00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:16.700
O most wicked speed!

257
00:15:16.830 --> 00:15:19.200
To post
With such dexterity

258
00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:21.080
to incestuous sheets!

259
00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:23.330
It is not,

260
00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:25.750
nor it cannot come to good.

261
00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:28.830
But break, my heart,

262
00:15:28.950 --> 00:15:31.620
for I must hold my tongue.

263
00:15:31.750 --> 00:15:34.200
Why, 'tis a loving and a fair reply.

264
00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:36.120
Be as ourself in Denmark.

265
00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:37.250
Gertrude, come.

266
00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:40.080
This gentle
and unforced accord of Hamlet

267
00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:42.200
Sits smiling to my heart.

268
00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:45.330
♪ How should I your true love know

269
00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:48.120
♪ From another one?

270
00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:49.750
♪ One

271
00:15:49.870 --> 00:15:52.120
♪ One

272
00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:56.580
♪ By his cockle hat and staff

273
00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:59.700
♪ And his sandal shoon

274
00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:03.250
♪ And his sandal shoon ♪

275
00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:08.330
(Laertes) Ophelia, my dear sister,
do not sleep,

276
00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:09.950
But let me hear from you.

277
00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:11.450
Do you doubt that?

278
00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:14.580
(Laertes clears his throat)

279
00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:16.330
For Hamlet,

280
00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:19.870
and the trifling of his favour,

281
00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:24.120
Hold it a fashion
and a toy in blood,

282
00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:27.200
Forward, not permanent,

283
00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:29.870
sweet, not lasting,

284
00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:33.330
The perfume and suppliance of a minute,
No more.

285
00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:36.000
- No more but so?
- Think it no more.

286
00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:41.330
Perhaps he loves you now,
but you must fear,

287
00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:44.370
His greatness weighed,
his will is not his own.

288
00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:47.000
For he himself
is subject to his birth.

289
00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:51.620
He may not,
as...unvalued persons do,

290
00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:52.870
Carve for himself,

291
00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:56.500
for on his choice depends
The sanity and health

292
00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:58.120
of this whole state.

293
00:16:58.250 --> 00:16:59.330
(Ophelia) Hm.

294
00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.620
- He says he loves you?
- Mm-hm.

295
00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:06.500
Mm-hm. Then weigh what loss
your honour may sustain

296
00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:10.700
If with too credent ear
you list his songs,

297
00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:13.830
Or lose your heart,

298
00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:17.370
or... (Clears his throat)

299
00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:21.120
...your chaste treasure open

300
00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:23.620
To his unmastered importunity.

301
00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:25.250
Ew! (Retching)

302
00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:28.120
Fear it, Ophelia, fear it,

303
00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:30.000
my dear sister,

304
00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:33.250
And keep you
in the rear of your affection

305
00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:36.580
Out of the shot and danger
of desire.

306
00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:39.370
I shall th'effect
of this good lesson keep

307
00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:42.200
As watchman to my heart.

308
00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:44.000
- But, good my brother...
- Mm-hm.

309
00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:46.830
...Do not,
as some ungracious pastors do,

310
00:17:46.950 --> 00:17:49.000
Show me the steep
and thorny way to heaven,

311
00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:50.750
Whiles, like a puffed
and reckless libertine,

312
00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:53.250
Himself the primrose path
of dalliance treads.

313
00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:56.080
- O fear me not!
- (Chuckles)

314
00:17:56.870 --> 00:17:59.120
- (Ophelia squeals)
- But here my father comes.

315
00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:02.750
Yet here, Laertes?
Aboard, aboard for shame.

316
00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:06.580
The wind sits in the shoulder of your sail,
And you are stayed for.

317
00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:09.120
Mwah!

318
00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:12.450
There, my blessing with thee.

319
00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:15.370
And these few precepts in thy memory
Look thou character.

320
00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:16.620
(Ophelia) Mm-hm.

321
00:18:18.620 --> 00:18:22.000
Give thy thoughts no tongue,

322
00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.370
Nor any unproportioned thought
his act.

323
00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:27.950
Be thou familiar,
but by no means vulgar.

324
00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:30.330
Those friends thou hast,

325
00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:32.750
and their adoption tried,

326
00:18:32.870 --> 00:18:36.120
Grapple them unto thy soul
with hoops of steel,

327
00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:37.750
But do not dull thy palm
with entertainment

328
00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:40.250
Of each new-hatched,
unfledged comrade.

329
00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:45.000
Beware
Of entrance to a quarrel,

330
00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:47.370
but being in,

331
00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:50.830
Bear't that th'opposed
may beware of thee.

332
00:18:50.950 --> 00:18:53.750
Give every man thy ear,
but few thy voice.

333
00:18:53.870 --> 00:18:55.750
Take each man’s censure,

334
00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:58.830
but reserve thy judgment.

335
00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.120
Costly thy habit
as thy purse can buy,

336
00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:04.330
- But not expressed in fancy.
- (Laughs)

337
00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:07.700
Rich, not gaudy. For the apparel...

338
00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:10.830
(Both) ...oft proclaims the man.

339
00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.000
Neither a...

340
00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:15.870
(Ophelia joins in)
...borrower nor a lender be,

341
00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:18.370
For loan oft loses
both itself and friend,

342
00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:21.750
- And borrowing...?
- Dulls...? Dulls the edge of husbandry!

343
00:19:25.950 --> 00:19:28.250
This above all:

344
00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:33.830
to thine own self be true,

345
00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:37.330
And it must follow
as the night the day,

346
00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:40.500
Thou canst not then be false
to any man.

347
00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:42.700
(Chuckling) Oh!

348
00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:46.750
Farewell,
my blessing season this in thee.

349
00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:48.000
- Oh.
- Oh.

350
00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:50.750
- Fromage.
- Fromage!

351
00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:54.120
The time invites you; go,
your servants tend.

352
00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:56.580
- Ophelia. Ophelia.
- (Polonius) Oh.

353
00:19:56.700 --> 00:19:58.870
Remember well
What I have said to you.

354
00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:00.620
Mm-hm. 'Tis in my memory locked,

355
00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:03.080
And you yourself
shall keep the key of it.

356
00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:06.000
Mwah, mwah, mwah,
mwah, mwah, mwah, mwah!

357
00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:08.080
(Laertes) Farewell.

358
00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:11.700
(Both, sadly) Aw.

359
00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:13.120
(Both chuckle)

360
00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:14.450
Ooh! (Chuckles)

361
00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:15.700
Oh! Hut!

362
00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:17.870
- (Grunting)
- (Audience laughs)

363
00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:21.500
- (Ophelia laughs)
- What is't, Ophelia,

364
00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:24.000
he hath said to you?

365
00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:27.870
So please you,
something touching the Lord Hamlet.

366
00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:31.080
Marry, well bethought.
'Tis told me he hath very oft of late

367
00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:34.250
Given...private time to you,

368
00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:37.200
and you yourself
Have of your audience

369
00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:39.500
been most free and bounteous.

370
00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:42.370
What is between you?

371
00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:45.250
Give me up...

372
00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:47.370
...the truth.

373
00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:51.000
He hath, my lord, of late made

374
00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:55.620
many tenders
Of his affection to me.

375
00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:56.750
- Affection?
- Mm-hm.

376
00:20:56.870 --> 00:20:59.200
- Whoa.
- Ooh!

377
00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:01.830
You speak like a green girl,

378
00:21:01.950 --> 00:21:04.870
Unsifted in such perilous circumstance.

379
00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:08.250
Do you believe his tenders,
as you call them?

380
00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:10.870
I do not know, my lord,
what I should think.

381
00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.870
Marry, I will teach you.
Think yourself a baby

382
00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:14.950
That you have ta'en these tenders
for true pay

383
00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:16.750
which are not sterling.

384
00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.250
Or, not to crack the wind
of the poor phrase,

385
00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:22.000
Running it thus,
tender yourself more dearly.

386
00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:25.120
My lord,
he hath importuned me with love

387
00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:27.080
In honourable fashion.

388
00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:29.750
Ay, fashion you may call it.
Go to, go to.

389
00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:32.120
And hath given countenance
to his speech, my lord,

390
00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:35.200
With almost
all the holy vows of heaven!

391
00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:37.500
Ay, springes to catch woodcocks!

392
00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:39.700
I do know,
When the blood burns,

393
00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:42.700
how prodigal the soul
Lends the tongue vows!

394
00:21:48.330 --> 00:21:49.450
What was I about to say?

395
00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:51.450
- (Audience laughs)
- (Ophelia) Um...

396
00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:53.500
I was about to say something.
Where did I leave?

397
00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:55.200
At "when the blood burns".

398
00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:56.870
Ay, marry, the blood.

399
00:21:58.870 --> 00:22:01.000
These blazes, daughter,
Giving more light than heat,

400
00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:03.120
extinct in both,
Even in their promise as it is a-making,

401
00:22:03.250 --> 00:22:04.870
You must not take for fire!

402
00:22:05.450 --> 00:22:07.750
For Lord Hamlet,
Believe so much in him that he is young,

403
00:22:07.870 --> 00:22:11.250
And with a larger tether may he walk
Than may be given you.

404
00:22:13.450 --> 00:22:17.080
In few, Ophelia,
Do not believe his vows.

405
00:22:18.330 --> 00:22:19.950
This is for all.

406
00:22:25.330 --> 00:22:27.500
I would not, in plain terms,
from this time forth

407
00:22:27.620 --> 00:22:30.200
Have you so slander any moment leisure
As to give words

408
00:22:30.330 --> 00:22:32.000
or talk with the Lord Hamlet.

409
00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:35.580
- Look to't, I charge you.
- I shall obey, my lord.

410
00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:37.370
- Good Polonius!
- My lord.

411
00:22:37.870 --> 00:22:40.450
Now follows
that you know young Fortinbras,

412
00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:42.370
Holding a weak supposal
of our worth,

413
00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:45.080
Or thinking
by our late dear brother’s death

414
00:22:45.200 --> 00:22:47.370
Our state to be disjoint
and out of frame,

415
00:22:47.500 --> 00:22:50.330
He hath not failed to pester us
with message

416
00:22:50.450 --> 00:22:52.250
Importing the surrender
of those lands,

417
00:22:52.370 --> 00:22:54.750
Lost by his father,
with all bonds of law,

418
00:22:54.870 --> 00:22:56.830
To our most valiant brother.

419
00:22:57.450 --> 00:22:59.080
So much for him.

420
00:22:59.200 --> 00:23:01.620
Thus much the business is:

421
00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.200
we have here writ
To Norway,

422
00:23:04.330 --> 00:23:07.500
uncle of young Fortinbras,
Who, impotent and bedrid,

423
00:23:07.620 --> 00:23:09.620
scarcely hears
Of this his nephew’s purpose,

424
00:23:09.750 --> 00:23:12.870
to suppress
His further gait herein,

425
00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:15.250
and we here dispatch
You, good Cornelius,

426
00:23:15.370 --> 00:23:18.870
and you, Voltemand,
For bearers of this greeting to old Norway.

427
00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:20.870
Farewell,
let your haste commend your duty.

428
00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:23.580
In that, and all things,
will we show our duty.

429
00:23:23.700 --> 00:23:25.370
- Ay, my lord.
- We doubt it nothing.

430
00:23:25.500 --> 00:23:27.000
Heartily farewell.

431
00:23:28.370 --> 00:23:31.500
My honoured lord,
you do not give the cheer.

432
00:23:32.750 --> 00:23:34.120
(Claudius chuckles)

433
00:23:34.250 --> 00:23:35.370
(People cheering)

434
00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:36.580
(Gertrude) What's this?

435
00:23:43.500 --> 00:23:45.500
(Cheering and whistling)

436
00:23:45.620 --> 00:23:47.450
(Upbeat electronic music)

437
00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:55.870
O that the universal globe of heaven

438
00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:58.620
Would turn all to a chaos.

439
00:24:00.250 --> 00:24:03.870
- Hail to your lordship.
- I am glad to see you well.

440
00:24:05.750 --> 00:24:06.830
Horatio!

441
00:24:06.950 --> 00:24:08.870
Or I do forget myself.

442
00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:11.200
The same, my lord,

443
00:24:11.330 --> 00:24:13.120
and your poor servant ever.

444
00:24:13.250 --> 00:24:15.250
Sir, my good friend,

445
00:24:15.370 --> 00:24:17.370
I'll change that name with you.

446
00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:19.750
And what make you
from Wittenberg, Horatio?

447
00:24:20.750 --> 00:24:22.000
- Marcellus.
- My good lord.

448
00:24:22.120 --> 00:24:24.120
I am very glad to see you.

449
00:24:25.750 --> 00:24:26.870
Good even, sir.

450
00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:29.250
But what in faith make you
from Wittenberg?

451
00:24:29.370 --> 00:24:31.750
A truant disposition, good my lord.

452
00:24:31.870 --> 00:24:35.000
I would not hear your enemy say so.
I know you are no truant, Horatio.

453
00:24:35.120 --> 00:24:37.620
But what is your affair in Elsinore?

454
00:24:38.120 --> 00:24:40.330
We'll teach you to drink deep
ere you depart.

455
00:24:40.450 --> 00:24:43.620
My lord, I came to see
your father's funeral.

456
00:24:43.750 --> 00:24:45.830
I prithee do not mock me,
fellow-student.

457
00:24:46.450 --> 00:24:48.750
I think it was to see
my mother's wedding.

458
00:24:48.870 --> 00:24:51.200
(Clears throat) Indeed, my lord,
it followed hard upon.

459
00:24:52.120 --> 00:24:53.450
Thrift, thrift, Horatio.

460
00:24:54.200 --> 00:24:56.620
The funeral baked meats
Did coldly furnish forth

461
00:24:56.750 --> 00:24:58.700
the marriage tables.

462
00:24:58.830 --> 00:25:00.830
Would I had met my dearest foe
in heaven

463
00:25:00.950 --> 00:25:03.000
Or ever I had seen that day,
Horatio.

464
00:25:05.080 --> 00:25:06.080
My father...

465
00:25:07.250 --> 00:25:11.120
- Methinks I see my father.
- Where, my lord?

466
00:25:12.080 --> 00:25:13.620
In my mind's eye, Horatio.

467
00:25:13.750 --> 00:25:15.450
(Audience laughs)

468
00:25:15.580 --> 00:25:17.330
I saw him once;
he was a goodly king.

469
00:25:17.450 --> 00:25:20.000
He was a man,
take him for all in all.

470
00:25:20.120 --> 00:25:21.870
I shall not look upon his like
again.

471
00:25:22.000 --> 00:25:23.750
My lord,
I think I saw him yesternight.

472
00:25:23.870 --> 00:25:26.000
- Saw? Who?
- My lord, the king your father.

473
00:25:28.120 --> 00:25:30.120
(Audience laughs)

474
00:25:30.250 --> 00:25:31.830
The king my father?

475
00:25:31.950 --> 00:25:35.870
Season your admiration for a while
With an attent ear till I may deliver

476
00:25:36.000 --> 00:25:39.330
Upon the witness of these gentlemen
This marvel to you.

477
00:25:39.450 --> 00:25:41.080
For God's love, let me hear.

478
00:25:41.200 --> 00:25:44.830
Two nights together had these gentlemen,
Marcellus and Barnardo, on their watch

479
00:25:44.950 --> 00:25:46.750
In the dead waste
and middle of the night

480
00:25:46.870 --> 00:25:49.080
Been thus encountered:

481
00:25:49.200 --> 00:25:51.750
a figure like your father

482
00:25:51.870 --> 00:25:55.200
Armed at point exact
appears before them,

483
00:25:55.330 --> 00:25:57.000
Goes slow and stately by,

484
00:25:57.120 --> 00:26:00.370
whilst they, distilled
Almost to jelly with the act of fear,

485
00:26:00.500 --> 00:26:02.370
Stand dumb and speak not to him.

486
00:26:02.500 --> 00:26:05.080
This to me
In dreadful secrecy impart they did,

487
00:26:05.200 --> 00:26:07.200
And I with them
the third night kept the watch,

488
00:26:07.330 --> 00:26:10.080
Where, as they had delivered,
both in time,

489
00:26:10.200 --> 00:26:11.330
Form of the thing,

490
00:26:11.450 --> 00:26:14.750
each word made true and good,
The apparition comes.

491
00:26:14.870 --> 00:26:18.750
I knew your father;
These hands are not more like.

492
00:26:18.870 --> 00:26:20.870
- Did you not speak to it?
- My lord, I did.

493
00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:22.200
But answer made it none.

494
00:26:22.330 --> 00:26:25.120
Yet once methought
It lifted up its head as it would speak,

495
00:26:25.250 --> 00:26:27.950
But...vanished from our sight.

496
00:26:28.830 --> 00:26:30.250
'Tis very strange.

497
00:26:30.370 --> 00:26:32.830
As I do live, my honoured lord,
'tis true;

498
00:26:32.950 --> 00:26:35.370
And we did think it writ down in our duty
To let you know of it.

499
00:26:35.500 --> 00:26:38.700
- O! Armed, say you?
- (Barnardo) Armed, my lord.

500
00:26:38.830 --> 00:26:40.830
- You say you saw his face?
- (Horatio) O yes, my lord.

501
00:26:40.950 --> 00:26:42.580
What looked he, frowningly?

502
00:26:42.700 --> 00:26:44.750
A countenance more in sorrow
than in anger.

503
00:26:44.870 --> 00:26:47.000
- And fixed his eyes upon you?
- Most constantly.

504
00:26:47.120 --> 00:26:49.370
- I would I had been there.
- It would have much amazed you.

505
00:26:49.500 --> 00:26:50.620
Very like.

506
00:26:51.370 --> 00:26:53.500
I will watch tonight.
Perchance 'twill walk again.

507
00:26:53.620 --> 00:26:55.120
I war'nt it will.

508
00:26:55.250 --> 00:26:58.200
I pray you all,
If you have hitherto concealed this sight,

509
00:26:58.330 --> 00:27:00.580
Let it be tenable
in your silence still.

510
00:27:00.700 --> 00:27:03.450
I will requite your loves.
So fare you well.

511
00:27:03.580 --> 00:27:05.830
(Marcellus and Barnardo)
Our duty to your honour.

512
00:27:08.370 --> 00:27:10.000
My father's spirit.

513
00:27:10.580 --> 00:27:11.580
In arms.

514
00:27:12.250 --> 00:27:13.500
All is not well.

515
00:27:14.120 --> 00:27:16.120
I doubt some foul play.

516
00:27:16.750 --> 00:27:18.250
Would the night were come.

517
00:27:19.200 --> 00:27:21.250
Till then sit still, my soul.

518
00:27:21.830 --> 00:27:23.750
Foul deeds will rise,

519
00:27:24.250 --> 00:27:27.330
Though all the earth o'erwhelm them,
to men's eyes.

520
00:27:28.000 --> 00:27:29.700
(Eerie orchestral music)

521
00:27:33.250 --> 00:27:34.700
(Fireworks exploding)

522
00:27:34.830 --> 00:27:36.120
(Marcellus) My lords.

523
00:27:36.250 --> 00:27:38.830
(Hamlet) What hour now?
(Horatio) I think it lacks of twelve.

524
00:27:38.950 --> 00:27:41.750
(Marcellus) No, it is struck.
(Horatio) Indeed? I heard it not.

525
00:27:42.750 --> 00:27:46.700
The air bites shrewdly,
it is very cold.

526
00:27:46.830 --> 00:27:48.750
It then draws near
the season

527
00:27:48.870 --> 00:27:51.000
Wherein the spirit
held his wont to walk.

528
00:27:53.000 --> 00:27:55.620
The King doth wake tonight
and takes his rouse.

529
00:27:55.750 --> 00:27:56.750
(Fireworks whistling)

530
00:27:56.870 --> 00:27:58.120
(Clock strikes)

531
00:27:58.250 --> 00:28:00.120
Look, my lord, it comes!

532
00:28:03.330 --> 00:28:06.500
Angels and ministers of grace
defend us!

533
00:28:06.620 --> 00:28:09.250
Be thou a spirit of health
or goblin damned,

534
00:28:09.370 --> 00:28:11.750
Bring with thee airs from heaven
or blasts from hell,

535
00:28:11.870 --> 00:28:15.000
Thou com'st in such a questionable shape
That I will speak to thee.

536
00:28:15.120 --> 00:28:17.330
I'll call thee Hamlet,

537
00:28:18.000 --> 00:28:19.000
King,

538
00:28:19.580 --> 00:28:20.580
father...

539
00:28:21.080 --> 00:28:22.080
(Mumbling)

540
00:28:22.200 --> 00:28:23.450
Royal Dane?

541
00:28:23.950 --> 00:28:26.830
- O answer me. What should we do?
- It beckons you, my lord,

542
00:28:27.000 --> 00:28:28.830
as if it some
Impartment did desire to you alone!

543
00:28:28.950 --> 00:28:30.830
- Leave me!
- Do not go to it, sir!

544
00:28:30.950 --> 00:28:32.700
- By no means!
- What should be the fear?

545
00:28:32.830 --> 00:28:34.830
What if it do assume
some horrible form

546
00:28:34.950 --> 00:28:37.000
Which might deprive
your sovereignty of reason

547
00:28:37.120 --> 00:28:38.370
And draw you into madness?

548
00:28:38.500 --> 00:28:40.450
Still it calls!
Go on, be not afeared!

549
00:28:40.580 --> 00:28:42.620
- You must not go, my lord!
- ‘Tis my command!

550
00:28:42.750 --> 00:28:44.870
Forgive us,
'tis not fit thus to obey you!

551
00:28:45.000 --> 00:28:47.450
Unhand me, gentlemen! I say away!

552
00:28:48.750 --> 00:28:51.500
By heaven,
I'll make a ghost of him that stays!

553
00:28:51.620 --> 00:28:53.580
Well, my lord,
we’ll wait on you without!

554
00:28:53.700 --> 00:28:55.200
Go on, I'll call to thee!

555
00:28:56.580 --> 00:28:58.370
(Audience laughs)

556
00:29:02.500 --> 00:29:03.830
(Hamlet crying)

557
00:29:05.580 --> 00:29:07.450
Speak, I’ll come no closer!

558
00:29:08.370 --> 00:29:09.750
Mark me.

559
00:29:10.370 --> 00:29:11.580
I will.

560
00:29:11.700 --> 00:29:14.250
My hour is almost come

561
00:29:14.370 --> 00:29:16.830
When I to sulph’rous
and tormenting flames

562
00:29:16.950 --> 00:29:18.370
Must render up myself.

563
00:29:18.500 --> 00:29:20.830
- Alas, poor ghost.
- Pity me not.

564
00:29:21.450 --> 00:29:24.120
But lend thy serious hearing
To what I shall unfold.

565
00:29:24.250 --> 00:29:26.250
Speak, I am bound to hear.

566
00:29:26.370 --> 00:29:29.620
So art thou to revenge
when thou shalt hear.

567
00:29:29.750 --> 00:29:33.250
- What?
- I am thy father’s spirit,

568
00:29:33.370 --> 00:29:36.500
Doomed for a certain term
to walk the night,

569
00:29:36.620 --> 00:29:39.750
And for the day confined
to fast in fires,

570
00:29:39.870 --> 00:29:42.620
Till the foul crimes done
in my days of nature

571
00:29:42.750 --> 00:29:45.200
Are burnt and purged away.

572
00:29:46.120 --> 00:29:49.580
But this eternal blazon must not be
To ears of flesh and blood.

573
00:29:50.200 --> 00:29:52.080
List, list!

574
00:29:52.950 --> 00:29:54.200
O list!

575
00:29:54.700 --> 00:29:57.200
- If thou didst ever thy dear father love...
- O God!

576
00:29:57.330 --> 00:30:01.120
...Revenge his foul
and most unnatural murder.

577
00:30:01.250 --> 00:30:04.000
- Murder?
- Murder most foul, as in the best it is,

578
00:30:04.120 --> 00:30:06.870
But this most foul,
strange and unnatural.

579
00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:09.250
Haste me to know’t,
that I with wings

580
00:30:09.370 --> 00:30:10.750
As swift as meditation

581
00:30:10.870 --> 00:30:13.750
or the thoughts of love
May sweep to my revenge.

582
00:30:13.870 --> 00:30:15.080
Now Hamlet, hear.

583
00:30:15.700 --> 00:30:18.250
‘Tis given out that,
sleeping in my orchard,

584
00:30:18.370 --> 00:30:19.950
A serpent stung me.

585
00:30:20.080 --> 00:30:23.620
So the whole ear of Denmark
Is by a forged process of my death

586
00:30:23.750 --> 00:30:25.250
Rankly abused.

587
00:30:25.370 --> 00:30:26.870
But know, thou noble youth,

588
00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:30.120
The serpent that did sting thy father’s life
Now wears his crown.

589
00:30:30.250 --> 00:30:33.250
O my prophetic soul! My uncle!

590
00:30:33.370 --> 00:30:35.620
Ay. That incestuous,

591
00:30:35.750 --> 00:30:38.330
that adulterate beast,
With witchcraft of his wit,

592
00:30:38.450 --> 00:30:41.120
won to his lust
The will of my most seeming-virtuous queen.

593
00:30:42.500 --> 00:30:45.450
O Hamlet,
what a falling off was there.

594
00:30:46.580 --> 00:30:49.870
But soft,
methinks I scent the morning air.

595
00:30:50.370 --> 00:30:52.000
Brief let me be.

596
00:30:53.120 --> 00:30:55.500
Sleeping within my orchard,

597
00:30:55.620 --> 00:30:57.450
My custom always of the afternoon,

598
00:30:57.580 --> 00:31:00.120
Upon my secure hour thy uncle stole

599
00:31:00.250 --> 00:31:03.080
With juice of cursed hebenon
in a vial,

600
00:31:03.200 --> 00:31:07.200
And in the porches of my ears did pour
The leperous distilment, whose effect

601
00:31:07.330 --> 00:31:09.370
Holds such an enmity
with blood of man

602
00:31:09.500 --> 00:31:11.500
That swift as quicksilver
it courses through

603
00:31:11.620 --> 00:31:14.080
The natural gates and alleys
of the body,

604
00:31:14.200 --> 00:31:15.830
And with a sudden vigour
it doth posset

605
00:31:15.950 --> 00:31:18.580
And curd,
like eager droppings into milk,

606
00:31:18.700 --> 00:31:20.620
The thin and wholesome blood.

607
00:31:21.500 --> 00:31:23.000
So did it mine,

608
00:31:23.120 --> 00:31:26.000
And a most instant tetter
barked about,

609
00:31:26.120 --> 00:31:27.500
Most lazar-like,

610
00:31:27.620 --> 00:31:31.120
with vile and loathsome crust
All my smooth body.

611
00:31:32.000 --> 00:31:35.000
Thus was I, sleeping,
by a brother’s hand

612
00:31:35.120 --> 00:31:39.200
Of life, of crown,
of queen at once dispatched,

613
00:31:39.330 --> 00:31:41.620
Cut off
even in the blossoms of my sin,

614
00:31:41.750 --> 00:31:44.370
No reck’ning made,
but sent to my account

615
00:31:44.500 --> 00:31:47.250
With all my imperfections
on my head.

616
00:31:47.870 --> 00:31:48.870
O horrible.

617
00:31:49.620 --> 00:31:50.620
O horrible.

618
00:31:51.750 --> 00:31:52.750
Most horrible.

619
00:31:54.700 --> 00:31:56.750
If thou has nature in thee,

620
00:31:57.450 --> 00:31:58.620
bear it not.

621
00:31:59.120 --> 00:32:02.700
Let not the royal bed of Denmark be
A couch for luxury

622
00:32:02.830 --> 00:32:04.580
and damned incest.

623
00:32:05.330 --> 00:32:07.870
But howsomever
thou pursuest this act,

624
00:32:08.580 --> 00:32:10.330
Taint not thy mind

625
00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:13.870
nor let thy soul contrive
Against thy mother aught.

626
00:32:14.500 --> 00:32:16.250
Leave her to heaven,

627
00:32:16.370 --> 00:32:18.750
And to those thorns
that in her bosom lodge

628
00:32:18.870 --> 00:32:20.950
To prick and sting her.

629
00:32:22.370 --> 00:32:23.750
Fare thee well at once.

630
00:32:27.620 --> 00:32:28.620
Adieu.

631
00:32:30.200 --> 00:32:31.200
Adieu.

632
00:32:32.620 --> 00:32:33.620
Adieu.

633
00:32:35.870 --> 00:32:37.370
Remember me.

634
00:32:40.330 --> 00:32:42.120
(String music)

635
00:32:46.870 --> 00:32:48.620
(Audience laughs)

636
00:32:48.750 --> 00:32:51.000
O all you host of heaven!

637
00:32:52.120 --> 00:32:53.330
O earth!

638
00:32:54.080 --> 00:32:55.700
What else?
And shall I couple hell?

639
00:32:55.830 --> 00:32:57.620
O fie!

640
00:32:57.750 --> 00:32:59.620
Hold, hold, my heart,

641
00:32:59.750 --> 00:33:03.120
And you, my sinews,
grow not instant old,

642
00:33:03.250 --> 00:33:05.000
But bear me stiffly up.

643
00:33:05.120 --> 00:33:06.250
Remember thee?

644
00:33:06.370 --> 00:33:07.870
Ay, thou poor ghost,

645
00:33:08.000 --> 00:33:11.330
whiles memory holds a seat
In this distracted globe.

646
00:33:11.450 --> 00:33:13.250
Remember thee? Yea.

647
00:33:13.370 --> 00:33:15.330
From the table of my memory

648
00:33:15.450 --> 00:33:17.500
I’ll wipe away
all trivial fond records,

649
00:33:17.620 --> 00:33:19.620
And thy commandment all alone
shall live

650
00:33:19.750 --> 00:33:21.620
Within the book
and volume of my brain.

651
00:33:26.580 --> 00:33:29.750
O...

652
00:33:30.870 --> 00:33:31.870
...most...

653
00:33:32.870 --> 00:33:34.950
...pernicious woman.

654
00:33:35.500 --> 00:33:36.950
(Laughs)

655
00:33:37.620 --> 00:33:40.700
O villain, villain,
smiling damned villain.

656
00:33:40.830 --> 00:33:43.750
Meet it is I set it down
That one may smile,

657
00:33:43.870 --> 00:33:46.120
and smile, and be a villain.

658
00:33:46.250 --> 00:33:48.500
At least I am sure
it may be so in Denmark.

659
00:33:49.500 --> 00:33:53.330
So, uncle...there you are.

660
00:33:55.080 --> 00:33:56.250
Now to my word.

661
00:33:56.750 --> 00:33:58.870
It is "Adieu. Adieu.

662
00:33:59.870 --> 00:34:00.870
Remember me."

663
00:34:03.620 --> 00:34:05.000
I have sworn’t.

664
00:34:08.120 --> 00:34:10.450
- Horatio! Marcellus!
- How is’t, my noble lord?

665
00:34:10.580 --> 00:34:12.580
- What news, my lord?
- O, wonderful.

666
00:34:12.700 --> 00:34:15.000
- Good, my lord, tell it.
- No, you will reveal it.

667
00:34:15.120 --> 00:34:17.120
- Not I, by heaven.
- Nor I, my lord.

668
00:34:17.250 --> 00:34:19.370
There’s never a villain dwelling
in all Denmark

669
00:34:19.500 --> 00:34:20.620
But he’s an arrant knave.

670
00:34:20.750 --> 00:34:23.370
There needs no ghost come from the grave
To tell us this.

671
00:34:23.500 --> 00:34:26.250
Why, you are in the right.
Without more circumstance at all,

672
00:34:26.370 --> 00:34:28.120
I hold it fit we shake hands
and part.

673
00:34:28.250 --> 00:34:30.080
These are but wild
and whirling words.

674
00:34:30.200 --> 00:34:32.870
- I am sorry they offend you.
- There’s no offence, my lord.

675
00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:36.450
Yes, by Saint Patrick
but there is, Horatio,

676
00:34:36.580 --> 00:34:38.080
And much offence too.

677
00:34:38.700 --> 00:34:42.080
Touching this vision here,
It is an honest ghost.

678
00:34:42.200 --> 00:34:44.370
Hm. And let me tell you...

679
00:34:46.120 --> 00:34:48.620
And now, good friends,
Give me one poor request.

680
00:34:48.750 --> 00:34:50.080
What is’t, my lord? We will.

681
00:34:50.200 --> 00:34:52.370
Never make known
what you have seen tonight.

682
00:34:52.500 --> 00:34:55.080
- (All) My lord, we will not.
- Nay, but swear’t!

683
00:34:55.200 --> 00:34:57.700
- In faith, my lord, not I.
- Nor I, my lord, in faith.

684
00:34:57.830 --> 00:34:59.830
- Nor I.
- (Ghost) Swear.

685
00:34:59.950 --> 00:35:04.120
- Come on. Consent to swear.
- (Horatio) Propose the oath, my lord.

686
00:35:04.250 --> 00:35:07.120
- Never to speak of this that you have seen.
- (Ghost) Swear.

687
00:35:07.250 --> 00:35:09.450
(Horatio) O day and night,
but this is wondrous strange!

688
00:35:09.580 --> 00:35:12.700
And therefore as a stranger
give it welcome.

689
00:35:12.830 --> 00:35:15.250
There are more things
in heaven and earth, Horatio,

690
00:35:15.370 --> 00:35:17.000
Than are dreamt of
in your philosophy.

691
00:35:17.120 --> 00:35:18.750
But come
Here, as before, never,

692
00:35:18.870 --> 00:35:20.370
so help you mercy,

693
00:35:20.500 --> 00:35:23.120
How strange or odd
some’er I bear myself,

694
00:35:23.250 --> 00:35:25.080
As I perchance hereafter

695
00:35:25.200 --> 00:35:28.000
shall think meet
To put an antic disposition on,

696
00:35:28.120 --> 00:35:30.370
That you, at such time seeing me,

697
00:35:30.500 --> 00:35:33.120
never note
That you know aught of me,

698
00:35:33.750 --> 00:35:35.370
This do swear.

699
00:35:35.500 --> 00:35:37.370
- (Ghost) Swear.
- Oh, God!

700
00:35:37.500 --> 00:35:38.620
- I swear!
- I swear!

701
00:35:38.750 --> 00:35:40.000
We all swear!

702
00:35:40.750 --> 00:35:42.200
Rest.

703
00:35:42.330 --> 00:35:45.000
Rest, perturbed spirit.

704
00:35:47.620 --> 00:35:48.870
Come, gentlemen,

705
00:35:49.370 --> 00:35:52.620
And still your fingers
on your lips, I pray.

706
00:35:52.750 --> 00:35:55.830
Something is rotten
in the state of Denmark.

707
00:35:57.200 --> 00:35:58.950
The time is out of joint.

708
00:35:59.830 --> 00:36:01.870
O cursed spite,

709
00:36:02.000 --> 00:36:04.750
That ever I was born
to set it right.

710
00:36:04.870 --> 00:36:06.700
Nay, come, let’s go together.

711
00:36:07.250 --> 00:36:08.620
(Quick string music)

712
00:36:44.750 --> 00:36:47.250
Give him this money

713
00:36:47.370 --> 00:36:50.750
and these notes, Reynaldo.

714
00:36:50.870 --> 00:36:52.000
I will, my lord.

715
00:36:52.120 --> 00:36:54.370
You shall do marvellous wisely,
good Reynaldo,

716
00:36:54.500 --> 00:36:57.700
Before you visit him, to make inquire
Of his...

717
00:36:58.700 --> 00:36:59.700
...behaviour.

718
00:36:59.830 --> 00:37:01.870
My lord, I did intend it.

719
00:37:02.000 --> 00:37:04.500
Inquire me first
what Danes there are in Paris,

720
00:37:04.620 --> 00:37:06.370
And where they keep, what company.

721
00:37:06.500 --> 00:37:09.750
And finding
That they do know my son,

722
00:37:10.250 --> 00:37:14.500
there put on him
What forgeries you please.

723
00:37:15.250 --> 00:37:17.750
The usual slips
As are companions noted

724
00:37:17.870 --> 00:37:20.500
and most known
To youth and liberty.

725
00:37:20.620 --> 00:37:22.450
As gaming, my lord?

726
00:37:22.580 --> 00:37:25.250
Ay, or drinking, fencing,

727
00:37:25.370 --> 00:37:27.250
swearing,
Quarrelling, whoring...

728
00:37:27.370 --> 00:37:30.120
- You may go so far.
- But my good lord...

729
00:37:30.250 --> 00:37:33.120
- Wherefore should you do this?
- Ay, my lord, I would know that.

730
00:37:33.250 --> 00:37:37.200
Marry, sir, here's my drift.
You laying these...slight sullies

731
00:37:37.330 --> 00:37:40.000
on my son,
Your party in converse,

732
00:37:40.120 --> 00:37:42.000
him you would sound,
He closes thus:

733
00:37:42.120 --> 00:37:44.250
"I know the gentleman,
I saw him yesterday,

734
00:37:44.370 --> 00:37:47.120
and as you say,
There was he gaming,

735
00:37:47.700 --> 00:37:49.870
there o’ertook in’s rouse,

736
00:37:50.000 --> 00:37:52.370
There falling out at tennis",

737
00:37:53.500 --> 00:37:57.700
or perchance "I saw him enter
such a house of sale".

738
00:38:01.120 --> 00:38:03.080
Videlicet a brothel, or so forth.

739
00:38:03.200 --> 00:38:07.250
See you now: your bait of falsehood takes
This carp of truth,

740
00:38:07.370 --> 00:38:11.500
and thus do we
By indirections find directions out.

741
00:38:11.620 --> 00:38:14.080
- God buy ye, fare ye well.
- (Reynaldo clears throat)

742
00:38:15.120 --> 00:38:18.450
Observe his inclination in yourself.

743
00:38:18.580 --> 00:38:20.000
I shall, my lord.

744
00:38:20.500 --> 00:38:24.250
And let him...ply his music.

745
00:38:24.830 --> 00:38:26.250
Well, my lord.

746
00:38:26.370 --> 00:38:27.370
(Both chuckle)

747
00:38:27.500 --> 00:38:29.200
How now, Ophelia, what's the matter?

748
00:38:29.330 --> 00:38:32.450
O my lord, my lord,
I have been so affrighted!

749
00:38:32.580 --> 00:38:33.870
With what, i'th' name of God?

750
00:38:34.000 --> 00:38:36.750
My lord,
as I was reading in my closet,

751
00:38:36.870 --> 00:38:40.250
Lord Hamlet,
with his doublet all unbraced,

752
00:38:40.370 --> 00:38:43.450
Pale as his shirt,
his knees knocking each other,

753
00:38:43.580 --> 00:38:45.870
And with a look
so piteous in purport

754
00:38:46.000 --> 00:38:48.950
As if he had been loosed out of hell
To speak of horrors,

755
00:38:49.080 --> 00:38:51.250
- he comes before me.
- Mad for thy love?

756
00:38:51.370 --> 00:38:53.500
My lord, I do not know,
But truly I do fear it.

757
00:38:53.620 --> 00:38:55.450
- What said he?
- He took me by the wrist

758
00:38:55.580 --> 00:38:56.870
and held me hard.

759
00:38:57.000 --> 00:38:59.330
And with his other hand,
thus o'er his brow,

760
00:38:59.450 --> 00:39:03.120
He falls to such perusal of my face
As he would draw it.

761
00:39:03.250 --> 00:39:04.620
Long stayed he so.

762
00:39:04.750 --> 00:39:07.250
At last,
a little shaking of mine arm,

763
00:39:07.370 --> 00:39:10.870
He raised a sigh
so piteous and profound

764
00:39:11.000 --> 00:39:14.580
As it did seem to shatter all his bulk
And end his being.

765
00:39:15.120 --> 00:39:16.870
That done, he lets me go,

766
00:39:17.000 --> 00:39:19.580
And with his head
over his shoulder turned,

767
00:39:19.700 --> 00:39:22.080
He seemed to find his way
without his eyes,

768
00:39:22.200 --> 00:39:24.200
For out o' doors he went
without their helps,

769
00:39:24.330 --> 00:39:26.450
And to the last
bended their light on me.

770
00:39:26.580 --> 00:39:29.080
Come, go with me.
I will go seek the King.

771
00:39:29.200 --> 00:39:31.250
This is the very ecstasy of love!

772
00:39:32.700 --> 00:39:36.580
What, have you...given him
any hard words of late?

773
00:39:36.700 --> 00:39:39.370
No, my good lord,
but as you did command,

774
00:39:39.500 --> 00:39:42.870
I did repel his letters and denied
His access to me.

775
00:39:43.000 --> 00:39:45.250
That hath made him mad.
I am sorry

776
00:39:46.370 --> 00:39:49.120
that with better heed and judgment
I had not noted him.

777
00:39:49.250 --> 00:39:52.250
I feared he did but trifle
And meant to wrack thee.

778
00:39:53.250 --> 00:39:55.120
But beshrew my jealousy.

779
00:39:55.250 --> 00:39:56.870
Come, go we to the King.

780
00:39:57.000 --> 00:39:59.750
This must be known,
which, being kept close, might move

781
00:39:59.870 --> 00:40:02.500
More grief to hide
than hate to utter love. Come.

782
00:40:03.120 --> 00:40:04.830
(Suspenseful orchestral music)

783
00:40:10.120 --> 00:40:14.500
Welcome,
dear Rosencrantz and Guildenstern.

784
00:40:15.250 --> 00:40:17.580
Moreover that we much
did long to see you,

785
00:40:17.700 --> 00:40:19.870
The need we have to use you
did provoke

786
00:40:20.000 --> 00:40:20.950
Our hasty sending.

787
00:40:22.000 --> 00:40:26.250
Something have you heard
Of Hamlet's transformation, so call it,

788
00:40:26.370 --> 00:40:28.370
Sith nor th'exterior
nor the inward man

789
00:40:28.500 --> 00:40:30.370
Resembles that it was.

790
00:40:30.500 --> 00:40:32.750
What it should be,
More than his father's death,

791
00:40:32.870 --> 00:40:35.870
that thus hath put him
So much from th'understanding of himself

792
00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:37.200
I cannot dream of.

793
00:40:37.750 --> 00:40:40.250
I entreat you both
That, being of so young days

794
00:40:40.370 --> 00:40:41.370
brought up with him,

795
00:40:41.500 --> 00:40:44.120
You draw him on to pleasures
and do gather,

796
00:40:44.250 --> 00:40:46.830
Whether aught to us unknown
afflicts him thus

797
00:40:46.950 --> 00:40:49.080
That, opened,
lies within our remedy.

798
00:40:49.200 --> 00:40:51.620
Good gentlemen,
he hath much talked of you,

799
00:40:51.750 --> 00:40:54.750
And two men there is not living
To whom he more adheres.

800
00:40:54.870 --> 00:40:57.620
If it will please you
As to expend your time with us awhile,

801
00:40:57.750 --> 00:40:59.700
Your visitation
shall receive such thanks

802
00:40:59.830 --> 00:41:01.500
As fits a king's remembrance.

803
00:41:01.620 --> 00:41:04.580
Both your Majesties might,
by the sovereign power you have of us,

804
00:41:04.700 --> 00:41:07.700
Put your dread pleasures more into command
Than to entreaty.

805
00:41:07.830 --> 00:41:08.750
But we both obey,

806
00:41:08.870 --> 00:41:12.120
And here give up ourselves
in the full bent

807
00:41:12.250 --> 00:41:15.250
To lay our service freely
at your feet

808
00:41:15.370 --> 00:41:16.580
To be commanded.

809
00:41:16.700 --> 00:41:19.250
Thanks, Rosencrantz
and gentle Guildenstern.

810
00:41:19.370 --> 00:41:22.250
Thanks, Guildenstern
and gentle Rosencrantz.

811
00:41:22.370 --> 00:41:25.700
And I beseech you instantly to visit
My too much changed son.

812
00:41:25.830 --> 00:41:28.620
Heavens make our presence
and our practices

813
00:41:28.750 --> 00:41:31.370
Pleasant and helpful to him.

814
00:41:31.500 --> 00:41:32.870
Ay, amen.

815
00:41:33.000 --> 00:41:34.500
Th’ambassadors from Norway,

816
00:41:34.620 --> 00:41:36.450
my good lord,
Are joyfully returned.

817
00:41:36.580 --> 00:41:38.830
Thou still hast been
the father of good news.

818
00:41:39.620 --> 00:41:40.870
Have I, my lord?

819
00:41:41.620 --> 00:41:44.500
I assure my good liege,
I hold my duty as I hold my soul,

820
00:41:44.620 --> 00:41:46.870
Both to my God
and to my gracious King;

821
00:41:47.000 --> 00:41:49.000
And I do think,
or else this brain of mine

822
00:41:49.120 --> 00:41:51.330
Hunts not the trail of policy so sure
As it hath used to do,

823
00:41:51.450 --> 00:41:53.620
that I have found
The very cause of Hamlet's lunacy.

824
00:41:54.200 --> 00:41:57.500
O speak of that.
That do I long to hear.

825
00:41:57.620 --> 00:42:00.870
I doubt it is no other but the main,
His father's death

826
00:42:01.000 --> 00:42:02.620
and our o'er-hasty marriage.

827
00:42:05.000 --> 00:42:06.830
Give first admittance
to th’ambassadors.

828
00:42:06.950 --> 00:42:09.580
My news shall be the fruit
to that great feast.

829
00:42:09.700 --> 00:42:11.370
Welcome, my good friends.

830
00:42:11.500 --> 00:42:14.620
Say, Voltemand,
what from our cousin Norway?

831
00:42:14.750 --> 00:42:17.870
Most fair return of greetings
and desires.

832
00:42:18.000 --> 00:42:21.120
Upon our first, he sent out to suppress
His nephew’s levies,

833
00:42:21.250 --> 00:42:24.080
which to him appeared
To be preparation ‘gainst the Polack;

834
00:42:24.200 --> 00:42:27.620
But better looked into, he truly found
It was against your Highness.

835
00:42:27.750 --> 00:42:31.870
Whereat grieved that so his sickness
Was falsely borne in hand,

836
00:42:32.000 --> 00:42:34.450
sends out arrests
On Fortinbras;

837
00:42:34.580 --> 00:42:36.750
which he, in brief, obeys,

838
00:42:36.870 --> 00:42:39.830
Makes vow before his uncle
never more

839
00:42:39.950 --> 00:42:42.500
To give th’assay of arms
against your Majesty.

840
00:42:42.620 --> 00:42:45.830
Whereon old Norway,
overcome with joy,

841
00:42:45.950 --> 00:42:48.120
Gives him commission
to employ those soldiers

842
00:42:48.250 --> 00:42:50.500
So levied, as before,
against the Polack,

843
00:42:50.620 --> 00:42:51.870
With an entreaty

844
00:42:52.450 --> 00:42:55.500
That it might please you
to give quiet pass

845
00:42:55.620 --> 00:42:57.830
Through your dominions
for this enterprise.

846
00:42:57.950 --> 00:42:59.370
It likes us well.

847
00:42:59.500 --> 00:43:01.120
We thank you for your labour.

848
00:43:01.250 --> 00:43:04.500
Go to your rest,
at night we’ll feast together.

849
00:43:05.500 --> 00:43:07.620
Most welcome home.

850
00:43:09.120 --> 00:43:10.750
This business is well ended.

851
00:43:12.200 --> 00:43:15.700
My liege and madam, to expostulate
What majesty should be,

852
00:43:15.830 --> 00:43:17.330
what duty is,

853
00:43:17.450 --> 00:43:20.500
Why...day is day,
night night, and time is time.

854
00:43:20.620 --> 00:43:22.750
Were nothing but to waste
night, day, and time.

855
00:43:22.870 --> 00:43:24.000
(Chuckles)

856
00:43:24.120 --> 00:43:25.750
Therefore,
since brevity is the soul of wit,

857
00:43:25.870 --> 00:43:27.370
And tediousness the limbs
and outward flourishes,

858
00:43:27.500 --> 00:43:29.330
I will be brief.
Your noble son is mad.

859
00:43:29.870 --> 00:43:31.250
(Audience laughs)

860
00:43:31.370 --> 00:43:35.500
Mad call I it,
for to define true madness,

861
00:43:35.620 --> 00:43:38.830
What is't but to be nothing else
but mad? But let that go.

862
00:43:38.950 --> 00:43:40.700
More matter with less art.

863
00:43:40.830 --> 00:43:43.000
Madam, I swear I use no art at all.

864
00:43:43.120 --> 00:43:46.330
That he is mad ‘tis true;
'tis true 'tis pity; and pity 'tis 'tis true.

865
00:43:46.450 --> 00:43:47.870
(Audience laughs)

866
00:43:48.620 --> 00:43:52.080
A foolish figure,
But farewell it, for I will use no art.

867
00:43:52.200 --> 00:43:54.450
Mad let us grant him then.

868
00:43:54.580 --> 00:43:57.250
And now remains
That we find out the cause of this effect.

869
00:43:57.370 --> 00:44:01.950
Perpend: I have a daughter,

870
00:44:03.450 --> 00:44:05.000
Have while she is mine,

871
00:44:06.000 --> 00:44:08.370
Who in her duty and obedience, mark,

872
00:44:08.500 --> 00:44:10.580
Hath given me this.

873
00:44:13.000 --> 00:44:14.370
Now... (Chuckles)

874
00:44:14.500 --> 00:44:17.080
...gather and...

875
00:44:18.250 --> 00:44:19.500
...surmise.

876
00:44:23.500 --> 00:44:26.580
"To the celestial
and my soul's idol,

877
00:44:26.700 --> 00:44:28.700
the most beautified Ophelia."

878
00:44:28.830 --> 00:44:30.250
That's an ill phrase.

879
00:44:30.370 --> 00:44:31.750
(Audience laughs)

880
00:44:31.870 --> 00:44:33.620
A vile phrase.

881
00:44:33.750 --> 00:44:36.870
"Beautified" is a vile phrase.
But you shall hear.

882
00:44:37.000 --> 00:44:38.750
Came this from Hamlet to her?

883
00:44:38.870 --> 00:44:41.370
Good madam, stay awhile,
I will be faithful.

884
00:44:45.370 --> 00:44:46.870
"Doubt thou the stars are fire,

885
00:44:47.000 --> 00:44:50.000
Doubt that the sun doth move,
Doubt truth to be a liar,

886
00:44:50.120 --> 00:44:52.500
But never doubt I love.

887
00:44:56.620 --> 00:44:59.500
O dear Ophelia,
I am ill at these numbers.

888
00:44:59.620 --> 00:45:02.120
But that I love thee best,
O most best, believe it.

889
00:45:02.250 --> 00:45:06.080
Thine evermore,
whilst this machine is to him, Hamlet."

890
00:45:09.370 --> 00:45:11.500
This in obedience
hath my daughter shown me,

891
00:45:12.200 --> 00:45:16.200
And, more above, hath his solicitings,
All given to mine ear.

892
00:45:17.330 --> 00:45:19.750
But how hath she received his love?

893
00:45:20.750 --> 00:45:22.370
- (Mumbles)
- What do you think of me?

894
00:45:23.250 --> 00:45:27.080
- As of a man faithful and honourable.
- I would fain prove so.

895
00:45:27.200 --> 00:45:30.250
But what might you think,
Or my dear Majesty your queen here think,

896
00:45:30.370 --> 00:45:32.080
When I had seen this...

897
00:45:33.200 --> 00:45:34.870
...hot love on the wing

898
00:45:35.000 --> 00:45:38.700
If I had played the desk or table-book,
Or looked upon this love with idle sight?

899
00:45:38.830 --> 00:45:41.330
No, I went round to work,
And my young mistress

900
00:45:41.450 --> 00:45:42.870
thus I did bespeak:

901
00:45:43.000 --> 00:45:46.000
"Lord Hamlet
is a prince out of thy star.

902
00:45:46.120 --> 00:45:47.120
This must not be."

903
00:45:47.250 --> 00:45:48.870
And then I prescripts gave her,

904
00:45:49.000 --> 00:45:51.450
That she should lock herself
from his resort,

905
00:45:51.580 --> 00:45:53.330
Admit no messengers,
receive no tokens;

906
00:45:53.450 --> 00:45:56.450
Which done,
she took the fruits of my advice,

907
00:45:56.580 --> 00:45:58.370
And he, repelled
- a short tale to make -

908
00:45:58.500 --> 00:46:03.620
Fell into a sadness, then into a fast,
Thence to a watch, thence into a weakness,

909
00:46:03.750 --> 00:46:05.870
Thence to a lightness,
and, by this declension,

910
00:46:06.000 --> 00:46:08.750
Into the madness wherein now he raves
And all we mourn for.

911
00:46:09.620 --> 00:46:11.200
(Audience laughs quietly)

912
00:46:11.330 --> 00:46:13.000
Do you think 'tis this?

913
00:46:13.120 --> 00:46:15.120
It may be; very like.

914
00:46:16.370 --> 00:46:18.370
Hath there been such a time
- I would fain know that -

915
00:46:18.500 --> 00:46:21.000
That I have positively said "Tis so",
When it proved otherwise?

916
00:46:21.580 --> 00:46:22.620
Not that I know.

917
00:46:22.750 --> 00:46:26.000
Take this from this
if this be otherwise.

918
00:46:26.120 --> 00:46:27.950
How may we try it further?

919
00:46:28.700 --> 00:46:31.580
- I'll loose my daughter to him.
- Oh.

920
00:46:31.700 --> 00:46:34.370
Be you and I
Behind an arras. If he love her not,

921
00:46:34.500 --> 00:46:36.330
And be not
from his reason fall'n thereon,

922
00:46:36.450 --> 00:46:39.750
Let me be no assistant for a state,
But keep a farm and carters.

923
00:46:40.370 --> 00:46:41.370
We will try it.

924
00:46:41.500 --> 00:46:44.080
But look where sadly the poor wretch
comes reading.

925
00:46:44.200 --> 00:46:46.000
Away, I do beseech you both, away.

926
00:46:46.120 --> 00:46:48.120
I'll board him presently.

927
00:46:49.250 --> 00:46:50.500
O give me leave.

928
00:46:51.750 --> 00:46:53.330
(Audience laughs quietly)

929
00:47:03.750 --> 00:47:05.250
(Audience laughs quietly)

930
00:47:23.370 --> 00:47:26.370
To be, or not to be,
that is the question.

931
00:47:27.500 --> 00:47:30.330
Whether 'tis nobler in the mind
to suffer

932
00:47:30.450 --> 00:47:33.200
The slings and arrows
of outrageous fortune,

933
00:47:33.330 --> 00:47:37.750
Or to take arms
against a sea of troubles.

934
00:47:38.620 --> 00:47:41.620
And by opposing end them.
To die, to sleep, no more.

935
00:47:41.750 --> 00:47:45.870
And by a sleep to say we end
The heart-ache

936
00:47:46.000 --> 00:47:49.870
and the thousand natural shocks
That flesh is heir to:

937
00:47:50.000 --> 00:47:52.950
'tis a consummation
Devoutly to be wished.

938
00:47:53.080 --> 00:47:55.870
To die, to sleep;

939
00:47:56.000 --> 00:47:59.250
To sleep, perchance to dream.

940
00:47:59.370 --> 00:48:02.000
Ay, there's the rub: For in that sleep
of death what dreams may come,

941
00:48:02.120 --> 00:48:04.580
When we have shuffled off this mortal coil,
Must give us pause.

942
00:48:04.700 --> 00:48:07.580
There's the respect
that makes calamity of so long life.

943
00:48:07.700 --> 00:48:11.000
For who would bear
the whips and scorns of time,

944
00:48:11.120 --> 00:48:12.120
Th' oppressor's wrong,

945
00:48:12.750 --> 00:48:16.370
the proud man's contumely,
The pangs of disprized love,

946
00:48:16.500 --> 00:48:18.580
the law's delay,
The insolence of office,

947
00:48:18.700 --> 00:48:21.500
and the spurns
That patient merit of th'unworthy takes,

948
00:48:21.620 --> 00:48:25.700
When he himself might his quietus make
With a bare bodkin?

949
00:48:27.000 --> 00:48:30.370
Who would fardels bear,

950
00:48:30.500 --> 00:48:34.250
To grunt and sweat
under a weary life,

951
00:48:34.370 --> 00:48:36.870
But that the dread
of something after death,

952
00:48:38.700 --> 00:48:40.250
The undiscovered country,

953
00:48:40.370 --> 00:48:42.950
from whose bourn
No traveller returns...

954
00:48:44.120 --> 00:48:45.750
...puzzles the will,

955
00:48:45.870 --> 00:48:49.250
And makes us rather bear
those ills we have

956
00:48:49.370 --> 00:48:52.080
Than fly to others
that we know not of?

957
00:48:54.250 --> 00:48:55.500
Thus conscience

958
00:48:56.250 --> 00:48:58.200
does make cowards

959
00:48:58.950 --> 00:49:00.200
of us all,

960
00:49:02.580 --> 00:49:06.250
And thus
the native hue of resolution

961
00:49:06.750 --> 00:49:11.120
Is sicklied o'er
with the pale cast of thought,

962
00:49:11.250 --> 00:49:12.500
And enterprises

963
00:49:12.620 --> 00:49:15.080
of great pitch and moment

964
00:49:15.200 --> 00:49:16.700
With this regard

965
00:49:16.830 --> 00:49:18.830
their currents turn awry

966
00:49:18.950 --> 00:49:21.450
And lose the name of action.

967
00:49:22.080 --> 00:49:23.580
How does my good Lord Hamlet?

968
00:49:23.700 --> 00:49:25.120
Oh. (Chuckles)

969
00:49:25.250 --> 00:49:26.870
Well, God-a-mercy.

970
00:49:27.500 --> 00:49:30.120
Do you know me, my lord?

971
00:49:31.620 --> 00:49:34.120
Excellent well.
You are a fishmonger.

972
00:49:34.250 --> 00:49:35.450
Not I, my lord.

973
00:49:35.580 --> 00:49:37.370
Then I would you were
so honest a man.

974
00:49:37.500 --> 00:49:38.750
- Honest, my lord?
- Ay sir.

975
00:49:38.870 --> 00:49:40.580
To be honest, as this world goes,

976
00:49:40.700 --> 00:49:42.950
is to be one man
picked out of ten thousand.

977
00:49:43.080 --> 00:49:44.450
That's very true, my lord.

978
00:49:45.370 --> 00:49:48.620
For if the sun breed maggots
in a dead dog.

979
00:49:50.000 --> 00:49:52.080
- Have you a daughter?
- I have, my lord.

980
00:49:52.200 --> 00:49:53.870
Let her not walk i'th' sun.

981
00:49:54.500 --> 00:49:56.200
Conception is a blessing,

982
00:49:56.330 --> 00:49:58.250
but not as your daughter
may conceive-friend, look to't.

983
00:49:58.370 --> 00:50:00.200
Still harping on my daughter.

984
00:50:00.330 --> 00:50:03.000
Yet he knew me not at first;
he said I was a fishmonger.

985
00:50:03.120 --> 00:50:06.370
He is far gone.
I'll speak to him again.

986
00:50:08.250 --> 00:50:09.750
(Audience laughs)

987
00:50:13.500 --> 00:50:15.000
Truly in my youth

988
00:50:15.120 --> 00:50:18.330
I suffered much extremity for love,

989
00:50:19.200 --> 00:50:20.200
very near this.

990
00:50:30.080 --> 00:50:31.500
What do you read, my lord?

991
00:50:33.500 --> 00:50:34.500
Words.

992
00:50:37.450 --> 00:50:38.450
Words.

993
00:50:39.870 --> 00:50:41.000
Words.

994
00:50:41.120 --> 00:50:42.700
What is the matter, my lord?

995
00:50:44.330 --> 00:50:46.200
Between who?

996
00:50:49.700 --> 00:50:51.500
I mean the matter that you read,
my lord.

997
00:50:52.750 --> 00:50:54.950
Oh. Slanders, sir.

998
00:50:55.500 --> 00:50:57.830
For the satirical rogue says here

999
00:50:57.950 --> 00:51:00.250
that old men have grey beards.

1000
00:51:00.370 --> 00:51:02.450
- That... Oh.
- (Audience laughs)

1001
00:51:02.580 --> 00:51:05.620
Their faces are wrinkled. Aw.

1002
00:51:06.200 --> 00:51:08.500
And that they have
a plentiful lack of wit.

1003
00:51:09.120 --> 00:51:10.870
- Ah.
- (Audience laughs)

1004
00:51:11.000 --> 00:51:14.500
All which, sir, though I most powerfully
and potently believe,

1005
00:51:14.620 --> 00:51:16.870
yet I hold it not honesty
to have it thus set down.

1006
00:51:17.000 --> 00:51:20.000
For you yourself, sir,
shall grow old as I am,

1007
00:51:20.120 --> 00:51:23.750
if like a crab
you could go backward.

1008
00:51:23.870 --> 00:51:26.200
Though this be madness,
yet there is method in't.

1009
00:51:26.330 --> 00:51:28.750
Will you walk out of the air,
my lord?

1010
00:51:29.450 --> 00:51:31.370
Into my grave?

1011
00:51:32.000 --> 00:51:33.700
Indeed, that's out of the air.

1012
00:51:33.830 --> 00:51:35.830
How pregnant
sometimes his replies are,

1013
00:51:35.950 --> 00:51:37.500
a happiness
that often madness hits on,

1014
00:51:37.620 --> 00:51:40.200
which reason and sanity
could not so prosperously be delivered of.

1015
00:51:40.330 --> 00:51:42.950
I will suddenly contrive the means of meeting
between him and my daughter.

1016
00:51:43.080 --> 00:51:44.250
I will take my leave of him.

1017
00:51:44.370 --> 00:51:47.370
You cannot, sir, take from me anything
that I will more willingly part withal.

1018
00:51:50.620 --> 00:51:52.250
(Audience laughs)

1019
00:51:54.200 --> 00:51:55.620
Except my life.

1020
00:51:59.080 --> 00:52:00.250
Except my life.

1021
00:52:02.700 --> 00:52:04.120
Except my life.

1022
00:52:11.000 --> 00:52:12.500
Fare you well, my lord.

1023
00:52:12.620 --> 00:52:15.080
These tedious old fools.

1024
00:52:16.000 --> 00:52:17.000
Oh.

1025
00:52:17.120 --> 00:52:18.250
(Chuckles)

1026
00:52:18.370 --> 00:52:19.750
(Audience laughs)

1027
00:52:20.370 --> 00:52:22.450
You go to seek the Lord Hamlet.
There he is.

1028
00:52:22.580 --> 00:52:25.330
- God save you, sir.
- My honoured lord!

1029
00:52:25.450 --> 00:52:28.080
- My most dear lord.
- My excellent good friends!

1030
00:52:28.200 --> 00:52:31.370
How dost thou, Guildenstern?

1031
00:52:31.500 --> 00:52:33.500
Ah, Rosencrantz.

1032
00:52:35.120 --> 00:52:38.250
- Good lads, how do you both?
- As the indifferent children of the earth.

1033
00:52:38.370 --> 00:52:39.950
Happy in that we are not over-happy:

1034
00:52:40.080 --> 00:52:43.250
on Fortune's cap
we are not the very button.

1035
00:52:43.370 --> 00:52:45.370
- Nor the soles of her shoe?
- Neither, my lord.

1036
00:52:45.500 --> 00:52:48.120
Then you live about her waist,
or in the middle of her favours?

1037
00:52:48.250 --> 00:52:50.250
Faith, her privates we.

1038
00:52:50.370 --> 00:52:53.080
Ooh, she is a strumpet.
What news?

1039
00:52:53.200 --> 00:52:55.750
None, my lord,
but the world's grown honest.

1040
00:52:55.870 --> 00:52:57.330
Then is doomsday near.

1041
00:52:57.450 --> 00:52:58.870
What have you, my good friends,

1042
00:52:59.000 --> 00:53:02.120
deserved at the hands of Fortune
that she sends you to prison hither?

1043
00:53:02.250 --> 00:53:04.750
- Prison, my lord?
- Denmark's a prison.

1044
00:53:04.870 --> 00:53:06.370
Then is the world one.

1045
00:53:06.500 --> 00:53:08.500
A goodly one,
in which there are many confines,

1046
00:53:08.620 --> 00:53:11.500
wards, and dungeons,
Denmark being one o'th' worst.

1047
00:53:11.620 --> 00:53:13.330
We think not so, my lord.

1048
00:53:13.450 --> 00:53:15.330
Why, then 'tis none to you,

1049
00:53:15.450 --> 00:53:19.750
for there is nothing either good or bad
but thinking makes it so.

1050
00:53:19.870 --> 00:53:21.450
To me it is a prison.

1051
00:53:21.580 --> 00:53:24.620
Why, then your ambition makes it one:
'tis too narrow for your mind.

1052
00:53:25.750 --> 00:53:27.620
O God.

1053
00:53:28.750 --> 00:53:30.750
I could be bounded in a nutshell

1054
00:53:30.870 --> 00:53:34.080
and count myself
a king of infinite space.

1055
00:53:35.370 --> 00:53:37.700
Were it not that I have bad dreams.

1056
00:53:39.700 --> 00:53:40.830
Shall we to th' court?

1057
00:53:40.950 --> 00:53:42.950
For my fay, I cannot reason.

1058
00:53:43.080 --> 00:53:45.330
(Both) We'll wait upon you.

1059
00:53:45.450 --> 00:53:48.870
No such matter. I will not sort you
with the rest of my servants.

1060
00:53:50.250 --> 00:53:53.450
But in the beaten way of friendship,
what make you at Elsinore?

1061
00:53:53.580 --> 00:53:55.580
To visit you, my lord,
no other occasion.

1062
00:53:55.700 --> 00:53:58.250
Beggar that I am,
I am even poor in thanks,

1063
00:53:58.370 --> 00:53:59.500
but I thank you.

1064
00:54:01.450 --> 00:54:02.870
Were you not sent for?

1065
00:54:03.620 --> 00:54:06.830
Is it your own inclining?
Is it a free visitation?

1066
00:54:12.750 --> 00:54:13.950
Speak.

1067
00:54:14.080 --> 00:54:16.250
- Ah! (Laughs)
- (Audience laughs)

1068
00:54:16.370 --> 00:54:18.080
What should we say, my lord?

1069
00:54:18.200 --> 00:54:19.870
Anything but to th' purpose.

1070
00:54:20.000 --> 00:54:21.080
(Guildenstern chuckles)

1071
00:54:21.200 --> 00:54:24.750
You were sent for, and there is
a kind of confession in your looks,

1072
00:54:24.870 --> 00:54:27.450
which your modesties
have not craft enough to colour.

1073
00:54:28.120 --> 00:54:30.120
I know the good King and Queen
have sent for you.

1074
00:54:30.250 --> 00:54:32.000
- To what end, my lord?
- That, you must teach me.

1075
00:54:32.120 --> 00:54:35.200
But let me conjure you,
by the rights of our fellowship,

1076
00:54:35.330 --> 00:54:37.500
by the consonancy of our youth!
Poof.

1077
00:54:37.620 --> 00:54:39.000
- (Laughs)
- (Audience laughs)

1078
00:54:39.120 --> 00:54:42.080
And by the obligation
of our ever-preserved love,

1079
00:54:42.620 --> 00:54:44.830
be even and direct with me

1080
00:54:44.950 --> 00:54:46.370
whether you were sent for or no.

1081
00:54:48.500 --> 00:54:50.000
(Rosencrantz) What say you?

1082
00:54:50.120 --> 00:54:51.700
Nay, then I have an eye of you.

1083
00:54:51.830 --> 00:54:54.250
If you love me, hold me not off.

1084
00:54:55.870 --> 00:54:57.750
My lord, we were sent for.

1085
00:55:02.120 --> 00:55:03.620
(Audience laughs)

1086
00:55:04.120 --> 00:55:05.620
I will tell you why;

1087
00:55:06.330 --> 00:55:08.500
so shall my anticipation
prevent your discovery,

1088
00:55:08.620 --> 00:55:11.250
and your secrecy to the King and Queen
moult no feather.

1089
00:55:13.750 --> 00:55:16.370
I have of late,
but wherefore I know not,

1090
00:55:16.500 --> 00:55:20.620
lost all my mirth,
forgone all custom of exercises;

1091
00:55:20.750 --> 00:55:23.580
and indeed it goes
so heavily with my disposition

1092
00:55:23.700 --> 00:55:27.370
that this goodly frame, the earth...

1093
00:55:28.500 --> 00:55:31.000
...seems to me a sterile promontory.

1094
00:55:31.830 --> 00:55:33.500
This most excellent canopy the air.

1095
00:55:33.620 --> 00:55:36.870
Look you,
this brave o'erhanging firmament.

1096
00:55:37.000 --> 00:55:40.700
This majestical roof
fretted with golden fire.

1097
00:55:41.700 --> 00:55:44.870
Why, it appeareth nothing to me...

1098
00:55:45.870 --> 00:55:49.250
...but a foul and pestilent congregation
of vapours.

1099
00:55:51.950 --> 00:55:54.450
What a piece of work is a man.

1100
00:55:55.620 --> 00:55:57.200
How noble in reason.

1101
00:55:57.750 --> 00:55:59.370
How infinite in faculties.

1102
00:55:59.870 --> 00:56:03.450
In form and moving
how express and admirable.

1103
00:56:04.370 --> 00:56:07.080
In action how like an angel.

1104
00:56:07.830 --> 00:56:09.120
In apprehension...

1105
00:56:10.370 --> 00:56:11.830
...how like a god.

1106
00:56:13.620 --> 00:56:15.000
The beauty of the world.

1107
00:56:16.120 --> 00:56:18.000
The paragon of animals.

1108
00:56:19.500 --> 00:56:20.870
And yet, to me...

1109
00:56:22.000 --> 00:56:25.330
...what is
this quintessence of dust?

1110
00:56:28.330 --> 00:56:29.750
Man delights not me.

1111
00:56:29.870 --> 00:56:31.120
(Chuckles) Um...

1112
00:56:31.250 --> 00:56:32.250
No.

1113
00:56:32.870 --> 00:56:34.620
Nor woman neither.

1114
00:56:34.750 --> 00:56:36.870
Though by your smiling
you seem to say so.

1115
00:56:37.000 --> 00:56:38.500
My lord, there was no such stuff
in my thoughts.

1116
00:56:38.620 --> 00:56:40.750
Why did ye laugh then,
when I said man delights not me?

1117
00:56:40.870 --> 00:56:43.120
To think, my lord,
if you delight not in man,

1118
00:56:43.250 --> 00:56:47.370
what lenten entertainment
the players shall receive from you.

1119
00:56:47.500 --> 00:56:48.500
We coted them on the way,

1120
00:56:48.620 --> 00:56:50.330
and hither are they coming
to offer you service.

1121
00:56:50.450 --> 00:56:51.450
What players are they?

1122
00:56:51.580 --> 00:56:54.370
Even those you were wont
to take such delight in,

1123
00:56:54.500 --> 00:56:56.370
the tragedians of the city!

1124
00:56:56.500 --> 00:57:00.580
Oh! Gentlemen, your hands!
You are welcome to Elsinore!

1125
00:57:00.700 --> 00:57:02.750
But my uncle-father
and aunt-mother are deceived.

1126
00:57:02.870 --> 00:57:04.250
In what, my dear lord?

1127
00:57:04.370 --> 00:57:05.830
I am but mad north-north-west.

1128
00:57:05.950 --> 00:57:08.250
When the wind is southerly,
I know a hawk from a handsaw.

1129
00:57:08.370 --> 00:57:10.000
Well be with you, gentlemen!

1130
00:57:10.120 --> 00:57:14.080
Hark you, I will prophesy
he comes to tell me of the players.

1131
00:57:15.120 --> 00:57:16.870
My lord, I have news to tell you.

1132
00:57:17.000 --> 00:57:19.750
- The actors are come hither, my lord.
- (Hamlet) Buzz, buzz.

1133
00:57:19.870 --> 00:57:20.950
Buzz, buzz.

1134
00:57:21.080 --> 00:57:23.330
The best actors in the world,
either for...

1135
00:57:24.450 --> 00:57:27.870
♪ Tragedy, comedy, history, pastoral

1136
00:57:28.000 --> 00:57:30.830
♪ Pastoral-comical
historical-pastoral

1137
00:57:30.950 --> 00:57:35.120
♪ Tragical-historical
tragical-comical-historical-pastoral

1138
00:57:35.250 --> 00:57:36.500
♪ Scene individable

1139
00:57:36.620 --> 00:57:42.450
♪ Or poem unlimited ♪

1140
00:57:44.120 --> 00:57:46.200
You are welcome, masters!
Welcome, all!

1141
00:57:46.330 --> 00:57:48.500
I am glad to see thee well!

1142
00:57:49.120 --> 00:57:51.500
(Panting) Welcome, good friends.

1143
00:57:52.500 --> 00:57:54.370
O, old friend!

1144
00:57:54.500 --> 00:57:56.200
My lady and mistress!

1145
00:57:56.330 --> 00:57:58.370
My dear lord.

1146
00:57:59.120 --> 00:58:02.370
Your ladyship is nearer to heaven
than when I saw you last.

1147
00:58:05.000 --> 00:58:07.120
We'll have a speech straight!

1148
00:58:07.250 --> 00:58:10.250
Come, give us a taste of your quality!
Come, a passionate speech!

1149
00:58:10.870 --> 00:58:12.830
What speech, my good lord?

1150
00:58:12.950 --> 00:58:15.450
I heard thee speak me a speech once,

1151
00:58:15.580 --> 00:58:17.700
but it was never acted,
or if it was, not above once,

1152
00:58:17.830 --> 00:58:20.000
for the play, I remember,
pleased not the million,

1153
00:58:20.120 --> 00:58:21.830
'twas caviar to the general.

1154
00:58:21.950 --> 00:58:24.750
But it was an excellent play.

1155
00:58:24.870 --> 00:58:27.620
One speech in't I chiefly loved.

1156
00:58:27.750 --> 00:58:30.450
'Twas Aeneas' tale to Dido.

1157
00:58:31.370 --> 00:58:33.500
When he speaks of Priam's slaughter.

1158
00:58:34.120 --> 00:58:37.250
If it live in your memory,
begin at this line.

1159
00:58:37.370 --> 00:58:39.080
Let me see, let me see...

1160
00:58:40.500 --> 00:58:42.000
"The rugged Pyrrhus,

1161
00:58:42.120 --> 00:58:43.830
like th'Hyrcanian beast..."

1162
00:58:43.950 --> 00:58:45.000
'Tis not so.

1163
00:58:45.750 --> 00:58:47.620
It begins with Pyrrhus.

1164
00:58:48.950 --> 00:58:52.200
"The rugged Pyrrhus,
he whose sable arms,

1165
00:58:52.330 --> 00:58:55.120
Black as his purpose,
did the night resemble

1166
00:58:55.620 --> 00:58:58.620
When he lay couched
in the ominous horse,

1167
00:58:58.750 --> 00:59:03.000
Hath now this dread
and black complexion smeared

1168
00:59:03.120 --> 00:59:04.870
With heraldry more dismal.

1169
00:59:05.700 --> 00:59:09.870
Head to foot
Now is he total gules,

1170
00:59:10.000 --> 00:59:13.250
horridly tricked
With blood of fathers...

1171
00:59:16.500 --> 00:59:17.500
...mothers...

1172
00:59:18.620 --> 00:59:20.250
...daughters, sons."

1173
00:59:20.370 --> 00:59:24.000
(Both) "And thus o'ersized
with coagulate gore,

1174
00:59:24.120 --> 00:59:27.580
With eyes like carbuncles,

1175
00:59:27.700 --> 00:59:29.620
the hellish Pyrrhus

1176
00:59:29.750 --> 00:59:33.250
Old grandsire Priam seeks."

1177
00:59:33.370 --> 00:59:36.580
'Fore God, my lord, well spoken,
with good accent and good discretion.

1178
00:59:37.120 --> 00:59:38.200
So proceed you.

1179
00:59:40.830 --> 00:59:43.250
"Anon he finds him,

1180
00:59:43.370 --> 00:59:45.700
Striking too short at Greeks.

1181
00:59:45.830 --> 00:59:48.870
His antique sword,
Rebellious to his arm,

1182
00:59:49.000 --> 00:59:50.870
lies where it falls,

1183
00:59:51.000 --> 00:59:53.000
Repugnant to command.

1184
00:59:54.580 --> 00:59:56.120
Unequal matched,

1185
00:59:56.870 --> 00:59:59.580
Pyrrhus at Priam drives,

1186
00:59:59.700 --> 01:00:02.700
in rage strikes wide;

1187
01:00:03.370 --> 01:00:06.000
But with the whiff and wind
of his fell sword

1188
01:00:06.120 --> 01:00:09.370
Th'unnerved father falls.

1189
01:00:10.830 --> 01:00:13.750
Then senseless Ilium,

1190
01:00:13.870 --> 01:00:15.830
Seeming to feel this blow,

1191
01:00:15.950 --> 01:00:19.080
with flaming top
Stoops to his base,

1192
01:00:19.200 --> 01:00:22.500
and with a hideous crash
Takes prisoner Pyrrhus' ear.

1193
01:00:22.620 --> 01:00:24.330
For lo, his sword,

1194
01:00:24.450 --> 01:00:28.580
Which was declining on the milky head
Of reverend Priam,

1195
01:00:28.700 --> 01:00:32.700
seemed i'th' air to stick.

1196
01:00:35.120 --> 01:00:39.330
So, as a painted tyrant,
Pyrrhus stood.

1197
01:00:40.450 --> 01:00:44.120
And like a neutral
to his will and matter,

1198
01:00:44.250 --> 01:00:46.000
did nothing.

1199
01:00:49.120 --> 01:00:53.200
But as we often see
against some storm...

1200
01:00:54.450 --> 01:00:57.450
...A silence in the heavens,

1201
01:00:57.580 --> 01:01:01.750
the rack stand still,
The bold winds speechless,

1202
01:01:02.250 --> 01:01:06.250
and the orb below
As hush as death,

1203
01:01:06.370 --> 01:01:10.370
anon the dreadful thunder
Doth rend the region.

1204
01:01:10.500 --> 01:01:12.370
So after Pyrrhus' pause

1205
01:01:13.000 --> 01:01:16.450
Aroused vengeance
sets him new awork,

1206
01:01:17.120 --> 01:01:20.450
And never did
the Cyclops' hammers fall

1207
01:01:20.580 --> 01:01:22.450
On Mars's armour,

1208
01:01:22.580 --> 01:01:25.500
forged for proof eterne,

1209
01:01:25.620 --> 01:01:29.500
With less remorse
than Pyrrhus' bleeding sword

1210
01:01:29.620 --> 01:01:32.950
Now falls on Priam!

1211
01:01:37.750 --> 01:01:38.750
Out!

1212
01:01:38.870 --> 01:01:42.750
Out, thou strumpet Fortune!

1213
01:01:44.620 --> 01:01:46.080
All you gods

1214
01:01:46.870 --> 01:01:50.500
In general synod
take away her power,

1215
01:01:51.120 --> 01:01:54.830
Break all the spokes
and fellies from her wheel,

1216
01:01:54.950 --> 01:01:58.950
And bowl the round nave
down the hill of heaven

1217
01:01:59.620 --> 01:02:02.370
As low as to the fiends."

1218
01:02:02.500 --> 01:02:04.450
This is too long.

1219
01:02:04.580 --> 01:02:06.500
(Audience laughs)

1220
01:02:06.620 --> 01:02:10.000
It shall to the barber's
with your beard!

1221
01:02:10.620 --> 01:02:11.870
Prithee say on.

1222
01:02:12.000 --> 01:02:15.620
He's for a jig or a tale of bawdry,
or he sleeps.

1223
01:02:16.450 --> 01:02:18.450
Say on, come to Hecuba.

1224
01:02:19.000 --> 01:02:20.370
"But who...

1225
01:02:23.580 --> 01:02:27.200
O who, had seen the mobled queen?"

1226
01:02:27.330 --> 01:02:29.450
- "The mobled queen"?
- "Mobled queen" is good.

1227
01:02:29.580 --> 01:02:32.080
"Run barefoot up and down,

1228
01:02:32.200 --> 01:02:35.870
threat'ning the flames
With bisson rheum,

1229
01:02:36.000 --> 01:02:38.950
a clout upon that head
Where late the diadem stood,

1230
01:02:39.080 --> 01:02:40.370
and, for a robe,

1231
01:02:40.500 --> 01:02:42.870
About her lank
and all o'erteemed loins

1232
01:02:43.000 --> 01:02:46.870
A blanket,
in th'alarm of fear caught up.

1233
01:02:47.370 --> 01:02:49.950
Who this had seen...

1234
01:02:51.000 --> 01:02:55.000
...with tongue in venom steeped,
'Gainst Fortune's state

1235
01:02:55.120 --> 01:02:57.450
would treason

1236
01:02:57.580 --> 01:02:59.200
have pronounced.

1237
01:03:00.080 --> 01:03:03.200
But if the gods themselves
did see her then,

1238
01:03:04.080 --> 01:03:08.500
When she saw Pyrrhus
make malicious sport

1239
01:03:08.620 --> 01:03:12.870
In mincing with his sword
her husband's limbs,

1240
01:03:13.620 --> 01:03:18.370
The instant burst of clamour
that she made!

1241
01:03:21.500 --> 01:03:26.000
Unless things mortal
move them not at all,

1242
01:03:26.700 --> 01:03:30.250
Would have made milch
the burning eyes of heaven

1243
01:03:30.370 --> 01:03:33.700
And passion in the gods."

1244
01:03:33.830 --> 01:03:36.000
Look, my lord,
if she has not changed her colour

1245
01:03:36.120 --> 01:03:37.620
and has tears in her eyes.

1246
01:03:37.750 --> 01:03:40.000
Prithee no more, good heart,
no more.

1247
01:03:41.370 --> 01:03:42.870
We’ll hear a play tomorrow night.

1248
01:03:43.370 --> 01:03:46.870
Good my lord, will you see
the players well bestowed?

1249
01:03:47.000 --> 01:03:49.620
For they are the abstract
and brief chronicles of the time.

1250
01:03:49.750 --> 01:03:52.000
My lord, I will use them
according to their desert.

1251
01:03:52.120 --> 01:03:55.120
(Shouting) God's bodkin, man,
much better!

1252
01:03:59.950 --> 01:04:03.120
Use every man after his desert,
and who shall scape whipping?

1253
01:04:04.500 --> 01:04:05.450
Take them in.

1254
01:04:06.000 --> 01:04:10.120
Welcome my good fellows.

1255
01:04:10.830 --> 01:04:12.450
Follow him, friends.

1256
01:04:14.000 --> 01:04:15.250
Old friend.

1257
01:04:18.870 --> 01:04:21.450
Can you play The Murder of Gonzago?

1258
01:04:21.580 --> 01:04:22.580
Oh.

1259
01:04:23.120 --> 01:04:25.330
The Murder of Gonzago?

1260
01:04:27.750 --> 01:04:28.870
Ay, my lord.

1261
01:04:29.000 --> 01:04:30.870
We’ll ha’t tomorrow night.

1262
01:04:31.000 --> 01:04:32.370
You could for a need

1263
01:04:32.500 --> 01:04:35.750
study a speech
which I would set down and insert in’t,

1264
01:04:35.870 --> 01:04:37.000
could you not?

1265
01:04:37.120 --> 01:04:38.250
Ay, my lord.

1266
01:04:38.370 --> 01:04:40.250
Very well. Follow that lord.

1267
01:04:41.620 --> 01:04:44.080
And look you mock him not.

1268
01:04:51.250 --> 01:04:53.250
Now I am alone.

1269
01:04:53.370 --> 01:04:54.370
(Clears his throat)

1270
01:04:54.500 --> 01:04:56.250
(Audience laughs)

1271
01:04:57.870 --> 01:05:00.370
My good friends,
I'll leave you till night.

1272
01:05:01.870 --> 01:05:03.200
You are welcome to Elsinore.

1273
01:05:03.330 --> 01:05:04.330
Good my lord.

1274
01:05:08.870 --> 01:05:12.370
O what a rogue
and peasant slave am I.

1275
01:05:14.500 --> 01:05:17.370
Is it not monstrous
that this player here,

1276
01:05:18.120 --> 01:05:20.620
But in a fiction,
in a dream of passion,

1277
01:05:20.750 --> 01:05:22.830
Could force her soul
so to her own conceit

1278
01:05:22.950 --> 01:05:25.000
That from its working
all her visage wanned,

1279
01:05:25.750 --> 01:05:28.200
Tears in her eyes,
distraction in her aspect,

1280
01:05:28.330 --> 01:05:29.120
A broken voice.

1281
01:05:30.370 --> 01:05:31.580
And all for nothing.

1282
01:05:32.620 --> 01:05:33.870
For Hecuba.

1283
01:05:34.000 --> 01:05:36.620
What's Hecuba to her,
or she to Hecuba,

1284
01:05:36.750 --> 01:05:38.330
That she should weep for her?

1285
01:05:39.370 --> 01:05:40.250
What would she do

1286
01:05:40.370 --> 01:05:43.250
Had she the motive and the cue for passion
That I have?

1287
01:05:43.370 --> 01:05:45.620
She would drown the stage
with tears,

1288
01:05:45.750 --> 01:05:48.370
Make mad the guilty
and appal the free.

1289
01:05:49.080 --> 01:05:52.870
Yet I,
A dull and muddy-mettled rascal, peak

1290
01:05:53.000 --> 01:05:56.200
Like John-a-dreams,
unpregnant of my cause,

1291
01:05:56.330 --> 01:05:59.450
And can say nothing.
No, not for a king

1292
01:05:59.580 --> 01:06:02.250
Upon whose property
and most dear life

1293
01:06:02.370 --> 01:06:05.000
A damned defeat was made.

1294
01:06:12.870 --> 01:06:14.330
Am I a coward?

1295
01:06:18.370 --> 01:06:19.830
Who calls me villain...

1296
01:06:21.500 --> 01:06:23.080
...breaks my pate across,

1297
01:06:23.950 --> 01:06:25.750
Tweaks me by the nose...

1298
01:06:26.870 --> 01:06:30.620
...gives me the lie i'th' throat
As deep as to the lungs?

1299
01:06:30.750 --> 01:06:32.700
Who does me this? Ha.

1300
01:06:35.750 --> 01:06:37.620
'Swounds, I should take it:

1301
01:06:38.330 --> 01:06:41.620
for it cannot be
But I am pigeon-livered.

1302
01:06:42.500 --> 01:06:45.620
Or ere this I should ha' fatted
all the region kites

1303
01:06:45.750 --> 01:06:47.370
With this slave's offal!

1304
01:06:47.500 --> 01:06:49.580
Bloody, bawdy villain!

1305
01:06:49.700 --> 01:06:55.370
Remorseless, treacherous,
lecherous, kindless villain!

1306
01:06:59.000 --> 01:07:01.750
- Why, what an ass am I.
- (Audience laughs quietly)

1307
01:07:01.870 --> 01:07:03.750
This is most brave.

1308
01:07:03.870 --> 01:07:05.370
- (Quiet cheer)
- (Audience laughs)

1309
01:07:05.500 --> 01:07:08.620
That I,
the son of a dear father murdered,

1310
01:07:08.750 --> 01:07:10.500
Prompted to my revenge

1311
01:07:10.620 --> 01:07:12.870
by heaven and hell,

1312
01:07:13.000 --> 01:07:15.000
Must, like a whore,

1313
01:07:15.120 --> 01:07:17.370
unpack my heart with words.

1314
01:07:20.080 --> 01:07:21.620
Fie upon't.

1315
01:07:22.250 --> 01:07:23.450
Foh.

1316
01:07:25.620 --> 01:07:27.620
About, my brains.

1317
01:07:29.620 --> 01:07:32.080
Hum.

1318
01:07:33.500 --> 01:07:34.830
I have heard

1319
01:07:35.450 --> 01:07:38.620
That guilty creatures
sitting at a play...

1320
01:07:41.750 --> 01:07:44.000
...Have,
by the very cunning of the scene,

1321
01:07:44.120 --> 01:07:45.830
Been struck so to the soul

1322
01:07:45.950 --> 01:07:48.830
that presently
They have proclaimed their malefactions.

1323
01:07:49.450 --> 01:07:51.870
For murder,
though it have no tongue,

1324
01:07:52.000 --> 01:07:54.750
will speak
With most miraculous organ.

1325
01:07:54.870 --> 01:07:56.830
I'll have these players play something
like the murder of my father

1326
01:07:56.950 --> 01:07:58.120
before mine uncle.

1327
01:07:58.250 --> 01:08:00.250
I'll observe his looks;
I'll tent him to the quick.

1328
01:08:00.370 --> 01:08:03.580
If he do blench, I know my course.

1329
01:08:04.830 --> 01:08:07.250
The spirit that I have seen...

1330
01:08:09.120 --> 01:08:10.750
...May be a devil.

1331
01:08:11.870 --> 01:08:14.700
And the devil hath power
T'assume a pleasing shape, yea,

1332
01:08:14.830 --> 01:08:17.750
and perhaps,
Out of my weakness and my melancholy,

1333
01:08:17.870 --> 01:08:19.830
As he is very potent
with such spirits,

1334
01:08:19.950 --> 01:08:22.370
Abuses me to damn me.

1335
01:08:24.000 --> 01:08:27.620
I'll have grounds
More relative than this.

1336
01:08:29.000 --> 01:08:30.330
The play's the thing...

1337
01:08:31.580 --> 01:08:34.250
...Wherein I'll catch
the conscience of the King.

1338
01:08:34.370 --> 01:08:36.580
(Dramatic orchestral music)

1339
01:08:41.250 --> 01:08:43.120
And can you
by no drift of conference

1340
01:08:43.250 --> 01:08:45.620
Get from him
why he puts on this confusion?

1341
01:08:45.750 --> 01:08:47.870
He does confess
he feels himself distracted,

1342
01:08:48.000 --> 01:08:50.370
But from what cause
he will by no means speak.

1343
01:08:50.500 --> 01:08:52.830
Nor do we find him forward
to be sounded,

1344
01:08:52.950 --> 01:08:55.700
But with a crafty madness
keeps aloof.

1345
01:08:55.830 --> 01:08:57.500
- Did he receive you well?
- Most like a gentleman.

1346
01:08:57.620 --> 01:08:59.750
But with much forcing
of his disposition.

1347
01:08:59.870 --> 01:09:01.500
Did you assay him to any pastime?

1348
01:09:01.620 --> 01:09:04.750
Madam, it so fell out that certain players
We o'erraught on the way.

1349
01:09:04.870 --> 01:09:08.250
Of these we told him, and there did seem
in him a kind of joy to hear of it.

1350
01:09:08.370 --> 01:09:10.200
They are here about the court,
And, as I think,

1351
01:09:10.330 --> 01:09:13.000
they have already order
This night to play before him.

1352
01:09:13.120 --> 01:09:14.620
'Tis most true,
And he beseeched me

1353
01:09:14.750 --> 01:09:16.950
to entreat your Majesties
To hear and see the matter.

1354
01:09:17.080 --> 01:09:18.370
With all my heart;

1355
01:09:18.500 --> 01:09:21.250
and it doth much content me
To hear him so inclined.

1356
01:09:22.120 --> 01:09:26.500
Good gentlemen, give him a further edge,
And drive his purpose into these delights.

1357
01:09:26.620 --> 01:09:28.370
- Go seek him out.
- We shall, my lord.

1358
01:09:28.500 --> 01:09:30.500
Sweet Gertrude, leave us too,

1359
01:09:30.620 --> 01:09:33.330
For we have closely
sent for Hamlet hither

1360
01:09:33.450 --> 01:09:36.620
That he, as 'twere by accident, may here
Affront Ophelia;

1361
01:09:36.750 --> 01:09:40.200
and we may gather,
If't be th'affliction of his love or no

1362
01:09:40.330 --> 01:09:41.450
That thus he suffers for.

1363
01:09:42.120 --> 01:09:43.120
Ophelia...

1364
01:09:44.120 --> 01:09:46.580
...I do wish your good beauties
be the happy cause

1365
01:09:46.700 --> 01:09:48.120
Of Hamlet's wildness;

1366
01:09:48.250 --> 01:09:51.330
so shall I hope your virtues
Will bring him to his wonted way again.

1367
01:09:51.450 --> 01:09:53.080
Madam, I wish it may.

1368
01:09:53.750 --> 01:09:55.450
Ophelia, walk you here,

1369
01:09:55.580 --> 01:09:58.120
Gracious, so please you,
We will bestow ourselves,

1370
01:09:58.250 --> 01:10:00.500
Read on this book.

1371
01:10:00.620 --> 01:10:03.620
I hear him coming.
Let's withdraw, my lord.

1372
01:10:06.870 --> 01:10:08.580
(Whispering)

1373
01:10:09.700 --> 01:10:10.700
(Hamlet chuckles)

1374
01:10:15.330 --> 01:10:16.870
Soft you now,
The fair Ophelia.

1375
01:10:17.000 --> 01:10:18.870
Mwah, mwah, mwah,
mwah, mwah, mwah, mwah!

1376
01:10:19.000 --> 01:10:22.500
Nymph, in thy orisons
Be all my sins remembered.

1377
01:10:22.620 --> 01:10:24.950
Good my lord,

1378
01:10:25.080 --> 01:10:28.000
How does your honour
for this many a day?

1379
01:10:28.120 --> 01:10:30.000
I humbly thank you, well.

1380
01:10:30.120 --> 01:10:31.620
My lord,

1381
01:10:31.750 --> 01:10:34.000
I have remembrances of yours

1382
01:10:34.120 --> 01:10:37.080
That I have longed long
to redeliver.

1383
01:10:37.200 --> 01:10:38.500
I pray you now receive them.

1384
01:10:38.620 --> 01:10:40.620
No, not I. I never gave you aught.

1385
01:10:41.580 --> 01:10:45.200
My honoured lord,
you know right well you did,

1386
01:10:45.330 --> 01:10:48.580
And with them words
of so sweet breath composed

1387
01:10:48.700 --> 01:10:51.000
As made the things more rich.

1388
01:10:51.750 --> 01:10:54.830
Their perfume lost,
Take these again; for to the noble mind

1389
01:10:54.950 --> 01:10:57.580
Rich gifts wax poor
when givers prove unkind.

1390
01:11:00.620 --> 01:11:02.120
There, my lord.

1391
01:11:08.000 --> 01:11:09.620
- Are you honest?
- My lord?

1392
01:11:09.750 --> 01:11:11.830
- Are you fair?
- What means your lordship?

1393
01:11:15.450 --> 01:11:16.450
Oh.

1394
01:11:18.870 --> 01:11:20.200
I did love you.

1395
01:11:21.080 --> 01:11:22.080
Once.

1396
01:11:22.200 --> 01:11:24.330
Indeed, my lord.

1397
01:11:25.080 --> 01:11:26.370
You made me believe so.

1398
01:11:28.500 --> 01:11:30.080
You should not have believed me.

1399
01:11:31.120 --> 01:11:33.250
I loved you not.

1400
01:11:34.000 --> 01:11:35.870
I was the more deceived.

1401
01:11:39.580 --> 01:11:41.120
Get thee to a nunnery.

1402
01:11:42.620 --> 01:11:44.950
Why wouldst thou be
a breeder of sinners?

1403
01:11:45.580 --> 01:11:48.700
I am myself indifferent honest,
but yet I could accuse me of such things

1404
01:11:48.830 --> 01:11:50.950
that it were better
my mother had not borne me.

1405
01:11:51.750 --> 01:11:54.620
I am very proud,
revengeful, ambitious,

1406
01:11:54.750 --> 01:11:57.950
with more offences at my beck
than I have thoughts to put them in,

1407
01:11:58.080 --> 01:12:01.620
imagination to give them shape,
or time to act them in.

1408
01:12:01.750 --> 01:12:05.370
What should such fellows as I do
crawling between earth and heaven, hm?

1409
01:12:05.500 --> 01:12:06.750
We are arrant knaves.

1410
01:12:08.370 --> 01:12:09.750
All.

1411
01:12:09.870 --> 01:12:11.750
Believe none of us.

1412
01:12:12.370 --> 01:12:14.620
Go thy ways to a nunnery.

1413
01:12:24.370 --> 01:12:26.870
- Where's your father?
- At home, my lord.

1414
01:12:27.000 --> 01:12:30.250
- Where is her father?
- At home, my lord!

1415
01:12:33.250 --> 01:12:35.750
Let the doors be shut upon him,

1416
01:12:35.870 --> 01:12:40.370
that he may play the fool
nowhere but in's own house!

1417
01:12:40.500 --> 01:12:41.830
O help him, you sweet heavens.

1418
01:12:41.950 --> 01:12:45.500
If thou dost marry,
I'll give thee this plague for thy dowry:

1419
01:12:45.620 --> 01:12:48.580
be thou as chaste as ice,
as pure as snow,

1420
01:12:48.700 --> 01:12:50.580
thou shalt not escape calumny.

1421
01:12:50.700 --> 01:12:54.370
Or if thou wilt needs marry,
marry a fool!

1422
01:12:57.250 --> 01:12:59.250
For wise men know well enough

1423
01:12:59.370 --> 01:13:02.500
what monsters you make of them.

1424
01:13:04.330 --> 01:13:08.000
- To a nunnery, go.
- Heavenly powers, restore him!

1425
01:13:08.580 --> 01:13:11.120
I have heard of your paintings
well enough.

1426
01:13:11.250 --> 01:13:14.370
God hath given you one face
and you make yourselves another.

1427
01:13:14.500 --> 01:13:16.500
You jig and amble,

1428
01:13:16.620 --> 01:13:19.500
and you lisp,
you nickname God's creatures,

1429
01:13:19.620 --> 01:13:22.700
and make your wantonness
your ignorance!

1430
01:13:22.830 --> 01:13:25.950
Go to! I'll no more on't!

1431
01:13:26.870 --> 01:13:30.950
It hath made me mad!

1432
01:13:38.500 --> 01:13:41.080
I say we will have no mo marriage.

1433
01:13:42.830 --> 01:13:45.000
Those that are married already,

1434
01:13:45.120 --> 01:13:48.080
all but one shall live.

1435
01:13:51.080 --> 01:13:52.500
The rest shall keep as they are.

1436
01:13:53.500 --> 01:13:55.580
To a nunnery, go.

1437
01:13:58.200 --> 01:14:01.750
O, what a noble mind

1438
01:14:01.870 --> 01:14:04.750
is here o'erthrown.

1439
01:14:04.870 --> 01:14:09.250
The courtier's, soldier's,
scholar's, eye, tongue, sword,

1440
01:14:09.370 --> 01:14:13.580
Th'expectancy and rose
of the fair state,

1441
01:14:13.700 --> 01:14:17.000
The glass of fashion
and the mould of form,

1442
01:14:17.120 --> 01:14:19.750
Th'observed of all observers,

1443
01:14:19.870 --> 01:14:21.870
quite, quite down.

1444
01:14:23.250 --> 01:14:25.080
And I,

1445
01:14:25.200 --> 01:14:28.250
of ladies most deject and wretched,

1446
01:14:28.370 --> 01:14:32.200
That sucked the honey
of his music vows,

1447
01:14:32.330 --> 01:14:36.580
Now see that noble
and most sovereign reason

1448
01:14:36.700 --> 01:14:41.250
Like sweet bells
jangled out of tune and harsh,

1449
01:14:42.450 --> 01:14:46.870
That unmatched form
and feature of blown youth...

1450
01:14:48.000 --> 01:14:51.370
...Blasted with ecstasy.

1451
01:14:52.000 --> 01:14:55.000
O woe is me...

1452
01:14:56.000 --> 01:14:58.870
...T'have seen what I have seen,

1453
01:14:59.450 --> 01:15:01.450
see what I see.

1454
01:15:04.000 --> 01:15:05.000
Love?

1455
01:15:05.500 --> 01:15:08.700
His affections do not that way tend,
Nor what he spake,

1456
01:15:08.830 --> 01:15:11.620
though it lacked form a little,
Was not like madness.

1457
01:15:12.250 --> 01:15:15.700
There's something in his soul
O'er which his melancholy sits on brood,

1458
01:15:15.830 --> 01:15:18.870
And I do fear the hatch and the disclose
Will be some danger.

1459
01:15:19.750 --> 01:15:23.000
Which for to prevent, I have
in quick determination thus set it down:

1460
01:15:23.620 --> 01:15:27.450
he shall with speed to England
For the demand of our neglected tribute.

1461
01:15:27.580 --> 01:15:30.620
Haply the seas and countries different,
With variable objects,

1462
01:15:30.750 --> 01:15:33.120
shall expel
This matter in his heart.

1463
01:15:33.830 --> 01:15:35.700
- What think you on't?
- It shall do well.

1464
01:15:35.830 --> 01:15:38.000
But yet do I believe
The origin and commencement of his grief

1465
01:15:38.120 --> 01:15:40.000
Sprung from neglected love.

1466
01:15:40.120 --> 01:15:43.450
How now, Ophelia? You need not tell us
what Lord Hamlet said, we heard it all.

1467
01:15:45.000 --> 01:15:47.750
My lord, do as you please,
But if you hold it fit, after the play

1468
01:15:47.870 --> 01:15:50.700
Let his queen-mother all alone entreat him
To show his grief,

1469
01:15:50.830 --> 01:15:54.080
let her be round with him,
And I'll be placed, so please you,

1470
01:15:54.200 --> 01:15:56.200
in the ear
Of all their conference.

1471
01:15:56.330 --> 01:15:58.750
If she find him not,
To England send him;

1472
01:15:58.870 --> 01:16:00.830
or confine him where
Your wisdom best shall think.

1473
01:16:00.950 --> 01:16:02.370
It shall be so.

1474
01:16:02.500 --> 01:16:05.370
Madness in great ones
must not unwatched go.

1475
01:16:05.500 --> 01:16:07.580
(Dramatic orchestral music)

1476
01:16:13.120 --> 01:16:14.250
I pray you all,

1477
01:16:14.370 --> 01:16:16.750
there is a play tonight
before the King.

1478
01:16:16.870 --> 01:16:19.250
One scene of it
comes near the circumstance

1479
01:16:19.370 --> 01:16:22.250
Which I have told thee
of my father's death.

1480
01:16:22.370 --> 01:16:25.000
I prithee,
when thou see’st that act afoot,

1481
01:16:25.620 --> 01:16:28.750
Even with the very comment
of thy soul

1482
01:16:28.870 --> 01:16:30.500
Observe my uncle.

1483
01:16:30.620 --> 01:16:32.000
If his occulted guilt

1484
01:16:32.120 --> 01:16:35.120
Do not itself unkennel
in one speech,

1485
01:16:35.250 --> 01:16:37.330
It is a damned ghost
that we have seen,

1486
01:16:37.450 --> 01:16:41.120
And my imaginations are as foul
as Vulcan’s stithy.

1487
01:16:41.250 --> 01:16:44.080
Give him heedful note;

1488
01:16:44.200 --> 01:16:46.620
For I mine eyes
will rivet to his face,

1489
01:16:46.750 --> 01:16:49.330
And, after,
we will all our judgments join

1490
01:16:49.450 --> 01:16:51.120
In censure of his seeming.

1491
01:16:51.620 --> 01:16:52.700
Hm?

1492
01:16:53.830 --> 01:16:55.120
They are coming to the play.

1493
01:16:55.250 --> 01:16:56.250
(Dramatic orchestra)

1494
01:16:56.370 --> 01:16:58.200
(Loud vocal warm-ups)

1495
01:16:59.500 --> 01:17:00.500
(Music stops)

1496
01:17:09.500 --> 01:17:12.620
Speak the speech, I pray you,
as I pronounced it to you,

1497
01:17:12.750 --> 01:17:14.000
trippingly on the tongue.

1498
01:17:14.120 --> 01:17:16.250
But if you mouth it,
as many of your players do,

1499
01:17:16.370 --> 01:17:19.370
I had as lief the town-crier
spoke my lines.

1500
01:17:23.620 --> 01:17:25.870
Nor do not saw the air

1501
01:17:26.000 --> 01:17:28.750
too much with your hand, thus,

1502
01:17:28.870 --> 01:17:31.620
but use all gently;
for in the very torrent, tempest,

1503
01:17:31.750 --> 01:17:33.870
and, as I may say,
whirlwind of your passion,

1504
01:17:34.000 --> 01:17:36.200
you must acquire and beget
a temperance

1505
01:17:36.330 --> 01:17:37.580
that may give it smoothness.

1506
01:17:37.700 --> 01:17:39.750
I warrant your honour.

1507
01:17:41.080 --> 01:17:42.450
Be not too tame neither.

1508
01:17:43.330 --> 01:17:45.200
But let your own discretion
be your tutor.

1509
01:17:45.330 --> 01:17:47.080
Suit the action to the word,
the word to the action.

1510
01:17:48.080 --> 01:17:49.370
With this special observance

1511
01:17:49.500 --> 01:17:52.120
that you o'erstep not
the modesty of nature.

1512
01:17:52.250 --> 01:17:55.120
For anything so o'erdone
is from the purpose of playing,

1513
01:17:55.250 --> 01:17:57.370
whose end,
both at the first and now,

1514
01:17:57.500 --> 01:17:58.870
was and is

1515
01:17:59.000 --> 01:18:02.700
- to hold as 'twere the mirror...
- Up to nature.

1516
01:18:04.120 --> 01:18:05.700
To show virtue her feature,

1517
01:18:05.830 --> 01:18:07.450
scorn her own image,

1518
01:18:07.580 --> 01:18:09.450
and the very age and body
of the time

1519
01:18:09.580 --> 01:18:10.830
his form and pressure.

1520
01:18:12.080 --> 01:18:13.370
Go make you ready.

1521
01:18:16.750 --> 01:18:17.870
Oh! Um...

1522
01:18:18.000 --> 01:18:20.500
- Will you two help to hasten them?
- Ay, my lord.

1523
01:18:21.700 --> 01:18:22.700
Oh.

1524
01:18:22.830 --> 01:18:23.830
Oh!

1525
01:18:23.950 --> 01:18:25.250
(Audience laughs)

1526
01:18:28.870 --> 01:18:30.750
What ho, Horatio.

1527
01:18:33.120 --> 01:18:35.750
Horatio,
thou art e'en as just a friend

1528
01:18:35.870 --> 01:18:38.080
As e'er my conversation
coped withal.

1529
01:18:38.200 --> 01:18:39.200
O my dear lord.

1530
01:18:39.330 --> 01:18:40.620
Nay, do not think I flatter.

1531
01:18:41.250 --> 01:18:43.870
Since my dear soul

1532
01:18:44.000 --> 01:18:47.620
was mistress of her choice,
And could of all distinguish her election,

1533
01:18:47.750 --> 01:18:49.950
Sh'ath sealed thee for herself.

1534
01:18:51.500 --> 01:18:54.830
Give me that friend
That is not passion's slave,

1535
01:18:55.700 --> 01:18:58.080
and I will wear them
In my heart's core,

1536
01:18:58.620 --> 01:19:02.250
ay, in my heart of heart,
As I do thee.

1537
01:19:06.370 --> 01:19:08.120
Something too much of this.

1538
01:19:09.250 --> 01:19:10.870
Mark thou the king, Horatio.

1539
01:19:11.370 --> 01:19:12.370
Observe him well.

1540
01:19:12.500 --> 01:19:14.500
My lord, mine eyes
shall still be on his face

1541
01:19:14.620 --> 01:19:16.870
And note the smallest alteration.

1542
01:19:17.950 --> 01:19:19.700
(Stage manager)
The house is now open.

1543
01:19:19.830 --> 01:19:23.330
- Get you a place. I must be idle.
- Please take your seats.

1544
01:19:23.450 --> 01:19:25.500
How fares our cousin Hamlet?

1545
01:19:25.620 --> 01:19:28.620
Excellent, i'faith,
of the chameleon’s dish.

1546
01:19:28.750 --> 01:19:31.080
I eat the air, promise-crammed.

1547
01:19:31.200 --> 01:19:33.200
You cannot feed capons so.

1548
01:19:33.330 --> 01:19:36.500
I have nothing with this answer, Hamlet.
These words are not mine.

1549
01:19:36.620 --> 01:19:38.000
No, nor mine now.

1550
01:19:40.700 --> 01:19:43.950
My lord, you played once
i'th' university, you say?

1551
01:19:44.080 --> 01:19:48.080
That did I, my lord,
and was accounted a good actor.

1552
01:19:48.200 --> 01:19:49.500
Oh! What did you enact?

1553
01:19:49.620 --> 01:19:51.830
I did enact Julius Caesar.

1554
01:19:51.950 --> 01:19:55.000
I was killed i'th' Capitol.
Brutus killed me.

1555
01:19:58.370 --> 01:20:02.080
"Cowards die many times
before their deaths."

1556
01:20:02.700 --> 01:20:05.120
(Stage manager)
Please take your seats,

1557
01:20:05.250 --> 01:20:07.750
this evening’s performance
is about to begin.

1558
01:20:07.870 --> 01:20:09.000
Be the players ready?

1559
01:20:09.120 --> 01:20:11.000
Ay, my lord,
they stay upon your patience.

1560
01:20:11.120 --> 01:20:13.200
Come hither,
my dear Hamlet, sit by me.

1561
01:20:13.330 --> 01:20:14.950
No, good mother,

1562
01:20:15.080 --> 01:20:17.500
here's metal more attractive.

1563
01:20:19.500 --> 01:20:20.500
Lady.

1564
01:20:22.750 --> 01:20:25.250
- Shall I lie in your lap?
- No, my lord.

1565
01:20:25.370 --> 01:20:27.700
- I mean, my head upon your lap.
- Ay, my lord.

1566
01:20:27.830 --> 01:20:29.330
Do you think I meant
country matters?

1567
01:20:29.450 --> 01:20:31.580
I think nothing, my lord.

1568
01:20:31.700 --> 01:20:33.620
That's a fair thought
to lie between maids' legs.

1569
01:20:33.750 --> 01:20:35.000
What is, my lord?

1570
01:20:35.120 --> 01:20:37.080
- Nothing.
- (Laughs)

1571
01:20:37.200 --> 01:20:38.620
You are merry, my lord.

1572
01:20:39.500 --> 01:20:41.330
- Who, I?
- Ay, my lord.

1573
01:20:41.450 --> 01:20:43.500
What should a man do but be merry?

1574
01:20:45.080 --> 01:20:47.250
For look you
how cheerfully my mother looks

1575
01:20:47.370 --> 01:20:49.120
and my father died
within's two hours.

1576
01:20:50.500 --> 01:20:53.080
Nay, 'tis twice two months, my lord.

1577
01:20:53.200 --> 01:20:54.450
So long?

1578
01:20:54.580 --> 01:20:57.830
O heavens, die two months ago
and not forgotten yet.

1579
01:20:57.950 --> 01:21:00.250
- What means this, my lord?
- (Hamlet) Mischief.

1580
01:21:00.370 --> 01:21:02.870
(Ophelia) Belike this imports
the argument of the play.

1581
01:21:03.750 --> 01:21:06.120
(Hamlet) We shall know
by these fellows.

1582
01:21:06.250 --> 01:21:08.000
The players cannot keep counsel:

1583
01:21:08.120 --> 01:21:09.750
they’ll tell all.

1584
01:21:09.870 --> 01:21:11.750
(Deep, suspenseful music playing)

1585
01:21:18.000 --> 01:21:20.250
For us and for our tragedy,

1586
01:21:20.370 --> 01:21:24.000
Here stooping to your clemency,
We beg your hearing...

1587
01:21:24.120 --> 01:21:25.120
...patiently.

1588
01:21:25.250 --> 01:21:27.750
Is this a prologue,
or the posy of a ring?

1589
01:21:27.870 --> 01:21:30.580
- 'Tis brief, my lord.
- As woman's love.

1590
01:21:34.750 --> 01:21:38.000
Full thirty times
hath Phoebus' cart gone round

1591
01:21:38.120 --> 01:21:41.000
Neptune's salt wash
and Tellus' orbed ground,

1592
01:21:41.120 --> 01:21:43.700
Since love our hearts
and Hymen did our hands

1593
01:21:44.370 --> 01:21:47.000
Unite commutual
in most sacred bands.

1594
01:21:47.620 --> 01:21:52.120
So many journeys may the sun and moon
Make us again count o'er

1595
01:21:52.250 --> 01:21:54.250
ere love be done.

1596
01:21:55.620 --> 01:21:57.500
But woe is me,

1597
01:21:57.620 --> 01:22:00.120
you are so sick of late,

1598
01:22:00.750 --> 01:22:03.500
So far from cheer
and from your former state,

1599
01:22:03.620 --> 01:22:05.250
That I distrust you.

1600
01:22:06.000 --> 01:22:07.620
Yet though I distrust,

1601
01:22:07.750 --> 01:22:10.450
Discomfort you, my lord,
it nothing must;

1602
01:22:11.080 --> 01:22:13.750
For women's fear
and love hold quantity,

1603
01:22:13.870 --> 01:22:16.000
In neither aught,

1604
01:22:16.120 --> 01:22:18.200
or in extremity.

1605
01:22:18.330 --> 01:22:20.330
Faith, I must leave thee, love,

1606
01:22:20.450 --> 01:22:21.870
and shortly too.

1607
01:22:22.000 --> 01:22:25.200
My operant powers
their functions leave to do.

1608
01:22:25.330 --> 01:22:28.450
And thou shalt live
in this fair world behind,

1609
01:22:28.580 --> 01:22:32.370
Honoured, beloved;
and haply one as kind

1610
01:22:32.500 --> 01:22:33.950
For husband shalt thou...

1611
01:22:34.080 --> 01:22:36.370
O confound the rest!

1612
01:22:36.500 --> 01:22:40.370
Such love must needs be treason
in my breast.

1613
01:22:41.120 --> 01:22:44.370
In second husband let me be accurst.

1614
01:22:44.500 --> 01:22:48.330
None wed the second
but who killed the first.

1615
01:22:48.450 --> 01:22:49.950
(Hamlet) That's wormwood!

1616
01:22:50.080 --> 01:22:52.700
The instances
that second marriage move

1617
01:22:52.830 --> 01:22:56.370
Are base respects of...thrift,

1618
01:22:56.500 --> 01:22:58.370
but none of love.

1619
01:22:58.500 --> 01:23:01.450
A second time
I kill my husband dead,

1620
01:23:01.580 --> 01:23:04.500
When second husband
kisses me in bed.

1621
01:23:04.620 --> 01:23:06.750
I do believe
you think what now you speak,

1622
01:23:07.450 --> 01:23:10.250
But what we do determine,
oft we break.

1623
01:23:10.370 --> 01:23:13.620
This world is not for ever;
'tis not strange

1624
01:23:13.750 --> 01:23:16.830
That even our loves
should with our fortunes change.

1625
01:23:17.750 --> 01:23:21.120
So think thou wilt
no second husband wed,

1626
01:23:21.250 --> 01:23:23.120
But die thy thoughts

1627
01:23:23.250 --> 01:23:25.450
when thy first lord is dead.

1628
01:23:26.950 --> 01:23:29.620
Nor earth to me give food,

1629
01:23:29.750 --> 01:23:31.750
nor heaven light,

1630
01:23:31.870 --> 01:23:35.830
Sport and repose
lock from me day and night,

1631
01:23:35.950 --> 01:23:39.870
To desperation
turn my trust and hope,

1632
01:23:40.450 --> 01:23:43.830
A hermit’s cheer in prison
be my scope.

1633
01:23:44.370 --> 01:23:47.250
Both here and hence
pursue me lasting strife,

1634
01:23:47.370 --> 01:23:49.500
If, once a widow,

1635
01:23:49.620 --> 01:23:51.370
ever I be wife.

1636
01:23:51.500 --> 01:23:53.080
If she should break it now.

1637
01:23:53.200 --> 01:23:54.620
(Player King) 'Tis deeply sworn.

1638
01:23:54.750 --> 01:23:57.370
Sweet, leave me here awhile.

1639
01:23:58.120 --> 01:24:01.080
My spirits grow dull,
and fain I would beguile

1640
01:24:01.700 --> 01:24:04.120
The tedious day with sleep.

1641
01:24:04.750 --> 01:24:07.370
Sleep rock thy brain,

1642
01:24:07.870 --> 01:24:12.250
And never come mischance
between us twain.

1643
01:24:12.870 --> 01:24:16.500
(Hamlet) Madam,
how like you this play?

1644
01:24:17.950 --> 01:24:19.120
(Audience laughs)

1645
01:24:19.250 --> 01:24:21.750
The lady doth protest too much,
methinks.

1646
01:24:21.870 --> 01:24:24.500
O, but she'll keep her word.

1647
01:24:24.620 --> 01:24:26.580
Have you heard the argument?

1648
01:24:27.250 --> 01:24:29.870
- Is there no offence in't?
- No, no.

1649
01:24:30.000 --> 01:24:32.620
They do but jest, poison in jest.

1650
01:24:32.750 --> 01:24:34.200
No offence i'th' world.

1651
01:24:34.700 --> 01:24:35.870
What do you call the play?

1652
01:24:36.000 --> 01:24:38.120
The Mousetrap.

1653
01:24:38.700 --> 01:24:41.580
'Tis a knavish piece of work,
but what o' that?

1654
01:24:41.700 --> 01:24:44.000
Your Majesty,
and we that have free souls,

1655
01:24:44.120 --> 01:24:45.580
it touches us not.

1656
01:24:45.700 --> 01:24:47.870
This is one Lucianus,
nephew to the King.

1657
01:24:48.000 --> 01:24:50.120
You are as good as a chorus,
my lord!

1658
01:24:50.250 --> 01:24:51.950
Sh! Begin, murderer.

1659
01:24:55.370 --> 01:24:57.450
Thoughts black.

1660
01:24:58.500 --> 01:25:00.580
Hands apt.

1661
01:25:00.700 --> 01:25:02.120
Drugs fit.

1662
01:25:02.250 --> 01:25:05.000
And time agreeing.

1663
01:25:05.120 --> 01:25:07.080
Confederate season,

1664
01:25:07.200 --> 01:25:10.620
else no creature seeing...

1665
01:25:12.250 --> 01:25:15.500
...Thou mixture rank,

1666
01:25:16.200 --> 01:25:19.250
of midnight weeds collected,

1667
01:25:19.370 --> 01:25:23.120
With Hecate's ban thrice blasted,

1668
01:25:23.250 --> 01:25:25.500
thrice infected!

1669
01:25:26.250 --> 01:25:28.120
Thy natural magic

1670
01:25:28.250 --> 01:25:30.620
and dire property

1671
01:25:31.620 --> 01:25:33.580
On wholesome life

1672
01:25:33.700 --> 01:25:37.080
usurps immediately.

1673
01:25:37.200 --> 01:25:40.000
(Hamlet) He poisons him
i'th' garden for his estate!

1674
01:25:40.120 --> 01:25:41.500
His name's Gonzago!

1675
01:25:41.620 --> 01:25:45.620
You shall see anon how the murderer
gets the love of Gonzago's wife!

1676
01:25:45.750 --> 01:25:48.750
(Ophelia) The King rises!
(Hamlet) What, frighted with false fire?

1677
01:25:48.870 --> 01:25:51.370
- How fares my lord?
- (Polonius) Give o'er the play!

1678
01:25:52.620 --> 01:25:55.120
Give me some light. Away.
Lights, lights, lights.

1679
01:25:56.580 --> 01:25:57.950
O good Horatio!

1680
01:25:58.080 --> 01:25:59.620
(Upbeat electronic music)

1681
01:25:59.750 --> 01:26:02.870
I'll take the ghost's word
for a thousand pound!

1682
01:26:03.000 --> 01:26:05.120
- Didst perceive?
- Very well, my lord!

1683
01:26:05.250 --> 01:26:08.750
- Upon the talk of the poisoning?
- I did very well note him!

1684
01:26:09.950 --> 01:26:13.250
Good my lord,
vouchsafe me a word with you!

1685
01:26:13.370 --> 01:26:14.750
(Hamlet) Sir, a whole history!

1686
01:26:14.870 --> 01:26:16.950
- The King, sir...
- (Hamlet) Ay, sir, what of him?

1687
01:26:17.080 --> 01:26:19.450
Is in his retirement
marvellous distempered.

1688
01:26:19.580 --> 01:26:20.580
With drink, sir?

1689
01:26:20.700 --> 01:26:23.370
No, my lord, with choler!
Good my lord!

1690
01:26:23.500 --> 01:26:25.870
- Pronounce!
- The Queen your mother,

1691
01:26:26.000 --> 01:26:28.750
in most great affliction of spirit,
hath sent me to you.

1692
01:26:28.870 --> 01:26:29.870
You are welcome.

1693
01:26:30.000 --> 01:26:32.750
She says your behaviour hath struck her
into amazement and admiration.

1694
01:26:32.870 --> 01:26:35.500
O wonderful son,
that can so stonish a mother!

1695
01:26:35.620 --> 01:26:38.000
She desires to speak with you
ere you go to bed.

1696
01:26:38.870 --> 01:26:40.120
We shall obey.

1697
01:26:41.450 --> 01:26:43.330
Were she ten times our mother.

1698
01:26:44.370 --> 01:26:46.120
Have you any further trade with us?

1699
01:26:46.250 --> 01:26:48.120
My lord, you once did love me.

1700
01:26:48.250 --> 01:26:49.580
And do still,

1701
01:26:49.700 --> 01:26:52.000
by these pickers and stealers.

1702
01:26:52.120 --> 01:26:55.330
Good my lord,
what is your cause of distemper?

1703
01:26:55.450 --> 01:26:58.080
You do surely bar the door
upon your own liberty

1704
01:26:58.200 --> 01:27:00.000
if you deny your griefs
to your friend.

1705
01:27:00.120 --> 01:27:01.450
Sir, I lack advancement.

1706
01:27:01.580 --> 01:27:02.750
How can that be,

1707
01:27:02.870 --> 01:27:04.830
when you have the voice
of the King himself

1708
01:27:04.950 --> 01:27:06.500
for your succession in Denmark?

1709
01:27:06.620 --> 01:27:07.870
(Recorder whistles)

1710
01:27:08.000 --> 01:27:09.000
(Audience laughs)

1711
01:27:09.120 --> 01:27:11.370
O, the recorders.
Let me see one.

1712
01:27:15.250 --> 01:27:16.620
Will you play upon this pipe?

1713
01:27:16.750 --> 01:27:18.200
My lord, I cannot.

1714
01:27:18.330 --> 01:27:20.330
- I pray you.
- Believe me, I cannot!

1715
01:27:20.450 --> 01:27:23.750
- I do beseech you.
- I know no touch of it, my lord.

1716
01:27:23.870 --> 01:27:25.200
It is as easy as lying.

1717
01:27:25.330 --> 01:27:27.580
Govern these ventages
with your fingers and thumb,

1718
01:27:27.700 --> 01:27:29.120
give it breath with your mouth,

1719
01:27:29.250 --> 01:27:31.870
and it will discourse
most eloquent music.

1720
01:27:32.000 --> 01:27:33.120
Look you, these are the stops.

1721
01:27:33.250 --> 01:27:35.870
But these cannot I command
to any utterance of harmony!

1722
01:27:36.000 --> 01:27:37.700
I have not the skill!

1723
01:27:40.870 --> 01:27:42.120
Why, look you now.

1724
01:27:43.500 --> 01:27:45.750
How unworthy a thing you make of me.

1725
01:27:47.620 --> 01:27:49.000
You would play upon me.

1726
01:27:50.620 --> 01:27:52.750
You would seem to know my stops.

1727
01:27:53.370 --> 01:27:55.870
You would pluck out
the heart of my mystery.

1728
01:27:56.700 --> 01:27:59.620
You would sound me
from my lowest note

1729
01:27:59.750 --> 01:28:01.620
to the top of my compass!

1730
01:28:01.750 --> 01:28:03.950
And there is much music,

1731
01:28:04.580 --> 01:28:07.450
excellent voice, in this little organ,

1732
01:28:07.580 --> 01:28:09.500
yet cannot you make it speak.

1733
01:28:12.250 --> 01:28:13.250
'Sblood...

1734
01:28:15.580 --> 01:28:17.000
...do you think

1735
01:28:17.830 --> 01:28:20.250
I am easier to be played on

1736
01:28:20.370 --> 01:28:22.370
than a pipe?

1737
01:28:25.120 --> 01:28:27.450
Call me what instrument you will,

1738
01:28:27.580 --> 01:28:29.200
though you fret me,

1739
01:28:29.330 --> 01:28:31.200
you cannot play upon me.

1740
01:28:33.450 --> 01:28:34.620
God bless you, sir.

1741
01:28:34.750 --> 01:28:37.370
My lord, the Queen would speak
with you, and presently.

1742
01:28:47.120 --> 01:28:50.500
Do you see yonder cloud
that's almost in shape of a camel?

1743
01:28:53.250 --> 01:28:55.870
By th' mass
and 'tis-like a camel indeed.

1744
01:28:56.000 --> 01:28:57.700
Methinks it is like a weasel.

1745
01:28:58.870 --> 01:29:00.580
It is backed like a weasel.

1746
01:29:00.700 --> 01:29:03.250
- Or like a whale.
- Very like a whale.

1747
01:29:05.700 --> 01:29:07.080
They fool me...

1748
01:29:08.080 --> 01:29:10.330
...to the top of my bent.

1749
01:29:17.870 --> 01:29:20.250
Then I will speak with my mother
by and by.

1750
01:29:20.370 --> 01:29:21.500
I will say so.

1751
01:29:21.620 --> 01:29:23.120
"By and by"

1752
01:29:23.870 --> 01:29:25.250
is easily said.

1753
01:29:26.120 --> 01:29:27.250
Now to my mother.

1754
01:29:28.120 --> 01:29:30.370
O heart, lose not thy nature.

1755
01:29:30.500 --> 01:29:33.120
Let me be cruel, not unnatural.

1756
01:29:34.450 --> 01:29:37.580
I will speak daggers to her,
but use none.

1757
01:29:37.700 --> 01:29:39.620
(Deep string music)

1758
01:29:40.250 --> 01:29:41.870
(Guard, clapping) Leave us!

1759
01:29:42.830 --> 01:29:46.000
Stand not upon the order
of your going but go at once!

1760
01:29:46.120 --> 01:29:47.250
(Claudius) Guildenstern.

1761
01:29:48.870 --> 01:29:49.870
I like him not,

1762
01:29:50.000 --> 01:29:52.500
nor stands it safe with us
To let his madness range.

1763
01:29:52.620 --> 01:29:54.200
Therefore prepare you.

1764
01:29:54.330 --> 01:29:58.000
I your commission will forthwith dispatch,
And he to England shall along with you.

1765
01:29:58.120 --> 01:30:00.870
Arm you, I pray you,
to this speedy voyage,

1766
01:30:01.000 --> 01:30:04.700
For we will fetters put about this fear
Which now goes too free-footed.

1767
01:30:04.830 --> 01:30:05.620
We will haste us.

1768
01:30:05.750 --> 01:30:07.330
My lord, the Queen
would speak with him tonight.

1769
01:30:07.450 --> 01:30:09.000
Behind the arras I'll convey myself.

1770
01:30:09.120 --> 01:30:11.000
'Tis meet that some more audience
than a mother,

1771
01:30:11.120 --> 01:30:12.700
Since nature makes them partial,

1772
01:30:12.830 --> 01:30:14.700
should o'erhear
The speech of vantage.

1773
01:30:15.870 --> 01:30:17.000
Fare you well, my liege.

1774
01:30:17.120 --> 01:30:20.870
I'll call upon you ere you go to bed,
And tell you what I know.

1775
01:30:21.000 --> 01:30:22.620
Thanks, dear my lord.

1776
01:30:25.000 --> 01:30:26.870
(Gentle instrumental music)

1777
01:30:49.620 --> 01:30:51.120
O, my offence is rank.

1778
01:30:52.000 --> 01:30:53.250
It smells to heaven.

1779
01:30:54.620 --> 01:30:58.500
It hath the primal eldest curse upon't,
A brother's murder.

1780
01:31:01.450 --> 01:31:04.700
Pray can I not,
Though inclination be as sharp as will.

1781
01:31:04.830 --> 01:31:07.120
My stronger guilt
defeats my strong intent,

1782
01:31:07.250 --> 01:31:09.120
And, like a man
to double business bound,

1783
01:31:09.250 --> 01:31:12.700
I stand in pause where I shall first begin,
And both neglect.

1784
01:31:20.620 --> 01:31:23.870
What if this cursed hand

1785
01:31:24.000 --> 01:31:26.620
Were thicker than itself
with brother's blood?

1786
01:31:27.500 --> 01:31:29.080
Is there not rain enough
in the sweet heavens

1787
01:31:29.200 --> 01:31:30.870
To wash it white as snow?

1788
01:31:31.830 --> 01:31:34.450
Whereto serves mercy
But to confront the visage of offence?

1789
01:31:35.370 --> 01:31:37.370
And what's in prayer
but this twofold force,

1790
01:31:37.500 --> 01:31:41.200
To be forestalled ere we come to fall
Or pardoned being down?

1791
01:31:43.120 --> 01:31:44.120
Then I'll look up.

1792
01:31:46.120 --> 01:31:47.370
My fault is past.

1793
01:31:48.250 --> 01:31:49.950
But O, what form of prayer
Can serve my turn?

1794
01:31:50.080 --> 01:31:53.750
"Forgive me my foul murder?"
That cannot be, since I am still possessed

1795
01:31:53.870 --> 01:31:55.950
Of those effects
for which I did the murder,

1796
01:31:56.080 --> 01:31:58.080
My crown, mine own ambition,
and my queen.

1797
01:32:01.120 --> 01:32:03.500
May one be pardoned
and retain th'offence?

1798
01:32:05.830 --> 01:32:07.870
In the corrupted currents
of this world,

1799
01:32:08.000 --> 01:32:10.750
Offence's gilded hand
may shove by justice,

1800
01:32:10.870 --> 01:32:13.750
And oft 'tis seen the wicked prize itself
Buys out the law.

1801
01:32:13.870 --> 01:32:16.870
But 'tis not so above:
There is no shuffling there.

1802
01:32:18.370 --> 01:32:19.370
What then? What rests?

1803
01:32:20.620 --> 01:32:22.500
Try what repentance can.
What can it not?

1804
01:32:22.620 --> 01:32:25.250
Yet what can it,
when one cannot repent?

1805
01:32:27.200 --> 01:32:29.120
O wretched state.

1806
01:32:30.370 --> 01:32:32.830
O bosom black as death.

1807
01:32:33.620 --> 01:32:38.250
O limed soul, that struggling to be free
Art more engaged!

1808
01:32:38.370 --> 01:32:41.000
Help, angels. Make assay.

1809
01:32:45.330 --> 01:32:47.330
Bow, stubborn knees.

1810
01:32:48.580 --> 01:32:50.370
And heart with strings of steel,

1811
01:32:50.500 --> 01:32:53.580
Be soft as sinews
of the new-born babe.

1812
01:32:56.750 --> 01:32:58.080
All may be well.

1813
01:33:02.950 --> 01:33:03.950
(Hamlet) 'Tis now...

1814
01:33:04.950 --> 01:33:08.950
...the very witching time of night,
When churchyards yawn

1815
01:33:09.080 --> 01:33:12.500
and hell itself breathes out
Contagion to this world.

1816
01:33:12.620 --> 01:33:16.200
Now could I drink hot blood,

1817
01:33:16.330 --> 01:33:21.000
And do such bitter business as the day
Would quake to look on.

1818
01:33:29.870 --> 01:33:31.080
Now might I do it.

1819
01:33:33.370 --> 01:33:34.370
Pat.

1820
01:33:35.120 --> 01:33:36.580
Now he is a-praying.

1821
01:33:40.870 --> 01:33:42.330
And now I'll do't.

1822
01:33:43.500 --> 01:33:44.500
(Gun clicks)

1823
01:33:46.950 --> 01:33:48.500
And so he goes to heaven?

1824
01:33:49.200 --> 01:33:51.750
And so am I revenged?
That would be scanned.

1825
01:33:51.870 --> 01:33:53.620
To take him
in the purging of his soul,

1826
01:33:53.750 --> 01:33:55.750
When he is fit and seasoned
for his passage?

1827
01:33:55.870 --> 01:33:58.370
A villain kills my father,
and for that I, his sole son,

1828
01:33:58.500 --> 01:34:00.750
do this same villain send
To heaven? No.

1829
01:34:00.870 --> 01:34:03.870
Up, sword,
and know thou a more horrid hent.

1830
01:34:04.000 --> 01:34:07.120
When he is drunk asleep,
or in his rage,

1831
01:34:07.250 --> 01:34:09.580
or in th'incestuous pleasure
of his bed,

1832
01:34:09.700 --> 01:34:11.500
At game a-swearing,

1833
01:34:12.250 --> 01:34:16.120
or about some act
That has no relish of salvation in't,

1834
01:34:16.700 --> 01:34:18.000
Then trip him,

1835
01:34:18.120 --> 01:34:20.120
that his heels may kick at heaven

1836
01:34:20.250 --> 01:34:22.250
And that his soul may be
as damned and black

1837
01:34:22.370 --> 01:34:23.830
As hell, whereto it goes.

1838
01:34:25.580 --> 01:34:27.370
My mother stays.

1839
01:34:28.250 --> 01:34:29.750
This physic

1840
01:34:30.250 --> 01:34:32.450
but prolongs thy sickly days.

1841
01:34:32.580 --> 01:34:34.080
My words fly up.

1842
01:34:35.200 --> 01:34:37.000
My thoughts remain below.

1843
01:34:39.200 --> 01:34:41.000
Words without thoughts...

1844
01:34:43.000 --> 01:34:44.620
...never to heaven go.

1845
01:34:44.750 --> 01:34:46.700
(Deep orchestral music)

1846
01:34:56.830 --> 01:34:58.620
(Music intensifies)

1847
01:35:04.370 --> 01:35:06.120
(Audience applauding)

1848
01:35:16.870 --> 01:35:18.500
(Audience chatting)

1849
01:35:20.620 --> 01:35:22.250
(Overlapping chatter)

1850
01:35:33.700 --> 01:35:35.250
(Overlapping chatter)

1851
01:35:37.120 --> 01:35:39.080
(Orchestra starts playing)

1852
01:35:44.000 --> 01:35:46.870
(Polonius) He will come straight.
Look you lay home to him.

1853
01:35:47.000 --> 01:35:49.080
Tell him your Grace hath screen’d
and stood between

1854
01:35:49.200 --> 01:35:50.250
Much heat and him.

1855
01:35:50.370 --> 01:35:53.250
I’ll war’nt you, fear me not.
Withdraw, I hear him coming.

1856
01:35:58.370 --> 01:36:01.200
Now mother, what's the matter?

1857
01:36:01.330 --> 01:36:04.580
Hamlet, thou hast thy father
much offended.

1858
01:36:04.700 --> 01:36:07.870
Mother, you have my father
much offended.

1859
01:36:08.000 --> 01:36:10.120
Come, come,
you answer with an idle tongue.

1860
01:36:10.250 --> 01:36:12.250
Go, go, you question
with a wicked tongue.

1861
01:36:12.370 --> 01:36:13.870
- Why, how now?
- What's the matter?

1862
01:36:14.000 --> 01:36:16.370
- Have you forgot me?
- No, by the rood, not so.

1863
01:36:17.120 --> 01:36:18.250
You are the Queen,

1864
01:36:18.370 --> 01:36:20.500
your husband's brother's wife,

1865
01:36:20.620 --> 01:36:23.620
And, would it were not so,
you are my mother.

1866
01:36:23.750 --> 01:36:26.500
Nay, then I'll set those to you
that can speak.

1867
01:36:26.620 --> 01:36:29.830
Come, come, and sit you down,
you shall not budge.

1868
01:36:29.950 --> 01:36:31.950
You go not till I set you up a glass

1869
01:36:32.080 --> 01:36:33.870
Where you may see
the inmost part of you.

1870
01:36:34.000 --> 01:36:36.120
What wilt thou do?
Thou wilt not murder me?

1871
01:36:36.250 --> 01:36:38.370
- Help, ho!
- (Polonius) What ho! Help!

1872
01:36:38.500 --> 01:36:40.870
- How now? A rat!
- (Gunshots)

1873
01:36:42.950 --> 01:36:45.370
- O me, what hast thou done?
- Nay, I know not.

1874
01:36:46.250 --> 01:36:47.750
Is it the King?

1875
01:36:47.870 --> 01:36:51.120
Hamlet these pranks
have been too broad to bear with...

1876
01:36:57.500 --> 01:36:58.870
(Gertrude) No.

1877
01:36:59.000 --> 01:37:00.500
(Polonius) No.

1878
01:37:05.330 --> 01:37:08.620
O what a rash and bloody deed
is this!

1879
01:37:08.750 --> 01:37:10.250
(Hamlet) A bloody deed!

1880
01:37:10.370 --> 01:37:13.000
Almost as bad, good mother,
As kill a king and marry with his brother!

1881
01:37:13.120 --> 01:37:15.370
- As kill a king?
- Ay, lady, it was my word.

1882
01:37:15.500 --> 01:37:18.620
Thou wretched, rash,
intruding fool, farewell.

1883
01:37:19.500 --> 01:37:21.620
I took thee for thy better.

1884
01:37:23.370 --> 01:37:24.620
Take thy fortune.

1885
01:37:24.750 --> 01:37:28.370
Thou find'st to be too busy
is some danger.

1886
01:37:30.580 --> 01:37:31.620
(Groans)

1887
01:37:33.450 --> 01:37:34.950
(Groaning and crying)

1888
01:37:46.750 --> 01:37:49.080
(Gertrude) No, no! No! No!

1889
01:37:50.330 --> 01:37:51.620
No, no.

1890
01:37:53.750 --> 01:37:55.330
Leave wringing of your hands.

1891
01:37:56.000 --> 01:37:59.250
Peace, sit you down,
And let me wring your heart;

1892
01:37:59.370 --> 01:38:02.700
for so I shall
If it be made of penetrable stuff.

1893
01:38:02.830 --> 01:38:05.370
What have I done,
that thou dar'st wag thy tongue

1894
01:38:05.500 --> 01:38:06.870
In noise so rude against me?

1895
01:38:07.000 --> 01:38:10.000
Such an act
That blurs the grace and blush of modesty,

1896
01:38:10.120 --> 01:38:11.620
Calls virtue hypocrite,

1897
01:38:11.750 --> 01:38:14.620
makes marriage vows
As false as dicers' oaths.

1898
01:38:14.750 --> 01:38:16.330
Ay me! What act?

1899
01:38:20.620 --> 01:38:22.080
(Gertrude groans)

1900
01:38:22.200 --> 01:38:24.620
Look here upon this picture.

1901
01:38:25.330 --> 01:38:26.370
And on this.

1902
01:38:26.500 --> 01:38:28.500
The presentment of two brothers.

1903
01:38:28.620 --> 01:38:30.500
See what a grace was seated
on this brow.

1904
01:38:31.080 --> 01:38:32.750
This was your husband.

1905
01:38:32.870 --> 01:38:36.250
Look you now what follows.
Here is your husband.

1906
01:38:36.370 --> 01:38:37.500
Have you eyes?

1907
01:38:38.000 --> 01:38:40.370
Could you on this fair mountain
leave to feed

1908
01:38:40.500 --> 01:38:42.750
And batten on this moor?

1909
01:38:42.870 --> 01:38:43.870
Have you eyes?

1910
01:38:44.500 --> 01:38:46.870
You cannot call it love;
for at your age

1911
01:38:47.000 --> 01:38:49.000
The heyday in the blood is tame,
it's humble,

1912
01:38:49.120 --> 01:38:50.620
And waits upon the judgment,

1913
01:38:50.750 --> 01:38:54.750
and what judgment
Would step from this to this?

1914
01:38:54.870 --> 01:38:56.250
O Hamlet, speak no more.

1915
01:38:56.750 --> 01:38:58.870
Thou turn'st my eyes
into my very soul,

1916
01:38:59.000 --> 01:39:01.700
And there I see
such black and grained spots

1917
01:39:01.830 --> 01:39:03.620
As will not leave their tinct.

1918
01:39:03.750 --> 01:39:07.000
Nay, but to live
In the rank sweat of an enseamed bed,

1919
01:39:07.120 --> 01:39:08.500
Stewed in corruption,

1920
01:39:08.620 --> 01:39:11.950
honeying and making love
Over the nasty sty.

1921
01:39:12.080 --> 01:39:14.750
O speak to me no more!
These words like daggers enter in my ears!

1922
01:39:14.870 --> 01:39:15.870
No more, sweet Hamlet.

1923
01:39:16.000 --> 01:39:19.200
A murderer...and a villain.

1924
01:39:20.370 --> 01:39:23.870
A slave that is not twentieth part
the tithe

1925
01:39:24.000 --> 01:39:25.450
of your precedent lord.

1926
01:39:26.370 --> 01:39:28.950
A cutpurse of the empire
and the rule.

1927
01:39:29.080 --> 01:39:30.080
No more!

1928
01:39:30.200 --> 01:39:32.120
A king of shreds and patches...

1929
01:39:32.250 --> 01:39:33.950
(Eerie music)

1930
01:39:34.870 --> 01:39:36.700
What would your gracious figure?

1931
01:39:41.500 --> 01:39:42.500
Alas.

1932
01:39:43.250 --> 01:39:44.250
He's mad.

1933
01:39:45.080 --> 01:39:47.580
Do you not come your tardy son
to chide,

1934
01:39:47.700 --> 01:39:50.500
That, lapsed in time and passion,
lets go by

1935
01:39:50.620 --> 01:39:53.200
Th'important acting
of your dread command?

1936
01:39:54.830 --> 01:39:55.830
O say.

1937
01:39:56.500 --> 01:39:58.000
(Eerie music, whispers)

1938
01:40:02.750 --> 01:40:04.120
(Clock chiming)

1939
01:40:13.080 --> 01:40:14.620
How is it with you, lady?

1940
01:40:15.750 --> 01:40:18.120
Alas, how is't with you,

1941
01:40:18.950 --> 01:40:21.580
That you do bend your eye
on vacancy,

1942
01:40:21.700 --> 01:40:24.200
And with th'incorporal air
do hold discourse?

1943
01:40:24.830 --> 01:40:25.870
O gentle son,

1944
01:40:26.580 --> 01:40:30.000
Upon the heat and flame
of thy distemper

1945
01:40:30.620 --> 01:40:32.370
Sprinkle cool patience.

1946
01:40:33.370 --> 01:40:34.450
Whereon do you look?

1947
01:40:35.370 --> 01:40:38.000
On him, on him.

1948
01:40:38.120 --> 01:40:39.950
Look you how pale he glares.

1949
01:40:40.080 --> 01:40:41.750
His form and cause conjoined,

1950
01:40:41.870 --> 01:40:44.620
preaching to stones,
Would make them capable.

1951
01:40:44.750 --> 01:40:46.500
Do not look upon me,

1952
01:40:47.080 --> 01:40:50.450
Lest with this piteous action you convert
My stern effects.

1953
01:40:50.580 --> 01:40:53.370
Then what I have to do
Will want true colour:

1954
01:40:53.500 --> 01:40:55.370
tears perchance for blood.

1955
01:40:55.500 --> 01:40:56.950
To whom do you speak this?

1956
01:40:58.000 --> 01:40:59.330
Do you see nothing there?

1957
01:40:59.450 --> 01:41:02.580
Nothing at all;
yet all that is I see.

1958
01:41:08.750 --> 01:41:10.370
Nor did you nothing hear?

1959
01:41:10.500 --> 01:41:12.750
No, nothing but ourselves.

1960
01:41:16.200 --> 01:41:18.330
Why, look you there,
look how it steals away!

1961
01:41:18.450 --> 01:41:22.370
My father, in his habit as he lived.

1962
01:41:23.200 --> 01:41:25.620
This is the very coinage
of your brain.

1963
01:41:25.750 --> 01:41:29.200
This bodiless creation ecstasy
Is very cunning in.

1964
01:41:29.330 --> 01:41:33.080
It is not madness that I have uttered.
Mother, for love of grace,

1965
01:41:33.200 --> 01:41:35.950
Lay not that flattering unction
to your soul,

1966
01:41:36.080 --> 01:41:38.330
That not your trespass
but my madness speaks.

1967
01:41:40.000 --> 01:41:41.580
Forgive me this.
Confess yourself to heaven.

1968
01:41:41.700 --> 01:41:44.370
Repent what's past,
avoid what is to come.

1969
01:41:44.500 --> 01:41:48.250
O Hamlet, thou hast cleft my heart
in twain!

1970
01:41:50.200 --> 01:41:52.500
O throw away the worser part of it

1971
01:41:52.620 --> 01:41:54.700
And live the purer
with the other half.

1972
01:41:57.120 --> 01:41:58.120
Mm.

1973
01:41:59.370 --> 01:42:00.370
Good night.

1974
01:42:00.950 --> 01:42:03.000
But go not to my uncle's bed.

1975
01:42:03.120 --> 01:42:05.620
Assume a virtue if you have it not.

1976
01:42:06.200 --> 01:42:07.200
Refrain tonight,

1977
01:42:07.330 --> 01:42:10.250
And that shall lend a kind of easiness
To the next abstinence.

1978
01:42:11.700 --> 01:42:13.750
Once more, good night,
For this same lord I do repent;

1979
01:42:13.870 --> 01:42:16.200
but heaven hath pleased it so,

1980
01:42:16.330 --> 01:42:18.500
To punish me with this
and this with me.

1981
01:42:19.080 --> 01:42:20.250
I will bestow him,

1982
01:42:20.370 --> 01:42:22.950
and will answer well
The death I gave him.

1983
01:42:24.250 --> 01:42:25.620
So, again, good night.

1984
01:42:26.620 --> 01:42:28.120
I must be cruel...

1985
01:42:29.120 --> 01:42:30.620
...only to be kind.

1986
01:42:31.500 --> 01:42:34.500
Thus bad begins,
and worse remains behind.

1987
01:42:36.370 --> 01:42:38.120
- One word more, good lady.
- What shall I do?

1988
01:42:38.250 --> 01:42:41.370
Not this, by no means,
that I bid you do:

1989
01:42:41.500 --> 01:42:43.500
Let the bloat King
tempt you again to bed,

1990
01:42:43.620 --> 01:42:45.120
And let him,
for a pair of reechy kisses

1991
01:42:45.250 --> 01:42:48.830
Or paddling in your neck
with his damned fingers,

1992
01:42:48.950 --> 01:42:50.750
Make you to ravel
all this matter out

1993
01:42:50.870 --> 01:42:53.620
That I essentially
am not in madness,

1994
01:42:53.750 --> 01:42:55.000
But mad in craft.

1995
01:42:56.120 --> 01:42:59.830
If words be made of breath
And breath of life,

1996
01:42:59.950 --> 01:43:03.370
I have no life to breathe
What thou hast said to me.

1997
01:43:05.450 --> 01:43:06.950
I must to England, you know that?

1998
01:43:07.080 --> 01:43:09.830
Alack, I had forgot.
'Tis so concluded on.

1999
01:43:10.700 --> 01:43:12.870
This man shall set me packing.

2000
01:43:13.000 --> 01:43:14.870
I'll lug the guts
into the neighbour room.

2001
01:43:15.700 --> 01:43:17.830
- Mother, good night indeed.
- Oh.

2002
01:43:17.950 --> 01:43:20.080
This counsellor
Is now most still,

2003
01:43:20.950 --> 01:43:22.370
most secret,

2004
01:43:23.250 --> 01:43:24.450
and most grave...

2005
01:43:25.870 --> 01:43:28.830
...Who was in life
a foolish prating knave.

2006
01:43:30.620 --> 01:43:34.250
Come, sir,
to draw toward an end with you.

2007
01:43:37.830 --> 01:43:39.120
Good night, mother.

2008
01:43:47.620 --> 01:43:49.080
(Claudius, calling) Gertrude?

2009
01:43:50.500 --> 01:43:51.750
(Gertrude sobbing)

2010
01:43:56.370 --> 01:43:58.200
There's matter in these sighs.

2011
01:43:58.870 --> 01:44:01.750
These profound heaves, you must translate.
'Tis fit we understand them.

2012
01:44:01.870 --> 01:44:03.000
Where is your son?

2013
01:44:04.250 --> 01:44:06.620
Bestow this place on us
a little while!

2014
01:44:10.250 --> 01:44:11.250
Ah, mine own lord...

2015
01:44:12.370 --> 01:44:13.700
...what have I seen tonight.

2016
01:44:13.830 --> 01:44:16.870
What, Gertrude, how does Hamlet?

2017
01:44:17.000 --> 01:44:21.120
Mad as the sea and wind
when both contend

2018
01:44:21.250 --> 01:44:23.370
Which is the mightier.

2019
01:44:23.500 --> 01:44:25.250
In his lawless fit,

2020
01:44:25.370 --> 01:44:27.500
Behind the arras
hearing something stir,

2021
01:44:27.620 --> 01:44:30.620
Whips out his weapon,
cries "A rat, a rat".

2022
01:44:30.750 --> 01:44:35.620
And in this brainish apprehension kills
The unseen good old man.

2023
01:44:39.580 --> 01:44:41.000
O heavy deed.

2024
01:44:43.000 --> 01:44:45.000
It had been so with us
had we been there.

2025
01:44:45.870 --> 01:44:47.620
His liberty is full of threats
to all;

2026
01:44:47.750 --> 01:44:49.750
To you yourself, to us, to everyone.

2027
01:44:50.830 --> 01:44:52.620
Alas, how shall this bloody deed
be answered?

2028
01:44:54.330 --> 01:44:57.750
It will be laid to us, whose providence
Should have kept short,

2029
01:44:57.870 --> 01:45:00.250
restrained, and out of haunt
This mad young man.

2030
01:45:00.370 --> 01:45:02.950
But so much was our love,
We would not understand what was most fit.

2031
01:45:03.080 --> 01:45:04.000
Where is he gone?

2032
01:45:05.250 --> 01:45:07.450
To draw apart the body
he hath killed.

2033
01:45:07.580 --> 01:45:10.620
He...weeps for what is done.

2034
01:45:10.750 --> 01:45:12.370
Ho, Guildenstern!

2035
01:45:14.120 --> 01:45:17.120
Friends both,
go join you with some further aid.

2036
01:45:17.250 --> 01:45:19.120
Hamlet in madness
hath Polonius slain,

2037
01:45:19.250 --> 01:45:22.000
Go seek him out, speak fair,
I pray you, haste.

2038
01:45:23.200 --> 01:45:26.250
Gertrude, away. The sun no sooner
shall the mountains touch

2039
01:45:26.370 --> 01:45:28.370
But we will ship him hence.

2040
01:45:28.500 --> 01:45:31.250
And this vile deed
We must with all our majesty and skill

2041
01:45:31.370 --> 01:45:33.870
Both countenance and excuse.
Gertrude...

2042
01:45:35.250 --> 01:45:36.370
Goodnight.

2043
01:45:41.000 --> 01:45:43.580
How dangerous is it
that this man goes loose.

2044
01:45:43.700 --> 01:45:45.000
How now, what hath befall'n?

2045
01:45:45.120 --> 01:45:47.450
Where the dead body is bestowed
We cannot get from him.

2046
01:45:47.580 --> 01:45:50.450
- But where is he?
- Without, guarded, to know your pleasure.

2047
01:45:50.580 --> 01:45:53.200
- Bring him before us.
- Ho! Bring in the lord!

2048
01:45:55.080 --> 01:45:56.830
(Mimics car engine)

2049
01:45:56.950 --> 01:45:58.500
(Audience laughs)

2050
01:45:59.620 --> 01:46:00.750
Hamlet...

2051
01:46:02.370 --> 01:46:03.500
...where's Polonius?

2052
01:46:03.620 --> 01:46:05.370
- At supper.
- At supper? Where?

2053
01:46:05.500 --> 01:46:08.080
Not where he eats,
but where he is eaten.

2054
01:46:08.620 --> 01:46:11.870
A certain convocation of politic worms
are e'en at him.

2055
01:46:12.000 --> 01:46:14.370
Your worm
is your only emperor for diet:

2056
01:46:15.000 --> 01:46:18.620
we fat all creatures else to fat us,
and we fat ourselves for maggots.

2057
01:46:18.750 --> 01:46:20.870
- Alas, alas.
- A man may fish with the worm

2058
01:46:21.000 --> 01:46:23.580
that hath eat of a king, and eat of the fish
that hath fed of that worm.

2059
01:46:23.700 --> 01:46:25.620
- What dost thou mean by this?
- Nothing.

2060
01:46:25.750 --> 01:46:27.330
(Audience laughs)

2061
01:46:27.450 --> 01:46:30.500
But to show you...how a king

2062
01:46:30.620 --> 01:46:34.080
may go a progress
through the guts of a beggar.

2063
01:46:34.200 --> 01:46:35.450
Where is Polonius?

2064
01:46:35.580 --> 01:46:36.750
In heaven.

2065
01:46:37.580 --> 01:46:39.330
Send thither to see.

2066
01:46:39.450 --> 01:46:42.950
If your messenger find him not there,
seek him i'th'other place yourself!

2067
01:46:43.870 --> 01:46:47.620
But if indeed you find him not
within this month...

2068
01:46:49.500 --> 01:46:52.870
...you shall nose him as you go up
the stairs into the lobby.

2069
01:46:53.000 --> 01:46:55.870
- Go seek him there.
- He will stay till you come.

2070
01:46:56.000 --> 01:46:57.000
Hamlet!

2071
01:46:58.080 --> 01:46:59.120
This deed,

2072
01:46:59.750 --> 01:47:02.000
for thine especial safety,
Which we do tender,

2073
01:47:02.120 --> 01:47:04.830
as we dearly grieve
For that which thou hast done,

2074
01:47:04.950 --> 01:47:07.620
must send thee hence
With fiery quickness.

2075
01:47:08.500 --> 01:47:09.750
Therefore prepare thyself.

2076
01:47:10.370 --> 01:47:12.250
The bark is ready,
and the wind at help,

2077
01:47:12.370 --> 01:47:15.750
Th'associates tend, and everything is bent
For England.

2078
01:47:15.870 --> 01:47:17.580
- For England?
- Ay, Hamlet.

2079
01:47:17.700 --> 01:47:19.870
- Good.
- So is it, if thou knew'st our purposes.

2080
01:47:20.000 --> 01:47:23.000
I see a cherub that sees them.

2081
01:47:27.500 --> 01:47:29.250
But come, for England.

2082
01:47:30.000 --> 01:47:32.750
- Farewell, dear mother.
- Thy loving father, Hamlet.

2083
01:47:32.870 --> 01:47:33.870
My mother.

2084
01:47:34.500 --> 01:47:36.500
Father and mother is man and wife,

2085
01:47:36.620 --> 01:47:38.450
Man and wife is one flesh;

2086
01:47:38.580 --> 01:47:39.830
so my mother.

2087
01:47:41.500 --> 01:47:42.830
Come, for England.

2088
01:47:43.620 --> 01:47:46.120
(Hamlet humming a tune)

2089
01:47:46.250 --> 01:47:48.580
Follow him at foot.
Tempt him with speed abroad.

2090
01:47:48.700 --> 01:47:50.750
Delay it not.
I’ll have him hence tonight.

2091
01:47:56.200 --> 01:47:57.200
And England...

2092
01:47:58.500 --> 01:48:00.370
...if my love
thou hold'st at aught,

2093
01:48:01.120 --> 01:48:04.200
thou mayst not coldly set
Our sovereign process,

2094
01:48:04.330 --> 01:48:07.080
which imports at full,
By letters congruing to that effect,

2095
01:48:07.200 --> 01:48:09.370
The present death of Hamlet.

2096
01:48:09.500 --> 01:48:11.000
Do it, England.

2097
01:48:12.000 --> 01:48:14.120
For like the hectic in my blood
he rages,

2098
01:48:14.250 --> 01:48:16.250
And thou must cure me.

2099
01:48:17.370 --> 01:48:18.830
Till I know 'tis done,

2100
01:48:19.620 --> 01:48:23.000
Howe'er my haps,
my joys were ne'er begun.

2101
01:48:23.120 --> 01:48:24.750
(Tense orchestral music)

2102
01:48:40.620 --> 01:48:44.500
Captain,
from me greet the Danish king.

2103
01:48:45.200 --> 01:48:48.120
Tell him that by his licence

2104
01:48:48.250 --> 01:48:51.500
Fortinbras
Craves the conveyance

2105
01:48:51.620 --> 01:48:54.250
of a promised march
Over his kingdom.

2106
01:48:55.200 --> 01:48:58.950
If that his Majesty
would aught with us,

2107
01:48:59.450 --> 01:49:03.000
We...shall express our duty

2108
01:49:03.120 --> 01:49:04.450
in his eye;

2109
01:49:05.330 --> 01:49:06.330
And let him know so.

2110
01:49:06.450 --> 01:49:08.120
I will do’t, my lord.

2111
01:49:08.870 --> 01:49:11.870
Go...softly on!

2112
01:49:12.000 --> 01:49:13.370
(Tense music continues)

2113
01:49:18.450 --> 01:49:21.250
Good sir, whose powers are these?

2114
01:49:23.250 --> 01:49:25.370
They are of Norway, sir.

2115
01:49:26.250 --> 01:49:28.620
How purposed, sir, I pray you?

2116
01:49:28.750 --> 01:49:31.330
Against some part of Poland.

2117
01:49:31.870 --> 01:49:33.370
Who commands them, sir?

2118
01:49:33.500 --> 01:49:37.330
The nephew to old Norway,
Fortinbras.

2119
01:49:38.700 --> 01:49:42.370
Goes it against the main of Poland, sir,
Or for some frontier?

2120
01:49:43.120 --> 01:49:46.000
Truly to speak,
and with no addition,

2121
01:49:46.830 --> 01:49:49.000
We go to gain
a little patch of ground

2122
01:49:49.120 --> 01:49:51.870
That hath in it no profit
but the name.

2123
01:49:52.500 --> 01:49:55.330
To pay five ducats, five,

2124
01:49:55.450 --> 01:49:57.750
I would not farm it.

2125
01:49:58.330 --> 01:50:00.330
Why, then the Polack
never will defend it.

2126
01:50:00.450 --> 01:50:03.330
Yes, it is already garrisoned.

2127
01:50:05.200 --> 01:50:08.620
Two thousand souls
and twenty thousand ducats

2128
01:50:08.750 --> 01:50:12.370
Will not debate the question
of this straw.

2129
01:50:12.500 --> 01:50:13.500
Mm-hm.

2130
01:50:15.450 --> 01:50:17.370
I humbly thank you, sir.

2131
01:50:17.500 --> 01:50:19.950
- God buy you, sir.
- Will’t please you go, my lord?

2132
01:50:20.080 --> 01:50:23.370
I’ll be with you straight.
Go a little before.

2133
01:50:36.370 --> 01:50:39.370
How all occasion
do inform against me,

2134
01:50:39.500 --> 01:50:41.120
And spur my dull revenge.

2135
01:50:44.120 --> 01:50:46.750
What is a man
If his chief good and market of his time

2136
01:50:46.870 --> 01:50:48.580
Be but to sleep and feed?

2137
01:50:49.620 --> 01:50:51.500
A beast, no more.

2138
01:50:52.200 --> 01:50:54.370
Sure he that made us
with such large discourse,

2139
01:50:54.500 --> 01:50:56.870
Looking before and after,
gave us not

2140
01:50:57.000 --> 01:50:58.750
That capability and godlike reason

2141
01:50:58.870 --> 01:51:00.500
To fust in us unused.

2142
01:51:00.620 --> 01:51:03.750
Now whether it be
Bestial oblivion,

2143
01:51:03.870 --> 01:51:07.870
or some craven scruple
Of thinking too precisely on th’event.

2144
01:51:08.370 --> 01:51:10.370
A thought which, quartered,

2145
01:51:10.500 --> 01:51:12.120
hath but one part wisdom

2146
01:51:12.250 --> 01:51:14.450
And ever three parts coward.

2147
01:51:14.580 --> 01:51:18.000
I do not know
Why yet I live to say this thing’s to do,

2148
01:51:18.120 --> 01:51:20.250
Sith I have cause, and will,

2149
01:51:20.370 --> 01:51:22.750
and strength, and means
To do’t.

2150
01:51:24.120 --> 01:51:26.580
Examples gross
as the earth exhort me,

2151
01:51:26.700 --> 01:51:29.250
Witness this army
of such mass and charge,

2152
01:51:29.370 --> 01:51:31.500
Led by a delicate and tender prince,

2153
01:51:31.620 --> 01:51:34.330
Whose spirit,
with divine ambition puffed,

2154
01:51:35.000 --> 01:51:36.830
Makes mouths at the invisible event,

2155
01:51:36.950 --> 01:51:40.000
Exposing what is mortal and unsure

2156
01:51:40.120 --> 01:51:42.500
To all that fortune, death,
and danger dare,

2157
01:51:42.620 --> 01:51:44.500
Even for an eggshell.

2158
01:51:46.000 --> 01:51:50.000
Rightly to be great
Is not to stir without great argument,

2159
01:51:50.700 --> 01:51:54.000
But greatly to find quarrel
in a straw

2160
01:51:54.120 --> 01:51:56.370
When honour’s at the stake!

2161
01:51:58.120 --> 01:51:59.750
How stand I then,

2162
01:52:00.250 --> 01:52:02.250
That have a father killed,
a mother stained,

2163
01:52:02.370 --> 01:52:04.370
Excitements of my reason
and my blood,

2164
01:52:04.500 --> 01:52:06.000
And let all sleep,

2165
01:52:06.120 --> 01:52:08.120
while to my shame I see

2166
01:52:08.250 --> 01:52:10.500
The imminent death
of twenty thousand men

2167
01:52:10.620 --> 01:52:12.620
That, for a fantasy
and trick of fame,

2168
01:52:12.750 --> 01:52:15.120
Go to their graves like beds,

2169
01:52:15.250 --> 01:52:16.580
fight for a plot

2170
01:52:16.700 --> 01:52:19.120
Whereon the numbers
cannot try the cause,

2171
01:52:19.250 --> 01:52:23.830
Which is not tomb enough and continent
To hide the slain?

2172
01:52:26.450 --> 01:52:28.750
O!

2173
01:52:35.500 --> 01:52:37.120
From this time forth...

2174
01:52:39.000 --> 01:52:41.450
...My thoughts be bloody

2175
01:52:42.330 --> 01:52:43.870
or be nothing worth.

2176
01:52:44.000 --> 01:52:45.620
(Quick string music)

2177
01:52:49.500 --> 01:52:52.500
- I will not speak with her.
- She is importunate,

2178
01:52:52.620 --> 01:52:54.000
Indeed distract.

2179
01:52:54.120 --> 01:52:55.830
Her mood will needs be pitied.

2180
01:52:55.950 --> 01:52:58.620
- What would she have?
- She speaks much of her father,

2181
01:52:58.750 --> 01:53:01.000
says she hears
There's tricks i'th' world,

2182
01:53:01.120 --> 01:53:03.370
and hems, and beats her heart,

2183
01:53:03.500 --> 01:53:05.750
Spurns enviously at straws,

2184
01:53:05.870 --> 01:53:08.750
speaks things in doubt
That carry but half sense.

2185
01:53:08.870 --> 01:53:11.370
Her speech is nothing,

2186
01:53:11.500 --> 01:53:14.500
Yet the unshaped use of it doth move

2187
01:53:14.620 --> 01:53:16.080
The hearers to collection.

2188
01:53:16.200 --> 01:53:19.080
'Twere good she were spoken with,
for she may strew

2189
01:53:19.200 --> 01:53:21.620
Dangerous conjectures
in ill-breeding minds.

2190
01:53:23.370 --> 01:53:24.330
Let her approach.

2191
01:53:26.620 --> 01:53:28.000
To my sick soul,

2192
01:53:28.870 --> 01:53:31.120
as sin’s true nature is,

2193
01:53:31.250 --> 01:53:34.120
Each toy seems prologue
to some great amiss.

2194
01:53:35.120 --> 01:53:37.620
So full of artless jealousy is guilt

2195
01:53:38.450 --> 01:53:40.120
It spills itself

2196
01:53:40.250 --> 01:53:41.870
in fearing to be spilt.

2197
01:53:42.000 --> 01:53:43.500
Madam, this letter...

2198
01:53:43.620 --> 01:53:46.120
Where is the beauteous
Majesty of Denmark?

2199
01:53:47.000 --> 01:53:48.000
(Horatio) Why?

2200
01:53:48.120 --> 01:53:50.120
How now, Ophelia?

2201
01:53:50.250 --> 01:53:53.450
♪ How should I your true love know

2202
01:53:54.200 --> 01:53:57.250
♪ From another one?

2203
01:53:57.370 --> 01:53:58.870
♪ Mm-mm-mm

2204
01:53:59.000 --> 01:54:00.500
♪ Mm-mm-mm ♪

2205
01:54:00.620 --> 01:54:01.620
Ah!

2206
01:54:02.330 --> 01:54:05.450
♪ By his cockle hat and staff

2207
01:54:05.580 --> 01:54:08.370
♪ And his sandal shoon

2208
01:54:08.500 --> 01:54:11.500
♪ Doo-doo-doo-doo doo-oo-ooh ♪

2209
01:54:11.620 --> 01:54:13.370
What imports this song?

2210
01:54:13.500 --> 01:54:15.500
Say you? Nay.

2211
01:54:16.000 --> 01:54:18.120
Pray you mark.

2212
01:54:19.450 --> 01:54:22.500
♪ He is dead and gone, lady

2213
01:54:23.200 --> 01:54:26.080
♪ He is dead and gone

2214
01:54:26.200 --> 01:54:27.620
♪ Mm-mm-mm

2215
01:54:27.750 --> 01:54:29.750
♪ Mm-mm-mm

2216
01:54:29.870 --> 01:54:33.200
♪ At his head a grass-green turf

2217
01:54:33.330 --> 01:54:36.000
♪ At his heels a stone ♪

2218
01:54:36.120 --> 01:54:38.250
- O ho!
- Nay, but Ophelia...

2219
01:54:38.370 --> 01:54:40.450
Pray you mark.

2220
01:54:42.250 --> 01:54:45.370
♪ White his shroud
as the mountain snow ♪

2221
01:54:45.500 --> 01:54:47.370
Alas, look here, my lord.

2222
01:54:47.500 --> 01:54:50.120
♪ Larded with sweet flowers

2223
01:54:50.750 --> 01:54:54.330
♪ Which bewept to the grave
did not go

2224
01:54:54.450 --> 01:54:57.500
♪ With true-love showers ♪

2225
01:54:58.120 --> 01:54:59.330
How do you, pretty lady?

2226
01:54:59.450 --> 01:55:01.450
- Well...
- (Audience laughs)

2227
01:55:01.580 --> 01:55:02.620
Good dild you.

2228
01:55:02.750 --> 01:55:06.370
Mm-hm. They say the owl
was a baker's daughter.

2229
01:55:06.500 --> 01:55:10.620
Lord, we know what we are,
but know not what we may be.

2230
01:55:11.370 --> 01:55:13.450
God be at your table!

2231
01:55:13.580 --> 01:55:15.580
- Conceit upon her father.
- Pray!

2232
01:55:16.700 --> 01:55:18.500
Let's have no words of this,

2233
01:55:18.620 --> 01:55:21.500
but when they ask you what it means,
say you this.

2234
01:55:21.620 --> 01:55:24.200
♪ Tomorrow is Saint Valentine's day

2235
01:55:24.330 --> 01:55:26.080
♪ All in the morning betime

2236
01:55:26.200 --> 01:55:30.250
♪ And I a maid at your window
To be your Valentine

2237
01:55:30.370 --> 01:55:33.580
♪ Then up he rose
then up he rose, then up he rose

2238
01:55:33.700 --> 01:55:37.370
♪ And donned his clo'es
And dupped the chamber door

2239
01:55:41.500 --> 01:55:44.500
♪ Let in the maid that out a maid
Ra-ta-ta-ta

2240
01:55:44.620 --> 01:55:45.950
♪ Never departed more

2241
01:55:46.080 --> 01:55:48.620
- ♪ More, more, more more, more, more ♪
- Pretty Ophelia...

2242
01:55:48.750 --> 01:55:50.750
Indeed, without an oath,
I'll make an end on't.

2243
01:55:50.870 --> 01:55:54.500
♪ By Gis and by Saint Charity
Alack and fie for shame

2244
01:55:54.620 --> 01:55:58.080
♪ Young men will do't if they come to't
By Cock, they are to blame

2245
01:55:58.200 --> 01:56:01.950
♪ Quoth she, "Before you tumbled me"
Quoth she, "Before you tumbled me"

2246
01:56:02.080 --> 01:56:04.870
♪ "You promised me to wed"

2247
01:56:05.000 --> 01:56:06.370
♪ He answers

2248
01:56:09.580 --> 01:56:12.250
♪ "So would I a done, by yonder sun"
Ra-ta-ta-ta

2249
01:56:12.370 --> 01:56:16.450
♪ "And thou hadst not come to my bed
Bed, bed, bed, bed, bed, bed" ♪

2250
01:56:17.620 --> 01:56:21.500
- How long hath she been thus?
- I hope all will be well.

2251
01:56:21.620 --> 01:56:23.700
We must be patient.

2252
01:56:23.830 --> 01:56:25.870
But I cannot choose but weep

2253
01:56:26.000 --> 01:56:29.830
to think they would lay him
i'th' cold ground.

2254
01:56:31.080 --> 01:56:32.830
My brother shall know of it.

2255
01:56:33.500 --> 01:56:34.500
And so...

2256
01:56:35.620 --> 01:56:38.500
...I thank you
for your good counsel.

2257
01:56:38.620 --> 01:56:40.120
Come, my coach.

2258
01:56:40.250 --> 01:56:43.330
Good night, ladies, good night.
Sweet ladies, good night, good night.

2259
01:56:43.450 --> 01:56:45.700
Follow her close;
give her good watch, I pray you.

2260
01:56:47.750 --> 01:56:49.870
O, this is the poison of deep grief.

2261
01:56:50.000 --> 01:56:52.000
It springs
All from her father's death.

2262
01:56:52.950 --> 01:56:54.750
O Gertrude, Gertrude,
When sorrows come,

2263
01:56:54.870 --> 01:56:57.620
they come not single spies,
But in battalions!

2264
01:56:57.750 --> 01:56:59.870
Laertes is in secret
come from France,

2265
01:57:00.000 --> 01:57:02.830
And wants not buzzers to infect his ear
With pestilent speeches

2266
01:57:02.950 --> 01:57:04.370
of his father's death.

2267
01:57:04.870 --> 01:57:06.950
- What is the matter?
- My lord.

2268
01:57:07.080 --> 01:57:09.870
The young Laertes, in a riotous head,
O'erbears your officers.

2269
01:57:10.000 --> 01:57:13.080
Where is this king?
Give me my father!

2270
01:57:13.620 --> 01:57:15.450
(Gertrude) Calmly, good Laertes.

2271
01:57:15.580 --> 01:57:17.620
That drop of blood that's calm

2272
01:57:17.750 --> 01:57:19.870
proclaims me bastard,

2273
01:57:20.000 --> 01:57:22.000
Cries cuckold to my father,

2274
01:57:22.120 --> 01:57:25.000
brands the harlot
Even here

2275
01:57:25.120 --> 01:57:29.000
between the chaste unsmirched brow
Of my true mother.

2276
01:57:29.120 --> 01:57:32.250
What is the cause, Laertes,
That thy rebellion looks so giant-like?

2277
01:57:32.370 --> 01:57:33.700
Let him go, Gertrude.

2278
01:57:33.830 --> 01:57:35.750
Do not fear our person.

2279
01:57:36.830 --> 01:57:39.000
Why thou art thus incensed?

2280
01:57:39.120 --> 01:57:40.700
Let him go, Gertrude.

2281
01:57:42.580 --> 01:57:44.120
- Speak, man.
- Where is my father?

2282
01:57:44.250 --> 01:57:45.370
- Dead.
- But not by him.

2283
01:57:45.500 --> 01:57:47.750
- Let him demand his fill.
- How came he dead?

2284
01:57:48.250 --> 01:57:50.330
I'll not be juggled with.

2285
01:57:51.000 --> 01:57:53.120
To hell, allegiance!

2286
01:57:53.250 --> 01:57:55.870
Vows to the blackest devil!

2287
01:57:56.000 --> 01:57:58.080
I dare damnation!

2288
01:57:58.200 --> 01:58:01.120
Only I will be revenged
Most thoroughly for my father!

2289
01:58:01.250 --> 01:58:04.700
Why now you speak
Like a good child and a true gentleman.

2290
01:58:05.870 --> 01:58:07.870
That I am guiltless
of your father's death

2291
01:58:08.000 --> 01:58:10.580
And am most sensibly
in grief for it,

2292
01:58:10.700 --> 01:58:13.870
It shall as level
to your judgment 'pear

2293
01:58:14.620 --> 01:58:16.750
As day does to your eye.

2294
01:58:16.870 --> 01:58:17.870
(Bell ringing)

2295
01:58:18.000 --> 01:58:20.120
How now, what noise is that?

2296
01:58:23.250 --> 01:58:24.700
(Heavy breathing)

2297
01:58:28.370 --> 01:58:29.620
(Grunting)

2298
01:58:32.330 --> 01:58:35.200
O heat, dry up my brains.

2299
01:58:35.330 --> 01:58:36.500
Dear maid.

2300
01:58:38.080 --> 01:58:39.370
Kind sister.

2301
01:58:40.080 --> 01:58:41.700
Sweet Ophelia.

2302
01:58:47.950 --> 01:58:50.620
O heavens,
is't possible a young maid's wits

2303
01:58:50.750 --> 01:58:52.620
Should be as mortal
as an old man's life?

2304
01:58:52.750 --> 01:58:55.750
They bore him bare-faced
on the bier!

2305
01:58:55.870 --> 01:58:57.000
Fare you well, my dove.

2306
01:58:57.120 --> 01:58:59.500
Hadst thou thy wits
and didst persuade revenge,

2307
01:58:59.620 --> 01:59:01.250
It could not move thus.

2308
01:59:08.620 --> 01:59:10.250
You must sing.

2309
01:59:13.500 --> 01:59:15.700
♪ A-down a-down ♪

2310
01:59:17.120 --> 01:59:18.500
♪ A-down a-down ♪

2311
01:59:18.620 --> 01:59:19.620
(Laughs)

2312
01:59:19.750 --> 01:59:22.120
And you call him ♪ a-down-a ♪

2313
01:59:23.870 --> 01:59:24.870
A-down-a.

2314
01:59:25.950 --> 01:59:28.200
O, how the wheel becomes it!

2315
01:59:30.000 --> 01:59:31.370
There's rosemary.

2316
01:59:32.870 --> 01:59:34.580
That's for remembrance.

2317
01:59:35.620 --> 01:59:36.950
Pray you, love.

2318
01:59:38.330 --> 01:59:39.330
Remember.

2319
01:59:39.450 --> 01:59:42.120
And there is pansies,
that's for thoughts.

2320
01:59:42.250 --> 01:59:45.330
- Thoughts and remembrance fitted.
- There's fennel.

2321
01:59:46.580 --> 01:59:48.830
For you, and columbines.

2322
01:59:48.950 --> 01:59:50.870
There's rue for you. (Gasps)

2323
01:59:51.000 --> 01:59:52.830
And here's some for me!

2324
01:59:53.870 --> 01:59:57.580
We may call it
herb of grace a Sundays.

2325
02:00:00.500 --> 02:00:03.080
You must wear your rue...

2326
02:00:04.080 --> 02:00:05.500
...with a difference.

2327
02:00:10.620 --> 02:00:12.700
There's a daisy!

2328
02:00:26.250 --> 02:00:28.120
I would give you some violets,

2329
02:00:28.250 --> 02:00:31.950
but they withered all
when my father died!

2330
02:00:34.450 --> 02:00:36.080
They say he made a good end.

2331
02:00:36.200 --> 02:00:38.500
♪ For bonny sweet Robin
is all my joy ♪

2332
02:00:38.620 --> 02:00:41.700
Thought and affliction,
passion, hell itself

2333
02:00:41.830 --> 02:00:44.870
She turns to favour
and to prettiness.

2334
02:00:45.000 --> 02:00:48.200
♪ And will he not come again?

2335
02:00:49.370 --> 02:00:52.450
♪ And will he not come again?

2336
02:00:54.250 --> 02:00:56.580
♪ No, no, he is dead

2337
02:00:57.120 --> 02:00:59.120
♪ Go to thy death-bed

2338
02:00:59.620 --> 02:01:02.370
♪ He never will come again

2339
02:01:04.750 --> 02:01:08.200
♪ His beard was as white... ♪

2340
02:01:08.330 --> 02:01:09.950
(Laertes joins in) ♪ ...as snow ♪

2341
02:01:14.200 --> 02:01:17.120
♪ All flaxen was his poll

2342
02:01:17.870 --> 02:01:19.870
♪ He is gone, he is gone

2343
02:01:20.000 --> 02:01:22.000
♪ And we cast away moan ♪

2344
02:01:22.120 --> 02:01:23.700
(Sobbing and screaming)

2345
02:01:24.330 --> 02:01:25.620
Ophelia.

2346
02:01:30.250 --> 02:01:33.500
God have mercy...

2347
02:01:34.620 --> 02:01:36.080
...on his soul.

2348
02:01:38.580 --> 02:01:41.330
And of all Christian souls.

2349
02:01:44.870 --> 02:01:46.250
God buy you.

2350
02:01:57.120 --> 02:01:58.500
Do you see this?

2351
02:02:02.330 --> 02:02:05.000
O God.

2352
02:02:05.120 --> 02:02:08.000
Laertes, I must commune with your grief,
Or you deny me right.

2353
02:02:09.620 --> 02:02:10.620
Go but apart.

2354
02:02:11.370 --> 02:02:14.080
Make choice
of whom your wisest friends you will,

2355
02:02:14.200 --> 02:02:16.700
And they shall hear and judge
'twixt you and me.

2356
02:02:17.580 --> 02:02:20.620
If by direct or by collateral hand
They find us touched,

2357
02:02:20.750 --> 02:02:23.620
we will our kingdom give,
Our crown, our life,

2358
02:02:23.750 --> 02:02:27.200
and all that we call ours
To you in satisfaction.

2359
02:02:28.580 --> 02:02:29.450
But if not,

2360
02:02:30.370 --> 02:02:32.750
Be you content
to lend your patience to us,

2361
02:02:32.870 --> 02:02:35.200
And we shall jointly labour
with your soul

2362
02:02:35.330 --> 02:02:36.750
To give it due content.

2363
02:02:36.870 --> 02:02:38.120
Let this be so.

2364
02:02:39.500 --> 02:02:41.330
His means of death,

2365
02:02:41.450 --> 02:02:44.120
his obscure funeral,

2366
02:02:44.250 --> 02:02:45.950
No noble rite,

2367
02:02:46.080 --> 02:02:47.830
nor formal ostentation,

2368
02:02:47.950 --> 02:02:49.250
Cry to be heard,

2369
02:02:49.370 --> 02:02:51.200
as 'twere from heaven to earth.

2370
02:02:51.870 --> 02:02:54.750
- That I must call't in question.
- So you shall.

2371
02:02:55.870 --> 02:02:58.370
And where th'offence is,
let the great axe fall.

2372
02:03:00.700 --> 02:03:01.700
I pray you...

2373
02:03:03.750 --> 02:03:04.750
...go with me.

2374
02:03:21.200 --> 02:03:24.580
Madam, your son
is safe arrived in Denmark.

2375
02:03:24.700 --> 02:03:26.500
This letter
I even now received of him

2376
02:03:26.620 --> 02:03:28.370
Wherein he writes
how he escaped the danger

2377
02:03:28.500 --> 02:03:31.250
And subtle treason
that the King had plotted.

2378
02:03:31.370 --> 02:03:34.370
Being crossed by the contention of the winds,
He found the letter sent with him,

2379
02:03:34.500 --> 02:03:37.000
Wherein he saw himself
betrayed to death.

2380
02:03:37.120 --> 02:03:38.370
Then I perceive

2381
02:03:38.500 --> 02:03:40.700
there’s treason in those looks

2382
02:03:40.830 --> 02:03:42.700
That seemed to sugar
o’er his villainy.

2383
02:03:43.250 --> 02:03:46.450
So, I will soothe and please him,
for a time.

2384
02:03:47.500 --> 02:03:49.580
But know you not, Horatio,
where he is?

2385
02:03:49.700 --> 02:03:52.330
Yes, madam, and he hath appointed me
To meet him

2386
02:03:52.450 --> 02:03:54.620
on the east side of the palace
Tomorrow morning.

2387
02:03:54.750 --> 02:03:56.120
O fail not, good Horatio,

2388
02:03:56.250 --> 02:03:58.500
And withal commend me
a mother’s care to him.

2389
02:03:58.620 --> 02:04:01.830
- Bid him awhile be wary of his presence.
- Never make doubt of that.

2390
02:04:01.950 --> 02:04:04.330
By this the news be come to Court
he is returned.

2391
02:04:04.450 --> 02:04:07.000
Observe the King
and you shall quickly find,

2392
02:04:07.120 --> 02:04:09.450
Hamlet being here,
things fell not to his mind.

2393
02:04:09.580 --> 02:04:11.700
Thanks be to heaven
for blessing of the Prince.

2394
02:04:11.830 --> 02:04:14.080
A thousand mothers' blessings
to my son.

2395
02:04:14.200 --> 02:04:15.250
Madam, adieu.

2396
02:04:16.830 --> 02:04:18.620
(Deep orchestral music)

2397
02:04:21.750 --> 02:04:22.950
"High and mighty,

2398
02:04:23.080 --> 02:04:25.120
you shall know I am set naked
on your kingdom.

2399
02:04:25.250 --> 02:04:28.120
Tomorrow shall I beg leave
to see your kingly eyes,

2400
02:04:28.250 --> 02:04:31.620
when I shall, first asking your pardon,
thereunto recount the occasion

2401
02:04:31.750 --> 02:04:33.750
of my sudden
and more strange return.

2402
02:04:33.870 --> 02:04:34.950
Hamlet."

2403
02:04:35.080 --> 02:04:37.330
What should this mean?
Are all the rest come back?

2404
02:04:37.450 --> 02:04:39.200
Or is it some abuse,
and no such thing?

2405
02:04:39.330 --> 02:04:41.120
- Know you the hand?
- 'Tis Hamlet's character.

2406
02:04:41.870 --> 02:04:44.870
"Naked". And in a postscript here
he says "alone".

2407
02:04:45.000 --> 02:04:47.000
- Can you devise me?
- I am lost in it, my lord.

2408
02:04:47.120 --> 02:04:48.120
But let him come.

2409
02:04:48.870 --> 02:04:51.700
It warms
the very sickness in my heart

2410
02:04:51.830 --> 02:04:54.120
That I shall live
and tell him to his teeth,

2411
02:04:54.250 --> 02:04:55.330
"Thus didest thou".

2412
02:04:55.450 --> 02:04:57.500
Now must your conscience
my acquittance seal,

2413
02:04:57.620 --> 02:05:00.000
And you must now
put me in your heart for friend,

2414
02:05:00.120 --> 02:05:02.870
Since you have heard,
and with a knowing ear,

2415
02:05:03.000 --> 02:05:06.200
That he which hath your noble father slain
Pursued my life.

2416
02:05:06.330 --> 02:05:09.500
It well appears. But tell me
Why you proceeded not against these feats.

2417
02:05:09.620 --> 02:05:12.370
O, for two special reasons,

2418
02:05:12.500 --> 02:05:14.750
Which may to you perhaps
seem much unsinewed,

2419
02:05:14.870 --> 02:05:16.450
But yet to me th'are strong.

2420
02:05:18.250 --> 02:05:21.000
The Queen his mother
Lives almost by his looks,

2421
02:05:21.120 --> 02:05:24.330
and for myself,
My virtue or my plague, be it either which,

2422
02:05:25.250 --> 02:05:27.330
She is so conjunctive
to my life and soul

2423
02:05:27.450 --> 02:05:29.500
That, as the star moves
not but in his sphere,

2424
02:05:29.620 --> 02:05:31.000
I could not but by her.

2425
02:05:31.120 --> 02:05:32.120
(Laertes chuckles)

2426
02:05:32.250 --> 02:05:34.620
The other motive
Why to a public count I might not go

2427
02:05:34.750 --> 02:05:36.870
Is the great love
the general gender bear him.

2428
02:05:37.000 --> 02:05:39.620
And so have I a noble father lost!

2429
02:05:40.370 --> 02:05:42.250
A sister driven into...

2430
02:05:43.000 --> 02:05:44.620
...desp'rate terms.

2431
02:05:44.750 --> 02:05:46.120
But my revenge will come.

2432
02:05:46.250 --> 02:05:47.750
I lov’d your father!

2433
02:05:50.870 --> 02:05:52.370
My good Laertes...

2434
02:05:53.870 --> 02:05:55.370
...will you be ruled by me?

2435
02:05:58.000 --> 02:05:58.830
Ay, my lord,

2436
02:05:58.950 --> 02:06:00.500
So you will not
o'errule me to a peace.

2437
02:06:00.620 --> 02:06:01.700
To thine own peace.

2438
02:06:04.620 --> 02:06:05.620
For Hamlet...

2439
02:06:07.370 --> 02:06:10.370
I will work him
To an exploit, now ripe in my device,

2440
02:06:10.500 --> 02:06:12.870
Under the which
he shall not choose but fall.

2441
02:06:13.620 --> 02:06:16.950
And for his death
no wind of blame shall breathe,

2442
02:06:17.080 --> 02:06:19.200
But even his mother
shall uncharge the practice

2443
02:06:19.330 --> 02:06:21.450
- And call it accident.
- My lord, I will be ruled,

2444
02:06:21.580 --> 02:06:24.330
The rather if you could devise it so
That I might be the organ.

2445
02:06:24.450 --> 02:06:25.620
It falls right.

2446
02:06:28.500 --> 02:06:31.120
You have been talked of
since your travel much,

2447
02:06:31.250 --> 02:06:34.750
And that in Hamlet's hearing, for qualities
Wherein they say you shine:

2448
02:06:34.870 --> 02:06:37.370
your skill in combat,
and for your rapier most especial.

2449
02:06:37.500 --> 02:06:39.370
That they cry out
‘twould be a sight indeed

2450
02:06:39.500 --> 02:06:40.580
If one could match you.

2451
02:06:41.830 --> 02:06:45.250
This report of you
Did Hamlet much envenom with his envy.

2452
02:06:45.370 --> 02:06:47.620
- Now out of this...
- What out of this, my lord?

2453
02:06:47.750 --> 02:06:50.830
Laertes,
was your father dear to you?

2454
02:06:52.830 --> 02:06:55.250
- Why ask you this?
- What would you undertake

2455
02:06:55.370 --> 02:06:59.200
To show yourself your father's son in deed
More than in words?

2456
02:07:01.370 --> 02:07:02.750
To cut his throat i'th' church.

2457
02:07:02.870 --> 02:07:05.080
No place indeed
should murder sanctuarize!

2458
02:07:05.200 --> 02:07:07.620
Revenge should have no bounds!

2459
02:07:09.870 --> 02:07:12.000
But good Laertes,
Will you do this?

2460
02:07:13.120 --> 02:07:15.080
Keep close within your chamber.

2461
02:07:15.200 --> 02:07:18.080
Hamlet, returned,
shall know you are come home.

2462
02:07:18.200 --> 02:07:20.500
We'll put on those
shall praise your excellence,

2463
02:07:20.620 --> 02:07:22.370
And wager o'er your heads.

2464
02:07:22.500 --> 02:07:26.120
He, being remiss,
Most generous, and free from all contriving,

2465
02:07:26.250 --> 02:07:28.870
Will not peruse the foils,
so that with ease,

2466
02:07:29.000 --> 02:07:30.700
Or with a little shuffling,

2467
02:07:31.330 --> 02:07:33.370
you may choose
A sword unbated,

2468
02:07:33.500 --> 02:07:35.500
and in a pass of practice

2469
02:07:35.620 --> 02:07:37.250
Requite him for your father.

2470
02:07:37.370 --> 02:07:39.950
I will do't. And for that purpose,
I'll anoint my sword.

2471
02:07:41.700 --> 02:07:44.200
I bought an unction
of a mountebank

2472
02:07:44.330 --> 02:07:47.120
So mortal
that but dip a knife in it,

2473
02:07:47.250 --> 02:07:49.580
Where it draws blood,
no cataplasm so rare,

2474
02:07:49.700 --> 02:07:52.370
Can save the thing from death
That is but scratched withal.

2475
02:07:52.870 --> 02:07:54.750
I'll touch my point
With this contagion,

2476
02:07:54.870 --> 02:07:57.620
that if I gall him slightly,
It may be death.

2477
02:07:57.750 --> 02:07:59.330
If this should fail,
And our drift look through

2478
02:07:59.450 --> 02:08:01.500
our bad performance,
'Twere better not essayed.

2479
02:08:02.370 --> 02:08:04.750
Therefore this project
Should have a back or second

2480
02:08:04.870 --> 02:08:07.000
If this did blast in proof.

2481
02:08:07.120 --> 02:08:08.620
Soft, let me see.

2482
02:08:10.330 --> 02:08:11.330
I ha't.

2483
02:08:12.370 --> 02:08:14.250
When in your motion
you are hot and dry,

2484
02:08:14.370 --> 02:08:16.750
As make your bouts
more violent to that end,

2485
02:08:16.870 --> 02:08:18.330
And that he calls for drink,

2486
02:08:19.000 --> 02:08:22.120
I'll have prepared him
A chalice for the nonce,

2487
02:08:22.250 --> 02:08:23.250
whereon but sipping,

2488
02:08:23.370 --> 02:08:26.250
If he by chance
escape your venomed stuck,

2489
02:08:26.370 --> 02:08:27.950
Our purpose may hold there.

2490
02:08:28.080 --> 02:08:29.080
But stay, who’s there?

2491
02:08:29.750 --> 02:08:31.250
(Gertrude) One woe

2492
02:08:31.870 --> 02:08:34.500
doth tread upon another's heel,

2493
02:08:34.620 --> 02:08:36.500
So fast they follow.

2494
02:08:38.870 --> 02:08:41.250
Your sister's drowned, Laertes.

2495
02:08:44.500 --> 02:08:45.500
Drowned?

2496
02:08:49.870 --> 02:08:50.870
O.

2497
02:08:53.500 --> 02:08:54.620
Uh, where?

2498
02:08:54.750 --> 02:08:57.750
There is a willow
grows aslant the brook

2499
02:08:57.870 --> 02:09:00.500
That shows his hoary leaves
in the glassy stream.

2500
02:09:01.580 --> 02:09:04.950
Therewith fantastic garlands
did she make

2501
02:09:05.580 --> 02:09:08.200
Of crow-flowers, nettles,

2502
02:09:08.330 --> 02:09:11.000
daisies, and long purples,

2503
02:09:11.750 --> 02:09:14.500
That liberal shepherds
give a grosser name,

2504
02:09:14.620 --> 02:09:18.120
But our cold maids
do dead men's fingers call them.

2505
02:09:19.120 --> 02:09:21.250
There on the pendent boughs

2506
02:09:21.370 --> 02:09:24.250
her crownet weeds
Clamb'ring to hang,

2507
02:09:24.870 --> 02:09:27.200
an envious sliver broke...

2508
02:09:28.250 --> 02:09:31.000
...When down her weedy trophies
and herself

2509
02:09:31.870 --> 02:09:34.120
Fell in the weeping brook.

2510
02:09:35.580 --> 02:09:37.370
Her clothes spread wide,

2511
02:09:38.000 --> 02:09:40.620
And mermaid-like awhile
they bore her up,

2512
02:09:40.750 --> 02:09:43.700
Which time
she chanted snatches of old lauds,

2513
02:09:44.330 --> 02:09:46.870
As one incapable
of her own distress.

2514
02:09:48.000 --> 02:09:50.000
Or like a creature

2515
02:09:50.580 --> 02:09:53.000
native and indued
Unto that element.

2516
02:09:54.450 --> 02:09:55.870
But long it could not be

2517
02:09:56.500 --> 02:09:59.700
Till that her garments,
heavy with their drink,

2518
02:10:00.200 --> 02:10:02.620
Pulled the poor wretch
from her melodious lay...

2519
02:10:04.120 --> 02:10:05.250
...To muddy death.

2520
02:10:08.080 --> 02:10:09.370
Alas, then...

2521
02:10:11.200 --> 02:10:12.750
...she is drowned.

2522
02:10:13.950 --> 02:10:14.950
(Gertrude) Drowned.

2523
02:10:15.620 --> 02:10:16.700
Drowned.

2524
02:10:19.000 --> 02:10:20.000
(Laertes scoffs)

2525
02:10:22.250 --> 02:10:23.250
Oh.

2526
02:10:24.370 --> 02:10:26.870
Too much of water hast thou...

2527
02:10:27.870 --> 02:10:31.120
...poor Ophelia,
And therefore I forbid my tears.

2528
02:10:34.080 --> 02:10:35.750
But yet
It is our trick;

2529
02:10:37.080 --> 02:10:40.200
nature her custom holds,
Let shame say what it will.

2530
02:10:40.330 --> 02:10:41.580
(Clears his throat)

2531
02:10:41.700 --> 02:10:42.950
Adieu, my lord.

2532
02:10:44.080 --> 02:10:47.750
I have a speech o' fire
that fain would blaze.

2533
02:10:50.120 --> 02:10:52.250
But that this folly drowns it.

2534
02:10:54.000 --> 02:10:55.000
Let's follow.

2535
02:10:57.250 --> 02:11:00.330
Gertrude, how much I had to do
to calm his rage!

2536
02:11:01.620 --> 02:11:03.250
Now fear I this...

2537
02:11:04.250 --> 02:11:05.750
...will give it start again.

2538
02:11:08.950 --> 02:11:10.120
Therefore let's follow.

2539
02:11:13.580 --> 02:11:15.370
(High-pitched orchestral music)

2540
02:11:20.500 --> 02:11:22.000
(Music becomes eerie)

2541
02:11:35.250 --> 02:11:38.120
♪ In youth when I did love, did love

2542
02:11:38.250 --> 02:11:41.080
♪ Methought it was very sweet

2543
02:11:41.200 --> 02:11:42.620
♪ Sweet

2544
02:11:42.750 --> 02:11:44.870
♪ Sweet

2545
02:11:45.000 --> 02:11:49.620
♪ To contract-O-the time
for-a-my behove

2546
02:11:49.750 --> 02:11:52.620
♪ O methought
there-a-was nothing-a-meet ♪

2547
02:11:53.250 --> 02:11:54.750
Will you ha' the truth an't?

2548
02:11:55.250 --> 02:11:57.250
If this had not been a gentlewoman,

2549
02:11:57.370 --> 02:11:59.750
she should have been buried
out o' Christian burial.

2550
02:11:59.870 --> 02:12:01.620
Why, there thou say'st.

2551
02:12:01.750 --> 02:12:05.000
And the more pity that great folk
should have countenance in this world

2552
02:12:05.120 --> 02:12:07.750
to drown or hang themselves
more than their even-Christen.

2553
02:12:08.620 --> 02:12:10.250
Come, my spade.

2554
02:12:11.750 --> 02:12:14.370
- I'll put a question to thee.
- Mm. Go on.

2555
02:12:14.500 --> 02:12:18.120
What is he that builds stronger
than either the mason,

2556
02:12:18.250 --> 02:12:20.250
the shipwright, or the carpenter?

2557
02:12:21.620 --> 02:12:22.620
Ooh!

2558
02:12:22.750 --> 02:12:24.250
The gallows-maker,

2559
02:12:24.370 --> 02:12:27.450
for that frame
outlives a thousand tenants.

2560
02:12:27.580 --> 02:12:28.700
(Both laugh)

2561
02:12:28.830 --> 02:12:31.700
That’s pretty. I like thy wit well.

2562
02:12:31.830 --> 02:12:34.120
No. To't again, come.

2563
02:12:34.750 --> 02:12:38.500
Who builds stronger than a mason,
a shipwright, or a carpenter?

2564
02:12:38.620 --> 02:12:40.750
Ay, tell me that and unyoke.

2565
02:12:41.370 --> 02:12:42.500
I cannot tell.

2566
02:12:42.620 --> 02:12:44.620
Cudgel thy brains no more about it.

2567
02:12:44.750 --> 02:12:47.450
And when you are asked
this question next, say

2568
02:12:47.580 --> 02:12:49.000
"A grave-maker".

2569
02:12:49.120 --> 02:12:52.750
The houses he makes
lasts till doomsday.

2570
02:12:52.870 --> 02:12:54.500
(Both growl)

2571
02:12:54.620 --> 02:12:55.620
Go to.

2572
02:12:55.750 --> 02:12:57.080
(Laughs)

2573
02:12:57.200 --> 02:12:58.750
(Hamlet) In the dark

2574
02:12:58.870 --> 02:13:01.450
Groped I to find
their grand commission which,

2575
02:13:01.580 --> 02:13:03.870
My fears forgetting manners,
I unsealed;

2576
02:13:04.000 --> 02:13:06.080
And where I found, Horatio,
the command,

2577
02:13:06.750 --> 02:13:09.080
That on the supervise,
no leisure bated,

2578
02:13:09.200 --> 02:13:11.370
No, not to stay
the grinding of the axe,

2579
02:13:11.500 --> 02:13:13.080
My head should be struck off.

2580
02:13:13.200 --> 02:13:14.200
Is't possible?

2581
02:13:14.700 --> 02:13:17.370
Here’s the commission,
read it at more leisure.

2582
02:13:18.000 --> 02:13:19.870
But wilt thou hear now
how I did proceed?

2583
02:13:20.000 --> 02:13:21.000
I beseech you.

2584
02:13:21.120 --> 02:13:23.700
I sat down
and devised a new commission,

2585
02:13:24.250 --> 02:13:27.450
An earnest conjuration
from the King.

2586
02:13:28.370 --> 02:13:30.500
That on the view and knowing
of these contents,

2587
02:13:30.620 --> 02:13:33.120
He should the bearers
put to sudden death,

2588
02:13:33.870 --> 02:13:35.250
Not shriving-time allowed.

2589
02:13:36.700 --> 02:13:39.200
I folded it,
In form of th’other, subscribed it,

2590
02:13:39.700 --> 02:13:40.870
placed it safely,

2591
02:13:41.000 --> 02:13:43.370
The changeling never known,
and thence did fly.

2592
02:13:43.500 --> 02:13:47.000
So Guildenstern and Rosencrantz
go to't.

2593
02:13:48.330 --> 02:13:49.500
Why, man,

2594
02:13:49.620 --> 02:13:52.250
they did make love
to this employment.

2595
02:13:52.750 --> 02:13:54.000
They are not near my conscience.

2596
02:13:54.120 --> 02:13:57.250
♪ The harbinger of death, of death

2597
02:13:57.370 --> 02:14:00.620
♪ To me I see him ride

2598
02:14:00.750 --> 02:14:02.370
(High-pitched) ♪ Ride

2599
02:14:02.500 --> 02:14:05.080
(Growly voice) ♪ Ride

2600
02:14:05.200 --> 02:14:08.750
♪ The cough, the cold
the gasping breath

2601
02:14:08.870 --> 02:14:11.750
♪ Doth bid me to provide ♪

2602
02:14:11.870 --> 02:14:15.080
Has this fellow no feeling of his business
a sings in grave-making?

2603
02:14:15.200 --> 02:14:17.120
Custom hath made it in him
a property of easiness.

2604
02:14:17.250 --> 02:14:20.370
♪ A pickaxe and a spade, a spade ♪

2605
02:14:22.870 --> 02:14:24.500
Whose grave's this, sirrah?

2606
02:14:25.000 --> 02:14:26.120
Mine, sir.

2607
02:14:26.830 --> 02:14:29.120
I think it be thine indeed,
for thou liest in't.

2608
02:14:29.250 --> 02:14:31.620
Sir, I do not lie in't,
yet it is mine.

2609
02:14:31.750 --> 02:14:34.620
Thou dost lie in't,
to be in't and say 'tis thine.

2610
02:14:34.750 --> 02:14:37.450
'Tis for the dead, not for the quick,
therefore thou liest.

2611
02:14:37.580 --> 02:14:40.000
'Tis a quick lie, sir,
'twill away again from me to you.

2612
02:14:40.750 --> 02:14:43.450
- What man dost thou dig it for?
- For no man, sir.

2613
02:14:43.580 --> 02:14:45.950
- What woman then?
- For none neither.

2614
02:14:46.750 --> 02:14:48.450
Who is to be buried in't?

2615
02:14:48.580 --> 02:14:52.580
One that was a woman, sir,
but rest her soul, she's dead.

2616
02:14:53.370 --> 02:14:55.620
How absolute the knave is.

2617
02:14:57.120 --> 02:14:59.000
How long hast thou been grave-maker?

2618
02:14:59.700 --> 02:15:01.870
Of all the days i'th' year
I came to't that day

2619
02:15:02.000 --> 02:15:03.700
that our young Hamlet was born,

2620
02:15:03.830 --> 02:15:05.750
he that is mad
and sent into England.

2621
02:15:05.870 --> 02:15:08.620
Ay, marry.
Why was he sent into England?

2622
02:15:08.750 --> 02:15:11.250
Why, because he was mad.

2623
02:15:11.370 --> 02:15:12.830
He shall recover his wits there.

2624
02:15:12.950 --> 02:15:15.120
Or if he do not,
'tis no great matter there.

2625
02:15:15.250 --> 02:15:17.620
- Why?
- 'Twill not be seen in him there.

2626
02:15:17.750 --> 02:15:19.830
There the men are as mad as he.

2627
02:15:19.950 --> 02:15:21.370
(Audience laughs)

2628
02:15:24.250 --> 02:15:26.750
How long will a man lie i'th' earth
ere he rot?

2629
02:15:27.500 --> 02:15:31.120
Faith, if he be not rotten
before he die,

2630
02:15:31.250 --> 02:15:34.000
he will last you some...eight year

2631
02:15:34.120 --> 02:15:35.620
or nine year.

2632
02:15:36.750 --> 02:15:38.120
Here's a skull now

2633
02:15:38.870 --> 02:15:40.120
hath lien you i'th' earth...

2634
02:15:41.370 --> 02:15:43.450
...three and twenty years.

2635
02:15:43.580 --> 02:15:46.250
- Whose was it?
- A whoreson mad fellow's it was.

2636
02:15:46.370 --> 02:15:48.500
- Whose do you think it was?
- Nay, I know not.

2637
02:15:48.620 --> 02:15:50.700
A pestilence on him for a mad rogue.

2638
02:15:50.830 --> 02:15:53.750
He poured a flagon of Rhenish
on my head once.

2639
02:15:53.870 --> 02:15:55.250
This same skull, sir...

2640
02:15:55.370 --> 02:15:56.370
(Whistles)

2641
02:15:57.000 --> 02:15:59.830
...was Yorick's skull,
the King's jester.

2642
02:16:00.370 --> 02:16:01.370
This?

2643
02:16:02.370 --> 02:16:03.370
E'en that.

2644
02:16:05.330 --> 02:16:07.200
Alas, poor Yorick.

2645
02:16:08.000 --> 02:16:09.000
I knew him.

2646
02:16:10.250 --> 02:16:14.250
Horatio, a fellow of infinite jest,

2647
02:16:14.370 --> 02:16:16.450
of most excellent fancy.

2648
02:16:16.950 --> 02:16:19.250
He hath bore me on his back

2649
02:16:19.370 --> 02:16:21.330
a thousand times.

2650
02:16:22.370 --> 02:16:25.250
And now how abhorred
in my imagination it is.

2651
02:16:25.370 --> 02:16:27.250
My gorge rises at it.

2652
02:16:28.500 --> 02:16:32.000
Here hung those lips that I have kissed
I know not how oft.

2653
02:16:34.370 --> 02:16:36.000
Where be your gibes now,

2654
02:16:36.620 --> 02:16:38.000
your gambols,

2655
02:16:38.120 --> 02:16:39.250
your songs,

2656
02:16:39.870 --> 02:16:41.250
your flashes of merriment,

2657
02:16:41.370 --> 02:16:44.450
that were wont to set the table
on a roar?

2658
02:16:46.080 --> 02:16:48.700
Not one now
to mock your own grinning?

2659
02:16:49.330 --> 02:16:50.450
(Orchestra playing)

2660
02:16:50.580 --> 02:16:51.950
Quite chop-fallen?

2661
02:16:53.870 --> 02:16:56.200
Now get you to my lady's chamber

2662
02:16:56.330 --> 02:16:57.580
and tell her,

2663
02:16:57.700 --> 02:16:59.450
let her paint an inch thick,

2664
02:16:59.580 --> 02:17:01.500
to this favour she must come.

2665
02:17:03.200 --> 02:17:04.450
Make her laugh at that.

2666
02:17:05.750 --> 02:17:07.000
But soft, but soft awhile.

2667
02:17:07.120 --> 02:17:09.950
Here comes the King,
the Queen, the courtiers.

2668
02:17:10.080 --> 02:17:11.620
Who is this they follow?

2669
02:17:12.200 --> 02:17:14.200
And with such maimed rites?

2670
02:17:14.870 --> 02:17:16.450
Couch we awhile and mark.

2671
02:17:16.580 --> 02:17:18.080
(Chanting in Latin)

2672
02:17:28.080 --> 02:17:29.330
(Laertes) What ceremony else?

2673
02:17:29.450 --> 02:17:32.580
Her obsequies have been as far enlarged
As we have warranty.

2674
02:17:32.700 --> 02:17:33.870
Her death was doubtful,

2675
02:17:34.000 --> 02:17:36.830
And but that great command
o'ersways the order,

2676
02:17:36.950 --> 02:17:39.750
She should in ground unsanctified
be lodged.

2677
02:17:39.870 --> 02:17:41.330
The fair Ophelia.

2678
02:17:41.450 --> 02:17:44.950
- Must there no more be done?
- No more be done.

2679
02:17:45.080 --> 02:17:48.330
We should profane the service of the dead
To sing sage requiem

2680
02:17:48.450 --> 02:17:52.750
and such rest to her
As to peace-parted souls.

2681
02:17:54.750 --> 02:17:56.330
Lay her i'th' earth.

2682
02:17:56.450 --> 02:17:57.450
(Clears throat)

2683
02:17:57.580 --> 02:18:00.500
And from her fair
and unpolluted flesh

2684
02:18:00.620 --> 02:18:02.080
May violets spring.

2685
02:18:03.370 --> 02:18:06.000
I tell thee, churlish priest,

2686
02:18:06.120 --> 02:18:10.450
A minist'ring angel shall my sister be
When thou liest howling.

2687
02:18:13.200 --> 02:18:14.700
Sweets to the sweet.

2688
02:18:15.330 --> 02:18:16.330
Farewell.

2689
02:18:16.870 --> 02:18:19.370
I hoped thou shouldst have been
my Hamlet's wife.

2690
02:18:20.250 --> 02:18:22.870
I thought thy bride-bed to have decked,
sweet maid,

2691
02:18:23.000 --> 02:18:24.370
And not have strewed thy grave.

2692
02:18:33.250 --> 02:18:35.330
O, treble woe

2693
02:18:35.450 --> 02:18:38.370
Fall ten times treble

2694
02:18:38.500 --> 02:18:41.370
on that cursed head
Whose wicked deed

2695
02:18:41.500 --> 02:18:44.370
thy most ingenious sense
Deprived thee of.

2696
02:18:47.450 --> 02:18:48.700
Hold off the earth awhile.

2697
02:18:50.950 --> 02:18:53.250
Till I have caught her once more
in mine arms.

2698
02:18:53.370 --> 02:18:55.080
(All shouting)

2699
02:18:55.200 --> 02:18:56.370
(Laertes grunts)

2700
02:18:59.330 --> 02:19:03.250
Now pile your dust
upon the quick and dead,

2701
02:19:03.830 --> 02:19:07.250
Till of this flat
a mountain you have made.

2702
02:19:07.830 --> 02:19:12.450
What is he whose grief
Bears such an emphasis,

2703
02:19:13.450 --> 02:19:16.750
whose phrase of sorrow
Conjures the wand'ring stars

2704
02:19:16.870 --> 02:19:20.330
and makes them stand
Like wonder-wounded hearers?

2705
02:19:20.830 --> 02:19:23.950
This is I, Hamlet the Dane.

2706
02:19:24.080 --> 02:19:25.250
The devil take thy soul!

2707
02:19:25.370 --> 02:19:27.620
(Claudius) Pluck them asunder!
(Gertrude) Hamlet!

2708
02:19:27.750 --> 02:19:30.120
Why, I will fight with him
upon this theme

2709
02:19:30.250 --> 02:19:32.700
Until my eyelids will no longer wag!

2710
02:19:32.830 --> 02:19:34.080
O my son, what theme?

2711
02:19:34.200 --> 02:19:35.620
I loved Ophelia!

2712
02:19:36.250 --> 02:19:38.120
Forty thousand brothers

2713
02:19:38.250 --> 02:19:41.750
Could not with all their quantity of love
Make up my sum!

2714
02:19:42.330 --> 02:19:44.200
What wilt thou do for her?

2715
02:19:45.080 --> 02:19:46.580
Show me what thou't do!

2716
02:19:47.450 --> 02:19:50.500
Woo't weep, woo't fight,
woo't fast, woo't tear thyself!

2717
02:19:51.120 --> 02:19:54.000
Woo't drink up eisel, eat a crocodile?
I'll do't!

2718
02:19:54.830 --> 02:19:57.500
Dost come here to whine,

2719
02:19:57.620 --> 02:20:00.500
To outface me
with leaping in her grave?

2720
02:20:00.620 --> 02:20:03.700
Be buried quick with her,
and so will I!

2721
02:20:03.830 --> 02:20:06.830
(Gertrude) This is mere madness,
And thus awhile the fit will work on him.

2722
02:20:08.870 --> 02:20:10.500
What is the reason...

2723
02:20:11.500 --> 02:20:14.120
...that you use me thus?

2724
02:20:15.080 --> 02:20:17.620
I loved you ever.

2725
02:20:19.500 --> 02:20:20.500
But it is no matter.

2726
02:20:21.870 --> 02:20:23.950
Let Hercules himself

2727
02:20:24.080 --> 02:20:25.370
do what he may.

2728
02:20:26.500 --> 02:20:28.000
The cat will mew!

2729
02:20:29.000 --> 02:20:31.120
And dog will have his day!

2730
02:20:31.250 --> 02:20:33.250
(Claudius) I pray thee,
good Horatio, wait upon him.

2731
02:20:35.620 --> 02:20:37.950
Strengthen your patience
in our last night's speech.

2732
02:20:38.080 --> 02:20:39.870
We'll put the matter
to the present push.

2733
02:20:40.000 --> 02:20:42.370
Good Gertrude,
set some watch over your son.

2734
02:20:42.500 --> 02:20:44.700
This grave
shall have a living monument.

2735
02:20:46.370 --> 02:20:48.750
An hour of quiet
shortly shall we see.

2736
02:20:49.370 --> 02:20:52.620
Till then
in patience our proceeding be.

2737
02:20:53.450 --> 02:20:55.000
(Tense orchestral music)

2738
02:21:13.250 --> 02:21:17.080
I am very sorry, good Horatio,
That to Laertes I forgot myself,

2739
02:21:17.200 --> 02:21:19.500
For by the image of my cause

2740
02:21:19.620 --> 02:21:21.200
I see
The portraiture of his.

2741
02:21:21.830 --> 02:21:23.120
Peace, who comes here?

2742
02:21:23.250 --> 02:21:24.700
Ah!

2743
02:21:24.830 --> 02:21:27.750
Your Lordship
is right welcome back to Denmark.

2744
02:21:27.870 --> 02:21:29.700
I humbly thank you sir.

2745
02:21:29.830 --> 02:21:33.120
Sweet lord,
if your lordship were at leisure,

2746
02:21:33.250 --> 02:21:35.950
I should impart a thing to you
from his Majesty.

2747
02:21:36.580 --> 02:21:38.870
I will receive it, sir,
with all diligence of spirit.

2748
02:21:39.000 --> 02:21:42.950
Hm. My lord, his Majesty
bade me signify to you

2749
02:21:43.080 --> 02:21:47.080
that he has laid a great wager
on your head.

2750
02:21:47.200 --> 02:21:50.370
There is newly come
to court Laertes,

2751
02:21:50.500 --> 02:21:53.750
believe me, an absolute gentleman,

2752
02:21:53.870 --> 02:21:55.830
full of most excellent differences,

2753
02:21:55.950 --> 02:22:00.080
of very soft society
and great showing.

2754
02:22:00.200 --> 02:22:01.370
What's his weapon?

2755
02:22:01.500 --> 02:22:03.000
Rapier and dagger.

2756
02:22:03.120 --> 02:22:04.950
That's two of his weapons. But well.

2757
02:22:06.500 --> 02:22:09.200
The king, sir, hath laid, sir,

2758
02:22:09.330 --> 02:22:12.450
that in a dozen passes
between yourself and him

2759
02:22:12.580 --> 02:22:15.500
he shall not exceed you three hits.

2760
02:22:15.620 --> 02:22:17.620
And it would come to immediate trial

2761
02:22:17.750 --> 02:22:19.700
if your lordship
would vouchsafe the answer.

2762
02:22:19.830 --> 02:22:21.200
How if I answer no?

2763
02:22:23.750 --> 02:22:24.700
Sir?

2764
02:22:28.000 --> 02:22:29.580
I will walk here in the hall.

2765
02:22:29.700 --> 02:22:33.000
If it please his Majesty,
it is the breathing time of day with me.

2766
02:22:34.370 --> 02:22:36.200
Let the foils be brought,
the gentleman willing,

2767
02:22:36.330 --> 02:22:38.500
and the King hold his purpose,
I will win for him if I can.

2768
02:22:38.620 --> 02:22:40.830
If not, I gain nothing but my shame
and the odd hits.

2769
02:22:40.950 --> 02:22:42.450
Shall I deliver you so?

2770
02:22:42.580 --> 02:22:45.370
- To this effect, sir.
- I commend my duty to your lordship.

2771
02:22:45.500 --> 02:22:46.500
Yours.

2772
02:22:46.620 --> 02:22:50.620
The Queen desires you to use
some gentle entertainment to Laertes

2773
02:22:50.750 --> 02:22:54.000
- before you fall to play.
- She well instructs me.

2774
02:22:58.870 --> 02:23:01.370
You will lose, my lord.

2775
02:23:02.250 --> 02:23:03.870
(Audience laughs quietly)

2776
02:23:04.620 --> 02:23:06.080
I do not think so.

2777
02:23:07.330 --> 02:23:10.200
Since he went into France,
I have been in continual practice.

2778
02:23:10.330 --> 02:23:11.870
(Both laugh)

2779
02:23:12.000 --> 02:23:14.330
I shall win at the odds.

2780
02:23:15.120 --> 02:23:18.500
Thou wouldst not think
how ill all's here

2781
02:23:19.200 --> 02:23:20.370
about my heart.

2782
02:23:21.620 --> 02:23:22.870
- But it is no matter.
- Nay.

2783
02:23:24.000 --> 02:23:28.120
Good my lord. If your mind
dislike anything, obey it.

2784
02:23:28.250 --> 02:23:30.700
I will forestall their repair hither
and say you are not fit.

2785
02:23:30.830 --> 02:23:31.950
Not a whit.

2786
02:23:33.370 --> 02:23:35.200
We defy augury.

2787
02:23:37.120 --> 02:23:38.750
There is special providence

2788
02:23:39.620 --> 02:23:41.250
in the fall of a sparrow.

2789
02:23:42.500 --> 02:23:45.000
If it be now, 'tis not to come.

2790
02:23:46.750 --> 02:23:49.330
If it be not to come,
it will be now.

2791
02:23:50.250 --> 02:23:51.500
If it be not now,

2792
02:23:52.330 --> 02:23:54.700
yet it will come.

2793
02:23:56.250 --> 02:23:57.870
The readiness is all.

2794
02:23:59.950 --> 02:24:03.950
Since no man, of aught he leaves,
knows aught, what is't to leave betimes?

2795
02:24:07.330 --> 02:24:08.330
Let be.

2796
02:24:11.000 --> 02:24:12.950
The King, the Queen and all
are coming in.

2797
02:24:13.080 --> 02:24:14.830
(Cheerfully) In happy time.

2798
02:24:16.000 --> 02:24:18.620
(Claudius) Come, Hamlet, come,
and take this hand from me.

2799
02:24:22.700 --> 02:24:25.500
Give me your pardon, sir.
I have done you wrong.

2800
02:24:25.620 --> 02:24:28.500
This presence knows,
and you must needs have heard,

2801
02:24:28.620 --> 02:24:30.500
How I am punished
with a sore distraction.

2802
02:24:31.620 --> 02:24:34.250
What I have done
I here proclaim was madness.

2803
02:24:35.370 --> 02:24:37.830
Let my disclaiming
from a purposed evil

2804
02:24:38.330 --> 02:24:40.750
Free me so far
in your most generous thoughts

2805
02:24:40.870 --> 02:24:43.080
That I have shot my arrow
o'er the house

2806
02:24:43.200 --> 02:24:44.200
And hurt my brother.

2807
02:24:44.330 --> 02:24:46.370
I am satisfied in nature,

2808
02:24:47.250 --> 02:24:49.500
Whose motive in this case
should stir me most

2809
02:24:49.620 --> 02:24:52.250
To my revenge;
but in my terms of honour

2810
02:24:52.450 --> 02:24:53.580
I stand aloof,

2811
02:24:54.370 --> 02:24:55.620
and will no reconcilement

2812
02:24:55.750 --> 02:24:58.750
Till by some elder masters
of known honour

2813
02:24:58.870 --> 02:25:02.750
I have a voice and precedent of peace
To keep my name ungored.

2814
02:25:04.750 --> 02:25:07.500
But till that time I do receive
your offered love like love

2815
02:25:07.620 --> 02:25:08.830
And will not wrong it.

2816
02:25:10.250 --> 02:25:12.000
I embrace it freely,

2817
02:25:12.120 --> 02:25:15.330
And will this brothers’ wager
frankly play.

2818
02:25:17.000 --> 02:25:19.370
- Give us the foils.
- Come, one for me.

2819
02:25:21.080 --> 02:25:23.080
I'll be your foil, Laertes.

2820
02:25:23.950 --> 02:25:24.750
In mine ignorance

2821
02:25:24.870 --> 02:25:28.370
Your skill shall,
like a star i'th' darkest night,

2822
02:25:28.500 --> 02:25:30.000
Stick fiery off indeed.

2823
02:25:30.120 --> 02:25:31.750
You mock me, sir.

2824
02:25:31.870 --> 02:25:33.750
No, by this hand.

2825
02:25:34.700 --> 02:25:36.370
Give them the foils, young Osric.

2826
02:25:36.500 --> 02:25:38.330
Cousin Hamlet,
You know the wager?

2827
02:25:38.450 --> 02:25:40.620
Very well, my lord.

2828
02:25:40.750 --> 02:25:43.500
Your Grace has laid the odds
o'th' weaker side.

2829
02:25:43.620 --> 02:25:45.700
I do not fear it.
I have seen you both.

2830
02:25:45.830 --> 02:25:47.950
This is too heavy.
Let me see another.

2831
02:25:48.080 --> 02:25:49.580
This likes me well.

2832
02:25:49.700 --> 02:25:52.080
- These foils have all a length?
- Ay, my good lord.

2833
02:25:52.200 --> 02:25:54.830
If Hamlet give
the first or second hit,

2834
02:25:54.950 --> 02:25:57.330
The King shall drink
to Hamlet’s better breath,

2835
02:25:57.450 --> 02:26:00.700
And in the cup
an union shall he throw

2836
02:26:00.830 --> 02:26:03.370
Richer than that
which four successive kings

2837
02:26:03.500 --> 02:26:05.450
In Denmark’s crown have worn.

2838
02:26:05.580 --> 02:26:06.750
Now come begin.

2839
02:26:06.870 --> 02:26:08.950
And you, the judges,
bear a wary eye.

2840
02:26:10.700 --> 02:26:12.080
(Hamlet) Come on, sir.

2841
02:26:12.620 --> 02:26:13.750
(Laertes) Come, my lord.

2842
02:26:34.330 --> 02:26:35.620
(Hamlet) One!
(Laertes) No!

2843
02:26:35.750 --> 02:26:39.000
- (Hamlet) Judgment!
- A hit, a very palpable hit.

2844
02:26:39.120 --> 02:26:41.620
- (Laertes) Well, again!
- Hamlet this pearl is thine!

2845
02:26:41.750 --> 02:26:43.950
Here's to thy health.
Give him the cup.

2846
02:26:44.080 --> 02:26:46.250
I'll play this bout first.
Set it by awhile.

2847
02:26:49.080 --> 02:26:50.120
(Hamlet) Come.

2848
02:26:59.370 --> 02:27:00.700
(Hamlet laughs)

2849
02:27:01.250 --> 02:27:02.620
(Both grunting)

2850
02:27:02.750 --> 02:27:04.450
(Quick breathing)

2851
02:27:08.370 --> 02:27:10.080
Another hit! What say you?

2852
02:27:10.200 --> 02:27:12.620
(Osric) A touch!
(Laertes) A touch, I do confess't!

2853
02:27:12.750 --> 02:27:14.450
Our son shall win.

2854
02:27:14.580 --> 02:27:15.950
He's scant of breath.

2855
02:27:16.080 --> 02:27:18.450
Here, Hamlet, take my napkin,
rub thy brows.

2856
02:27:19.370 --> 02:27:21.830
The Queen carouses to thy fortune,
Hamlet.

2857
02:27:21.950 --> 02:27:23.750
- Good madam.
- Gertrude.

2858
02:27:24.950 --> 02:27:25.870
Do not drink.

2859
02:27:26.700 --> 02:27:29.500
I will, my lord,
I pray you pardon me.

2860
02:27:33.330 --> 02:27:34.330
(Hamlet laughs)

2861
02:27:34.450 --> 02:27:37.500
I dare not drink yet, madam,
by and by.

2862
02:27:37.620 --> 02:27:40.000
- Come, let me wipe thy face.
- My lord, I'll hit him now.

2863
02:27:40.120 --> 02:27:41.370
I do not think't.

2864
02:27:41.500 --> 02:27:44.000
And yet it is almost
against my conscience.

2865
02:27:44.830 --> 02:27:46.620
(Cheerfully)
Come for the third, Laertes!

2866
02:27:46.750 --> 02:27:48.620
You do but dally!

2867
02:27:48.750 --> 02:27:50.450
I am afeard you make a wanton of me.

2868
02:27:51.250 --> 02:27:52.370
(Hamlet laughs)

2869
02:27:52.500 --> 02:27:53.500
Say you so?

2870
02:27:56.120 --> 02:27:57.120
(Osric) Sirs!

2871
02:28:00.500 --> 02:28:01.500
(Screams)

2872
02:28:08.870 --> 02:28:09.870
Nay.

2873
02:28:13.750 --> 02:28:17.000
- (Hamlet) Let me see!
- Part them. They are incensed.

2874
02:28:17.120 --> 02:28:18.620
Forebear, my lords!

2875
02:28:19.500 --> 02:28:21.200
(Hamlet clicks his tongue)

2876
02:28:28.250 --> 02:28:30.120
They bleed on both sides.

2877
02:28:32.620 --> 02:28:34.450
Come again.

2878
02:28:36.620 --> 02:28:38.330
(Horatio) How is it, my lord?

2879
02:28:38.450 --> 02:28:39.870
(Osric) How is't, Laertes?

2880
02:28:41.700 --> 02:28:45.620
(Laertes) Why, as a woodcock
to mine own springe, sir,

2881
02:28:46.580 --> 02:28:49.080
I am justly killed
with mine own treachery.

2882
02:28:49.200 --> 02:28:50.200
(Hamlet) What?

2883
02:28:51.000 --> 02:28:53.700
(Osric) Look to the Queen there, ho!
(Hamlet) How does the Queen?

2884
02:28:53.830 --> 02:28:56.450
- She swoons to see them bleed.
- No, no!

2885
02:28:57.000 --> 02:28:58.870
The drink, the drink.

2886
02:28:59.370 --> 02:29:00.370
O my dear Hamlet.

2887
02:29:00.870 --> 02:29:02.000
The drink.

2888
02:29:03.870 --> 02:29:05.330
I am poisoned.

2889
02:29:05.450 --> 02:29:07.200
- (Groans)
- O villainy.

2890
02:29:07.330 --> 02:29:09.750
Ho! Let the door be locked.
Treachery!

2891
02:29:09.870 --> 02:29:12.370
- Seek it out!
- (Laertes) It is here, Hamlet!

2892
02:29:12.950 --> 02:29:14.830
Hamlet, thou art slain.

2893
02:29:14.950 --> 02:29:16.950
No medicine in the world
can do thee good.

2894
02:29:17.080 --> 02:29:19.370
In thee
there is not half an hour's life.

2895
02:29:20.580 --> 02:29:22.950
The treacherous instrument
is in thy hand,

2896
02:29:23.080 --> 02:29:25.950
Unbated and envenomed.

2897
02:29:26.750 --> 02:29:29.330
The foul practice
Hath turned itself on me.

2898
02:29:29.450 --> 02:29:30.450
Lo.

2899
02:29:31.330 --> 02:29:33.700
Here I lie,
Never to rise again.

2900
02:29:36.330 --> 02:29:37.830
Thy mother's poisoned.

2901
02:29:40.120 --> 02:29:41.500
I can no more.

2902
02:29:42.870 --> 02:29:43.870
The King!

2903
02:29:44.950 --> 02:29:46.120
The King's to blame!

2904
02:29:46.250 --> 02:29:47.870
(Hamlet) The point envenomed too!

2905
02:29:48.000 --> 02:29:50.330
Then, venom, to thy work!

2906
02:29:59.370 --> 02:30:00.370
(Screams)

2907
02:30:09.830 --> 02:30:12.330
O yet defend me, friends.
I am but hurt.

2908
02:30:15.870 --> 02:30:19.200
Here, thou incestuous, murd'rous,

2909
02:30:19.870 --> 02:30:21.620
damned Dane.

2910
02:30:23.500 --> 02:30:25.700
Drink off this potion.

2911
02:30:42.080 --> 02:30:43.620
Follow my mother.

2912
02:30:51.950 --> 02:30:54.120
(Laertes) He is justly served.

2913
02:30:55.120 --> 02:30:57.950
It is a poison tempered by himself.

2914
02:30:58.620 --> 02:31:00.700
Exchange forgiveness with me,

2915
02:31:01.500 --> 02:31:03.200
noble Hamlet.

2916
02:31:04.250 --> 02:31:07.750
Mine and my family's death
come not upon thee.

2917
02:31:08.830 --> 02:31:10.250
Nor thine on me.

2918
02:31:11.120 --> 02:31:13.200
Heaven make thee free of it.

2919
02:31:14.830 --> 02:31:16.120
I follow thee.

2920
02:31:29.620 --> 02:31:30.620
I am dead.

2921
02:31:33.750 --> 02:31:34.870
Horatio.

2922
02:31:36.620 --> 02:31:37.750
(Groans)

2923
02:31:37.870 --> 02:31:40.000
Wretched Queen, adieu.

2924
02:31:43.580 --> 02:31:47.870
You that look pale and tremble
at this chance,

2925
02:31:48.500 --> 02:31:51.250
That are but mutes or audience
to this act...

2926
02:31:53.620 --> 02:31:55.200
...Had I but time...

2927
02:31:56.250 --> 02:31:58.000
...as this fell sergeant, Death,

2928
02:31:58.120 --> 02:32:00.950
Is strict in his arrest.

2929
02:32:02.330 --> 02:32:04.580
O, I could tell you.

2930
02:32:07.250 --> 02:32:08.620
But let it be.

2931
02:32:09.750 --> 02:32:11.250
- Horatio.
- Hm?

2932
02:32:13.620 --> 02:32:14.870
I am dead.

2933
02:32:16.200 --> 02:32:17.370
Thou livest.

2934
02:32:18.500 --> 02:32:21.620
Report me and my cause aright
To the unsatisfied.

2935
02:32:21.750 --> 02:32:23.250
Never believe it!

2936
02:32:23.370 --> 02:32:25.700
I am more an antique Roman
than a Dane.

2937
02:32:25.830 --> 02:32:27.330
Here's yet some liquor left.

2938
02:32:27.450 --> 02:32:29.950
Give me the cup.
Let go, by Heaven!

2939
02:32:30.580 --> 02:32:31.580
I'll ha't.

2940
02:32:32.870 --> 02:32:35.000
If thou didst ever hold me
in thy heart,

2941
02:32:35.830 --> 02:32:38.580
Absent thee from felicity awhile,

2942
02:32:38.700 --> 02:32:41.000
And in this harsh world...

2943
02:32:42.120 --> 02:32:44.370
...draw thy breath in pain...

2944
02:32:45.500 --> 02:32:47.080
...To tell my story.

2945
02:32:53.000 --> 02:32:54.000
The rest...

2946
02:32:55.620 --> 02:32:56.750
...is silence.

2947
02:33:19.250 --> 02:33:22.000
Now cracks a noble heart.

2948
02:33:23.870 --> 02:33:26.750
Good night, sweet prince,

2949
02:33:27.250 --> 02:33:30.370
And flights of angels
sing thee to thy rest.

2950
02:33:34.000 --> 02:33:37.000
(Osric) Young Fortinbras
with conquest comes from Poland.

2951
02:33:37.120 --> 02:33:40.120
(Fortinbras) Where is this sight?
(Horatio) What is it you would see?

2952
02:33:41.200 --> 02:33:44.450
If aught of woe or wonder,
cease your search.

2953
02:33:46.080 --> 02:33:47.330
This quarry...

2954
02:33:48.330 --> 02:33:50.000
...cries on havoc.

2955
02:33:52.120 --> 02:33:53.620
O proud Death...

2956
02:33:54.620 --> 02:33:57.330
...What feast is toward
in thine eternal cell,

2957
02:33:57.450 --> 02:33:59.870
That thou so many princes at a shot

2958
02:34:00.000 --> 02:34:01.450
So bloodily hast struck?

2959
02:34:01.580 --> 02:34:02.870
The sight is dismal,

2960
02:34:03.620 --> 02:34:06.500
And our affairs from England
come too late.

2961
02:34:07.330 --> 02:34:09.620
The ears are senseless
that should give us hearing

2962
02:34:09.750 --> 02:34:12.330
To tell him
his commandment is fulfilled,

2963
02:34:12.870 --> 02:34:15.330
That Rosencrantz and Guildenstern
are dead.

2964
02:34:15.450 --> 02:34:16.750
(Horatio) Give order...

2965
02:34:19.200 --> 02:34:20.620
...that these bodies

2966
02:34:21.250 --> 02:34:23.120
High on the stage

2967
02:34:23.250 --> 02:34:24.950
be place to the view.

2968
02:34:28.830 --> 02:34:30.370
And let me speak...

2969
02:34:32.250 --> 02:34:36.000
...to th’yet unknowing world
How these things came about.

2970
02:34:37.000 --> 02:34:38.330
So shall you hear

2971
02:34:38.830 --> 02:34:42.500
Of carnal, bloody,
and unnatural acts,

2972
02:34:42.620 --> 02:34:46.080
Of accidental judgments,
casual slaughters,

2973
02:34:46.200 --> 02:34:49.120
Of deaths put on by cunning
and forced cause,

2974
02:34:49.250 --> 02:34:50.750
And, in this upshot...

2975
02:34:51.830 --> 02:34:53.330
...purposes mistook...

2976
02:34:54.620 --> 02:34:56.580
...Fall’n on th’inventors heads.

2977
02:34:56.700 --> 02:35:00.250
All this can I
Truly deliver.

2978
02:35:02.080 --> 02:35:03.830
(Fortinbras)
Let us haste to hear it.

2979
02:35:05.000 --> 02:35:08.120
And call the noblest
to the audience!

2980
02:35:10.000 --> 02:35:12.620
For me, with sorrow

2981
02:35:13.330 --> 02:35:15.750
I embrace my fortune!

2982
02:35:15.870 --> 02:35:17.750
(Deep orchestral music)

2983
02:35:17.870 --> 02:35:21.000
I have some rights of memory
in this kingdom,

2984
02:35:21.580 --> 02:35:23.250
Which now to claim

2985
02:35:23.870 --> 02:35:26.250
my vantage doth invite me.

2986
02:35:28.830 --> 02:35:32.370
Bear Hamlet
like a soldier to the stage.

2987
02:35:33.830 --> 02:35:35.750
For he was likely,
had he been put on,

2988
02:35:35.870 --> 02:35:37.830
To have proved most royal;

2989
02:35:38.750 --> 02:35:40.120
and for his passage,

2990
02:35:41.000 --> 02:35:42.330
The soldier’s music

2991
02:35:42.450 --> 02:35:44.580
and rite of war

2992
02:35:44.700 --> 02:35:47.580
Speak proudly for him.

2993
02:35:49.750 --> 02:35:51.120
Take up the bodies.

2994
02:35:52.950 --> 02:35:54.500
Such a sight as this

2995
02:35:55.330 --> 02:35:56.750
Becomes the field.

2996
02:35:57.750 --> 02:35:58.950
But here...

2997
02:36:00.250 --> 02:36:01.870
...show much amiss.

2998
02:36:06.370 --> 02:36:07.370
Go!

2999
02:36:09.700 --> 02:36:11.870
Bid the soldiers shoot.

3000
02:36:12.870 --> 02:36:14.870
(Music intensifies)

3001
02:36:16.620 --> 02:36:17.620
(Music stops)

3002
02:36:18.120 --> 02:36:20.120
(Applause)

3003
02:36:33.580 --> 02:36:35.580
(Cheering)
